h, that's a great way to put it.", "tokens": [51087, 865, 11, 300, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 829, 309, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10485974569169301, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358475145341717e-12}, {"id": 13, "seek": 5516, "start": 71.22, "end": 76.75999999999999, "text": " For over a century now, physicists have used complex numbers to calculate how subatomic particles behave.", "tokens": [51168, 1171, 670, 257, 4901, 586, 11, 48716, 362, 1143, 3997, 3547, 281, 8873, 577, 1422, 267, 21401, 10007, 15158, 13, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10485974569169301, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358475145341717e-12}, {"id": 14, "seek": 5516, "start": 77.12, "end": 83.38, "text": " And by complex numbers, I mean numbers with an imaginary component, you know, the square root of negative one.", "tokens": [51463, 400, 538, 3997, 3547, 11, 286, 914, 3547, 365, 364, 26164, 6542, 11, 291, 458, 11, 264, 3732, 5593, 295, 3671, 472, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10485974569169301, "compression_ratio": 1.6560509554140128, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358475145341717e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 8338, "start": 83.38, "end": 88.0, "text": " And just to be super clear for you listening, this isn't some fringe theory we're talking about today.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 445, 281, 312, 1687, 1850, 337, 291, 4764, 11, 341, 1943, 380, 512, 38764, 5261, 321, 434, 1417, 466, 965, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15505169316342002, "compression_ratio": 1.5228215767634854, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428740099757143e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 8338, "start": 88.24, "end": 88.82, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [50608, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15505169316342002, "compression_ratio": 1.5228215767634854, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428740099757143e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 8338, "start": 88.94, "end": 90.38, "text": " This math works perfectly.", "tokens": [50643, 639, 5221, 1985, 6239, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15505169316342002, "compression_ratio": 1.5228215767634854, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428740099757143e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 8338, "start": 90.67999999999999, "end": 90.83999999999999, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50730, 865, 13, 50738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15505169316342002, "compression_ratio": 1.5228215767634854, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428740099757143e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 8338, "start": 90.83999999999999, "end": 96.16, "text": " And it literally powers the semiconductors in the phone or the computer you're listening to this deep dive on right now.", "tokens": [50738, 400, 309, 3736, 8674, 264, 36924, 5547, 294, 264, 2593, 420, 264, 3820, 291, 434, 4764, 281, 341, 2452, 9192, 322, 558, 586, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15505169316342002, "compression_ratio": 1.5228215767634854, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428740099757143e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 8338, "start": 96.39999999999999, "end": 97.97999999999999, "text": " It is insanely accurate.", "tokens": [51016, 467, 307, 40965, 8559, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15505169316342002, "compression_ratio": 1.5228215767634854, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428740099757143e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 8338, "start": 98.17999999999999, "end": 101.22, "text": " It's arguably the most successful scientific theory we have.", "tokens": [51105, 467, 311, 26771, 264, 881, 4406, 8134, 5261, 321, 362, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15505169316342002, "compression_ratio": 1.5228215767634854, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428740099757143e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 8338, "start": 101.32, "end": 101.75999999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51262, 7587, 13, 51284], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15505169316342002, "compression_ratio": 1.5228215767634854, "no_speech_prob": 1.5428740099757143e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 10176, "start": 101.76, "end": 109.32000000000001, "text": " But it leaves us with this massive, almost philosophical foundational question.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 309, 5510, 505, 365, 341, 5994, 11, 1920, 25066, 32195, 1168, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345431918189638, "compression_ratio": 1.517391304347826, "no_speech_prob": 1.3040434617556107e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 10176, "start": 109.64, "end": 111.94, "text": " Does the universe have to run on complex numbers?", "tokens": [50759, 4402, 264, 6445, 362, 281, 1190, 322, 3997, 3547, 30, 50874], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345431918189638, "compression_ratio": 1.517391304347826, "no_speech_prob": 1.3040434617556107e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 10176, "start": 112.18, "end": 112.30000000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50886, 1779, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345431918189638, "compression_ratio": 1.517391304347826, "no_speech_prob": 1.3040434617556107e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 10176, "start": 112.66000000000001, "end": 119.78, "text": " Like, did reality order the complex number package or did we just wrap it in that box because, well, it made the math easier for us humans?", "tokens": [50910, 1743, 11, 630, 4103, 1668, 264, 3997, 1230, 7372, 420, 630, 321, 445, 7019, 309, 294, 300, 2424, 570, 11, 731, 11, 309, 1027, 264, 5221, 3571, 337, 505, 6255, 30, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345431918189638, "compression_ratio": 1.517391304347826, "no_speech_prob": 1.3040434617556107e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 10176, "start": 120.02000000000001, "end": 123.86000000000001, "text": " It is the absolute definition of theoretical muddy waters.", "tokens": [51278, 467, 307, 264, 8236, 7123, 295, 20864, 38540, 12975, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345431918189638, "compression_ratio": 1.517391304347826, "no_speech_prob": 1.3040434617556107e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 10176, "start": 124.18, "end": 125.06, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51486, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51530], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11345431918189638, "compression_ratio": 1.517391304347826, "no_speech_prob": 1.3040434617556107e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 12506, "start": 125.06, "end": 131.2, "text": " Are we discovering the universe's inherent operating system, like written in stone since the Big Bang?", "tokens": [50365, 2014, 321, 24773, 264, 6445, 311, 26387, 7447, 1185, 11, 411, 3720, 294, 7581, 1670, 264, 5429, 11538, 30, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12040815449724293, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.549144384820067e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 12506, "start": 131.68, "end": 140.1, "text": " Or are we just inventing a really efficient programming language to describe what we see from our very limited human perspective?", "tokens": [50696, 1610, 366, 321, 445, 7962, 278, 257, 534, 7148, 9410, 2856, 281, 6786, 437, 321, 536, 490, 527, 588, 5567, 1952, 4585, 30, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12040815449724293, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.549144384820067e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 12506, "start": 140.5, "end": 144.48000000000002, "text": " And that right there is our mission for this deep dive.", "tokens": [51137, 400, 300, 558, 456, 307, 527, 4447, 337, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12040815449724293, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.549144384820067e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 12506, "start": 144.62, "end": 144.76, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51343, 865, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12040815449724293, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.549144384820067e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 12506, "start": 144.96, "end": 149.58, "text": " We are taking you on a journey to the very bedrock of physical reality today.", "tokens": [51360, 492, 366, 1940, 291, 322, 257, 4671, 281, 264, 588, 2901, 17799, 295, 4001, 4103, 965, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12040815449724293, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.549144384820067e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 12506, "start": 149.84, "end": 152.94, "text": " We're basically going to try and reverse engineer quantum mechanics.", "tokens": [51604, 492, 434, 1936, 516, 281, 853, 293, 9943, 11403, 13018, 12939, 13, 51759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12040815449724293, "compression_ratio": 1.5806451612903225, "no_speech_prob": 1.549144384820067e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 15294, "start": 152.94, "end": 153.38, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071250974669937, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171537850148687e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 15294, "start": 153.94, "end": 162.4, "text": " I want you to imagine taking apart a beautiful, really intricate mechanical watch, but you're not doing it just to see how the little gears tick.", "tokens": [50415, 286, 528, 291, 281, 3811, 1940, 4936, 257, 2238, 11, 534, 38015, 12070, 1159, 11, 457, 291, 434, 406, 884, 309, 445, 281, 536, 577, 264, 707, 20915, 5204, 13, 50838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071250974669937, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171537850148687e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 15294, "start": 162.5, "end": 162.7, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50843, 1779, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071250974669937, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171537850148687e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 15294, "start": 162.76, "end": 167.0, "text": " You're taking it apart to prove mathematically that it couldn't possibly have been built any other way.", "tokens": [50856, 509, 434, 1940, 309, 4936, 281, 7081, 44003, 300, 309, 2809, 380, 6264, 362, 668, 3094, 604, 661, 636, 13, 51068], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071250974669937, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171537850148687e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 15294, "start": 167.2, "end": 169.34, "text": " Or, you know, to prove that it actually could.", "tokens": [51078, 1610, 11, 291, 458, 11, 281, 7081, 300, 309, 767, 727, 13, 51185], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071250974669937, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171537850148687e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 15294, "start": 169.57999999999998, "end": 172.32, "text": " Which brings us perfectly to the texts we are exploring today.", "tokens": [51197, 3013, 5607, 505, 6239, 281, 264, 15765, 321, 366, 12736, 965, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071250974669937, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171537850148687e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 15294, "start": 172.68, "end": 179.2, "text": " I was recently reading through this massive stack of research originating from the Flixion Research Group, published in 2026.", "tokens": [51352, 286, 390, 3938, 3760, 807, 341, 5994, 8630, 295, 2132, 4957, 990, 490, 264, 3235, 970, 313, 10303, 10500, 11, 6572, 294, 945, 10880, 13, 51678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071250974669937, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171537850148687e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 15294, "start": 179.38, "end": 180.4, "text": " And it's a lot, right?", "tokens": [51687, 400, 309, 311, 257, 688, 11, 558, 30, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1071250974669937, "compression_ratio": 1.5853658536585367, "no_speech_prob": 1.6171537850148687e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 18040, "start": 180.4, "end": 185.42000000000002, "text": " Oh, it's incredibly dense, but it completely challenged how I view mathematical physics.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 309, 311, 6252, 18011, 11, 457, 309, 2584, 17737, 577, 286, 1910, 18894, 10649, 13, 50616], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10199821562994094, "compression_ratio": 1.4930875576036866, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842991644126944e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 18040, "start": 185.66, "end": 193.78, "text": " I have to say, when you sent these over to me, I was intimidated, to say the least, but also completely hooked once I got into it.", "tokens": [50628, 286, 362, 281, 584, 11, 562, 291, 2279, 613, 670, 281, 385, 11, 286, 390, 40234, 11, 281, 584, 264, 1935, 11, 457, 611, 2584, 20410, 1564, 286, 658, 666, 309, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10199821562994094, "compression_ratio": 1.4930875576036866, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842991644126944e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 18040, "start": 194.0, "end": 195.34, "text": " It's a fascinating collection.", "tokens": [51045, 467, 311, 257, 10343, 5765, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10199821562994094, "compression_ratio": 1.4930875576036866, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842991644126944e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 18040, "start": 195.58, "end": 199.82, "text": " First off, there's a companion piece in this stack called the RSVP Codex.", "tokens": [51124, 2386, 766, 11, 456, 311, 257, 22363, 2522, 294, 341, 8630, 1219, 264, 25855, 53, 47, 15549, 87, 13, 51336], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10199821562994094, "compression_ratio": 1.4930875576036866, "no_speech_prob": 1.2842991644126944e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 19982, "start": 199.82, "end": 208.82, "text": " And honestly, it reads less like a physics paper and more like a philosophical manifesto that got, like, hidden inside an abstract algebra textbook.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 6095, 11, 309, 15700, 1570, 411, 257, 10649, 3035, 293, 544, 411, 257, 25066, 10067, 78, 300, 658, 11, 411, 11, 7633, 1854, 364, 12649, 21989, 25591, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12872083069848234, "compression_ratio": 1.4947368421052631, "no_speech_prob": 1.4215853971419334e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 19982, "start": 209.54, "end": 210.98, "text": " That is a perfect description of it.", "tokens": [50851, 663, 307, 257, 2176, 3855, 295, 309, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12872083069848234, "compression_ratio": 1.4947368421052631, "no_speech_prob": 1.4215853971419334e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 19982, "start": 211.04, "end": 217.79999999999998, "text": " It's basically an index of essays connecting these deep mathematical structures to human concepts.", "tokens": [50926, 467, 311, 1936, 364, 8186, 295, 35123, 11015, 613, 2452, 18894, 9227, 281, 1952, 10392, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12872083069848234, "compression_ratio": 1.4947368421052631, "no_speech_prob": 1.4215853971419334e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 21780, "start": 217.8, "end": 223.10000000000002, "text": " I mean, I'm talking about chapter titles like commutator ethics and the conservation of care.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 914, 11, 286, 478, 1417, 466, 7187, 12992, 411, 800, 325, 1639, 19769, 293, 264, 16185, 295, 1127, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13260908480043765, "compression_ratio": 1.63135593220339, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778492236049544e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 21780, "start": 223.68, "end": 226.84, "text": " It sets this beautifully provocative tone right out of the gate.", "tokens": [50659, 467, 6352, 341, 16525, 47663, 8027, 558, 484, 295, 264, 8539, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13260908480043765, "compression_ratio": 1.63135593220339, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778492236049544e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 21780, "start": 227.14000000000001, "end": 231.58, "text": " It suggests that the mathematical grammar we use isn't just cold, objective calculation.", "tokens": [50832, 467, 13409, 300, 264, 18894, 22317, 321, 764, 1943, 380, 445, 3554, 11, 10024, 17108, 13, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13260908480043765, "compression_ratio": 1.63135593220339, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778492236049544e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 21780, "start": 232.12, "end": 240.52, "text": " It implies that our math might actually reflect the specific way human observation and, well, human consciousness interface with reality.", "tokens": [51081, 467, 18779, 300, 527, 5221, 1062, 767, 5031, 264, 2685, 636, 1952, 14816, 293, 11, 731, 11, 1952, 10081, 9226, 365, 4103, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13260908480043765, "compression_ratio": 1.63135593220339, "no_speech_prob": 1.3778492236049544e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 24052, "start": 240.52, "end": 241.74, "text": " Which is a wild thought.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 257, 4868, 1194, 13, 50426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12354657456681535, "compression_ratio": 1.5507246376811594, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 24052, "start": 242.4, "end": 251.62, "text": " But the main event for us today, the real heavy lifting of this deep dive, is a rigorous 78-page treatise titled Unistochastic Quantum Mechanics.", "tokens": [50459, 583, 264, 2135, 2280, 337, 505, 965, 11, 264, 957, 4676, 15798, 295, 341, 2452, 9192, 11, 307, 257, 29882, 26369, 12, 15161, 2387, 908, 19841, 1156, 468, 8997, 2750, 44964, 30175, 1167, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12354657456681535, "compression_ratio": 1.5507246376811594, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 24052, "start": 251.74, "end": 253.42000000000002, "text": " And rigorous is really putting it mildly.", "tokens": [50926, 400, 29882, 307, 534, 3372, 309, 15154, 356, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12354657456681535, "compression_ratio": 1.5507246376811594, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 24052, "start": 253.5, "end": 254.66000000000003, "text": " It is brutally dense.", "tokens": [51014, 467, 307, 48476, 18011, 13, 51072], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12354657456681535, "compression_ratio": 1.5507246376811594, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 24052, "start": 255.06, "end": 259.52, "text": " But what makes this treatise so gripping, I think, is the author's method.", "tokens": [51092, 583, 437, 1669, 341, 2387, 908, 370, 17865, 3759, 11, 286, 519, 11, 307, 264, 3793, 311, 3170, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12354657456681535, "compression_ratio": 1.5507246376811594, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 24052, "start": 260.52, "end": 266.40000000000003, "text": " You know how in a standard college physics class, the professor just writes the Schrodinger equation on the chalkboard", "tokens": [51365, 509, 458, 577, 294, 257, 3832, 3859, 10649, 1508, 11, 264, 8304, 445, 13657, 264, 2065, 340, 3584, 260, 5367, 322, 264, 28660, 3787, 51659], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12354657456681535, "compression_ratio": 1.5507246376811594, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674032167664609e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 26640, "start": 266.4, "end": 271.26, "text": " and essentially says, accept this, memorize it, and let's move on.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 4476, 1619, 11, 3241, 341, 11, 27478, 309, 11, 293, 718, 311, 1286, 322, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223497103800817, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108595577227214e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 26640, "start": 271.32, "end": 272.62, "text": " Just shut up and calculate, yeah?", "tokens": [50611, 1449, 5309, 493, 293, 8873, 11, 1338, 30, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223497103800817, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108595577227214e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 26640, "start": 272.62, "end": 272.91999999999996, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50676, 7587, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223497103800817, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108595577227214e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 26640, "start": 273.21999999999997, "end": 274.44, "text": " The shut up and calculate approach.", "tokens": [50706, 440, 5309, 493, 293, 8873, 3109, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223497103800817, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108595577227214e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 26640, "start": 274.88, "end": 277.7, "text": " The author of this text absolutely refuses to do that.", "tokens": [50789, 440, 3793, 295, 341, 2487, 3122, 33222, 281, 360, 300, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223497103800817, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108595577227214e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 26640, "start": 277.78, "end": 279.94, "text": " They refuse to just postulate quantum mechanics.", "tokens": [50934, 814, 16791, 281, 445, 2183, 5256, 13018, 12939, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223497103800817, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108595577227214e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 26640, "start": 280.15999999999997, "end": 283.88, "text": " They attempt to build the entire quantum universe from scratch.", "tokens": [51053, 814, 5217, 281, 1322, 264, 2302, 13018, 6445, 490, 8459, 13, 51239], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223497103800817, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108595577227214e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 26640, "start": 283.88, "end": 289.0, "text": " And they do it using nothing but basic rules about probability and information loss.", "tokens": [51239, 400, 436, 360, 309, 1228, 1825, 457, 3875, 4474, 466, 8482, 293, 1589, 4470, 13, 51495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223497103800817, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108595577227214e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 26640, "start": 289.34, "end": 294.26, "text": " What really stands out to me is the author's strict discipline here.", "tokens": [51512, 708, 534, 7382, 484, 281, 385, 307, 264, 3793, 311, 10910, 13635, 510, 13, 51758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14223497103800817, "compression_ratio": 1.667857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108595577227214e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 29426, "start": 294.26, "end": 296.86, "text": " They maintain what they call an assumption ledger.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 6909, 437, 436, 818, 364, 15302, 4684, 1321, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 29426, "start": 297.12, "end": 298.0, "text": " Yes, the ledger.", "tokens": [50508, 1079, 11, 264, 4684, 1321, 13, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 29426, "start": 298.14, "end": 299.03999999999996, "text": " I love this part.", "tokens": [50559, 286, 959, 341, 644, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 29426, "start": 299.12, "end": 299.92, "text": " It's so cool.", "tokens": [50608, 467, 311, 370, 1627, 13, 50648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 29426, "start": 300.24, "end": 305.03999999999996, "text": " At the end of every single chapter, there is this brutal, uncompromising audit.", "tokens": [50664, 1711, 264, 917, 295, 633, 2167, 7187, 11, 456, 307, 341, 17878, 11, 8585, 28722, 3436, 17748, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 29426, "start": 305.53999999999996, "end": 310.32, "text": " A literal box on the page that states, here is exactly what we have mathematically proven,", "tokens": [50929, 316, 20411, 2424, 322, 264, 3028, 300, 4368, 11, 510, 307, 2293, 437, 321, 362, 44003, 12785, 11, 51168], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 29426, "start": 310.58, "end": 313.42, "text": " and here is exactly what we had to assume to get here.", "tokens": [51181, 293, 510, 307, 2293, 437, 321, 632, 281, 6552, 281, 483, 510, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 29426, "start": 313.7, "end": 317.06, "text": " They don't let you sneak any hidden physics in through the back door.", "tokens": [51337, 814, 500, 380, 718, 291, 13164, 604, 7633, 10649, 294, 807, 264, 646, 2853, 13, 51505], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 29426, "start": 317.56, "end": 321.26, "text": " Every single piece of reality has to be meticulously accounted for.", "tokens": [51530, 2048, 2167, 2522, 295, 4103, 575, 281, 312, 41566, 25038, 43138, 337, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 29426, "start": 321.62, "end": 322.7, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this.", "tokens": [51733, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 51787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1260931853092078, "compression_ratio": 1.6827586206896552, "no_speech_prob": 1.8108431421026694e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 32270, "start": 322.7, "end": 328.7, "text": " Because if we're going to build the universe from scratch, we can't start with atoms or", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 321, 434, 516, 281, 1322, 264, 6445, 490, 8459, 11, 321, 393, 380, 722, 365, 16871, 420, 50665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 32270, "start": 328.7, "end": 331.44, "text": " multidimensional space or entanglement.", "tokens": [50665, 2120, 327, 332, 11075, 1901, 420, 948, 656, 3054, 13, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 32270, "start": 331.56, "end": 332.97999999999996, "text": " No, that's way too complex.", "tokens": [50808, 883, 11, 300, 311, 636, 886, 3997, 13, 50879], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 32270, "start": 333.08, "end": 335.7, "text": " We have to start at the absolute, bare bones bottom.", "tokens": [50884, 492, 362, 281, 722, 412, 264, 8236, 11, 6949, 10491, 2767, 13, 51015], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 32270, "start": 336.15999999999997, "end": 338.62, "text": " We have to talk about basic states of knowledge.", "tokens": [51038, 492, 362, 281, 751, 466, 3875, 4368, 295, 3601, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 32270, "start": 339.18, "end": 340.98, "text": " Essentially, we're talking about coin flips.", "tokens": [51189, 23596, 11, 321, 434, 1417, 466, 11464, 40249, 13, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 32270, "start": 341.3, "end": 341.59999999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51295, 1779, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 32270, "start": 341.96, "end": 347.24, "text": " We begin with a geometric concept the text calls the probability simplex.", "tokens": [51328, 492, 1841, 365, 257, 33246, 3410, 264, 2487, 5498, 264, 8482, 2199, 87, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 32270, "start": 347.38, "end": 349.0, "text": " Okay, that already sounds like heavy jargon.", "tokens": [51599, 1033, 11, 300, 1217, 3263, 411, 4676, 15181, 10660, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 32270, "start": 349.4, "end": 351.2, "text": " What exactly is a simplex?", "tokens": [51700, 708, 2293, 307, 257, 2199, 87, 30, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14128933107949854, "compression_ratio": 1.602112676056338, "no_speech_prob": 1.8179158265546613e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 35120, "start": 351.2, "end": 353.0, "text": " Don't let the name intimidate you.", "tokens": [50365, 1468, 380, 718, 264, 1315, 17042, 473, 291, 13, 50455], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276107135119739, "compression_ratio": 1.6169354838709677, "no_speech_prob": 1.1463311853573965e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 35120, "start": 353.15999999999997, "end": 356.68, "text": " Think of it as a shape that just represents all possible states of knowledge.", "tokens": [50463, 6557, 295, 309, 382, 257, 3909, 300, 445, 8855, 439, 1944, 4368, 295, 3601, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276107135119739, "compression_ratio": 1.6169354838709677, "no_speech_prob": 1.1463311853573965e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 35120, "start": 356.84, "end": 358.03999999999996, "text": " Okay, a shape of knowledge.", "tokens": [50647, 1033, 11, 257, 3909, 295, 3601, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276107135119739, "compression_ratio": 1.6169354838709677, "no_speech_prob": 1.1463311853573965e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 35120, "start": 358.12, "end": 358.34, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50711, 865, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276107135119739, "compression_ratio": 1.6169354838709677, "no_speech_prob": 1.1463311853573965e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 35120, "start": 358.56, "end": 363.42, "text": " Let's say you have a system with a set of distinct, distinguishable outcomes.", "tokens": [50733, 961, 311, 584, 291, 362, 257, 1185, 365, 257, 992, 295, 10644, 11, 20206, 712, 10070, 13, 50976], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276107135119739, "compression_ratio": 1.6169354838709677, "no_speech_prob": 1.1463311853573965e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 35120, "start": 363.56, "end": 367.82, "text": " It could be the six faces of a die or, you know, different clicks on a Geiger counter.", "tokens": [50983, 467, 727, 312, 264, 2309, 8475, 295, 257, 978, 420, 11, 291, 458, 11, 819, 18521, 322, 257, 2876, 4810, 5682, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276107135119739, "compression_ratio": 1.6169354838709677, "no_speech_prob": 1.1463311853573965e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 35120, "start": 368.0, "end": 368.2, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51205, 1033, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276107135119739, "compression_ratio": 1.6169354838709677, "no_speech_prob": 1.1463311853573965e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 35120, "start": 368.44, "end": 368.9, "text": " Simple of?", "tokens": [51227, 21532, 295, 30, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276107135119739, "compression_ratio": 1.6169354838709677, "no_speech_prob": 1.1463311853573965e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 35120, "start": 369.2, "end": 372.91999999999996, "text": " A state of knowledge is just a list of probabilities for those outcomes.", "tokens": [51265, 316, 1785, 295, 3601, 307, 445, 257, 1329, 295, 33783, 337, 729, 10070, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1276107135119739, "compression_ratio": 1.6169354838709677, "no_speech_prob": 1.1463311853573965e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 37292, "start": 372.92, "end": 378.7, "text": " So, if I have a loaded die, my list might say there's a 50% chance of rolling a six and maybe", "tokens": [50365, 407, 11, 498, 286, 362, 257, 13210, 978, 11, 452, 1329, 1062, 584, 456, 311, 257, 2625, 4, 2931, 295, 9439, 257, 2309, 293, 1310, 50654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13688639472512637, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302494956263233e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 37292, "start": 378.7, "end": 381.16, "text": " a 10% chance for each of the other five numbers.", "tokens": [50654, 257, 1266, 4, 2931, 337, 1184, 295, 264, 661, 1732, 3547, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13688639472512637, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302494956263233e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 37292, "start": 381.84000000000003, "end": 382.24, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50811, 7587, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13688639472512637, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302494956263233e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 37292, "start": 382.54, "end": 385.76, "text": " And all those percentages, they have to add up to 100%.", "tokens": [50846, 400, 439, 729, 42270, 11, 436, 362, 281, 909, 493, 281, 2319, 6856, 51007], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13688639472512637, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302494956263233e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 37292, "start": 385.76, "end": 388.42, "text": " You are 100% sure something is going to happen.", "tokens": [51007, 509, 366, 2319, 4, 988, 746, 307, 516, 281, 1051, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13688639472512637, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302494956263233e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 37292, "start": 388.72, "end": 390.26, "text": " You just don't know exactly what.", "tokens": [51155, 509, 445, 500, 380, 458, 2293, 437, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13688639472512637, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302494956263233e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 39026, "start": 390.26, "end": 391.92, "text": " That's the fundamental rule of probability.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 264, 8088, 4978, 295, 8482, 13, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18636595862252373, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 39026, "start": 392.09999999999997, "end": 392.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50457, 1779, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18636595862252373, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 39026, "start": 392.53999999999996, "end": 396.58, "text": " So, the probabilities cannot be negative and they must sum to one.", "tokens": [50479, 407, 11, 264, 33783, 2644, 312, 3671, 293, 436, 1633, 2408, 281, 472, 13, 50681], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18636595862252373, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 39026, "start": 397.21999999999997, "end": 403.53999999999996, "text": " Now, geometrically, if you graph all those possible valid lists of probabilities, they", "tokens": [50713, 823, 11, 12956, 81, 984, 11, 498, 291, 4295, 439, 729, 1944, 7363, 14511, 295, 33783, 11, 436, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18636595862252373, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 39026, "start": 403.53999999999996, "end": 407.34, "text": " form a shape and that shape is the probability simplex.", "tokens": [51029, 1254, 257, 3909, 293, 300, 3909, 307, 264, 8482, 2199, 87, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18636595862252373, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 39026, "start": 407.42, "end": 407.56, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51223, 1779, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18636595862252373, "compression_ratio": 1.5892857142857142, "no_speech_prob": 1.4266196730894354e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 40756, "start": 407.56, "end": 411.52, "text": " The sharp corners of this shape represent absolute certainty.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 8199, 12413, 295, 341, 3909, 2906, 8236, 27022, 13, 50563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 40756, "start": 412.0, "end": 415.92, "text": " For example, a state where you are 100% sure you will roll a six.", "tokens": [50587, 1171, 1365, 11, 257, 1785, 689, 291, 366, 2319, 4, 988, 291, 486, 3373, 257, 2309, 13, 50783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 40756, "start": 416.4, "end": 417.1, "text": " That's a corner.", "tokens": [50807, 663, 311, 257, 4538, 13, 50842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 40756, "start": 417.42, "end": 421.9, "text": " And then everything inside the volume of the shape, that represents some degree of uncertainty,", "tokens": [50858, 400, 550, 1203, 1854, 264, 5523, 295, 264, 3909, 11, 300, 8855, 512, 4314, 295, 15697, 11, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 40756, "start": 422.1, "end": 422.26, "text": " right?", "tokens": [51092, 558, 30, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 40756, "start": 422.36, "end": 423.4, "text": " Like my loaded die.", "tokens": [51105, 1743, 452, 13210, 978, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 40756, "start": 424.0, "end": 424.52, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51187, 48746, 736, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 40756, "start": 424.92, "end": 430.02, "text": " Now, if we want to build a physical theory, we need to mathematically describe how that system", "tokens": [51233, 823, 11, 498, 321, 528, 281, 1322, 257, 4001, 5261, 11, 321, 643, 281, 44003, 6786, 577, 300, 1185, 51488], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 40756, "start": 430.02, "end": 430.94, "text": " changes over time.", "tokens": [51488, 2962, 670, 565, 13, 51534], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 40756, "start": 431.08, "end": 435.02, "text": " So, we use a transition matrix, specifically something called a stochastic map.", "tokens": [51541, 407, 11, 321, 764, 257, 6034, 8141, 11, 4682, 746, 1219, 257, 342, 8997, 2750, 4471, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 40756, "start": 435.16, "end": 436.4, "text": " Well, let me make sure I'm following this.", "tokens": [51745, 1042, 11, 718, 385, 652, 988, 286, 478, 3480, 341, 13, 51807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1200353280821843, "compression_ratio": 1.5895061728395061, "no_speech_prob": 1.8040597227902966e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 43640, "start": 436.4, "end": 442.03999999999996, "text": " A stochastic map, if I have my list of probabilities today, my state of knowledge right now, this", "tokens": [50365, 316, 342, 8997, 2750, 4471, 11, 498, 286, 362, 452, 1329, 295, 33783, 965, 11, 452, 1785, 295, 3601, 558, 586, 11, 341, 50647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1161823842062879, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.1785369772102094e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 43640, "start": 442.03999999999996, "end": 445.7, "text": " map is just the mathematical rule that tells me what my probabilities will be tomorrow.", "tokens": [50647, 4471, 307, 445, 264, 18894, 4978, 300, 5112, 385, 437, 452, 33783, 486, 312, 4153, 13, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1161823842062879, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.1785369772102094e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 43640, "start": 446.06, "end": 447.47999999999996, "text": " That's a perfect way to look at it.", "tokens": [50848, 663, 311, 257, 2176, 636, 281, 574, 412, 309, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1161823842062879, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.1785369772102094e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 43640, "start": 447.62, "end": 452.38, "text": " And the defining rule for a stochastic matrix is that its columns have to add up to one.", "tokens": [50926, 400, 264, 17827, 4978, 337, 257, 342, 8997, 2750, 8141, 307, 300, 1080, 13766, 362, 281, 909, 493, 281, 472, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1161823842062879, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.1785369772102094e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 43640, "start": 453.0, "end": 455.28, "text": " Because probability can't just appear or disappear.", "tokens": [51195, 1436, 8482, 393, 380, 445, 4204, 420, 11596, 13, 51309], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1161823842062879, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.1785369772102094e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 43640, "start": 455.58, "end": 456.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51324, 7587, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1161823842062879, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.1785369772102094e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 43640, "start": 456.62, "end": 460.29999999999995, "text": " Probability cannot be created out of thin air and it cannot be magically destroyed.", "tokens": [51376, 8736, 2310, 2644, 312, 2942, 484, 295, 5862, 1988, 293, 309, 2644, 312, 39763, 8937, 13, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1161823842062879, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.1785369772102094e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 43640, "start": 460.76, "end": 465.64, "text": " If you start with a valid state of knowledge, the map guarantees you end up with a valid", "tokens": [51583, 759, 291, 722, 365, 257, 7363, 1785, 295, 3601, 11, 264, 4471, 32567, 291, 917, 493, 365, 257, 7363, 51827], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1161823842062879, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.1785369772102094e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 46564, "start": 465.64, "end": 466.5, "text": " state of knowledge.", "tokens": [50365, 1785, 295, 3601, 13, 50408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 46564, "start": 466.59999999999997, "end": 467.09999999999997, "text": " That makes sense.", "tokens": [50413, 663, 1669, 2020, 13, 50438], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 46564, "start": 467.15999999999997, "end": 468.36, "text": " It's just strict accounting.", "tokens": [50441, 467, 311, 445, 10910, 19163, 13, 50501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 46564, "start": 468.97999999999996, "end": 474.4, "text": " But here is where the author adds the very first physical constraint to our whole universe", "tokens": [50532, 583, 510, 307, 689, 264, 3793, 10860, 264, 588, 700, 4001, 25534, 281, 527, 1379, 6445, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 46564, "start": 474.4, "end": 475.06, "text": " building project.", "tokens": [50803, 2390, 1716, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 46564, "start": 475.59999999999997, "end": 478.91999999999996, "text": " The text introduces by stochastic maps.", "tokens": [50863, 440, 2487, 31472, 538, 342, 8997, 2750, 11317, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 46564, "start": 479.26, "end": 479.96, "text": " By stochastic.", "tokens": [51046, 3146, 342, 8997, 2750, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 46564, "start": 480.08, "end": 481.44, "text": " So, the prefix by meaning two.", "tokens": [51087, 407, 11, 264, 46969, 538, 3620, 732, 13, 51155], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 46564, "start": 481.68, "end": 481.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51167, 1779, 13, 51180], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 46564, "start": 482.2, "end": 486.18, "text": " Not only do the columns have to sum to one, but the rows have to sum to one as well.", "tokens": [51193, 1726, 787, 360, 264, 13766, 362, 281, 2408, 281, 472, 11, 457, 264, 13241, 362, 281, 2408, 281, 472, 382, 731, 13, 51392], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 46564, "start": 486.24, "end": 486.41999999999996, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51395, 1033, 13, 51404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19532779511951265, "compression_ratio": 1.5608695652173914, "no_speech_prob": 1.728189856844975e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 48642, "start": 486.42, "end": 487.66, "text": " I can see the symmetry there.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 393, 536, 264, 25440, 456, 13, 50427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 48642, "start": 487.74, "end": 488.72, "text": " It's mathematically neat.", "tokens": [50431, 467, 311, 44003, 10654, 13, 50480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 48642, "start": 489.24, "end": 490.48, "text": " But why does that matter physically?", "tokens": [50506, 583, 983, 775, 300, 1871, 9762, 30, 50568], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 48642, "start": 490.84000000000003, "end": 493.0, "text": " Why do we care about the rows adding up to one?", "tokens": [50586, 1545, 360, 321, 1127, 466, 264, 13241, 5127, 493, 281, 472, 30, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 48642, "start": 493.22, "end": 498.84000000000003, "text": " Because row normalization introduces this vital concept of reversibility and information", "tokens": [50705, 1436, 5386, 2710, 2144, 31472, 341, 11707, 3410, 295, 14582, 2841, 293, 1589, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 48642, "start": 498.84000000000003, "end": 499.62, "text": " preservation.", "tokens": [50986, 27257, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 48642, "start": 499.98, "end": 500.42, "text": " Reversibility.", "tokens": [51043, 1300, 840, 2841, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 48642, "start": 500.52000000000004, "end": 500.68, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51070, 1033, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 48642, "start": 501.24, "end": 503.42, "text": " Let's think about a deterministic map.", "tokens": [51106, 961, 311, 519, 466, 257, 15957, 3142, 4471, 13, 51215], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 48642, "start": 503.8, "end": 507.66, "text": " A rule that simply relabels outcomes without losing any underlying detail.", "tokens": [51234, 316, 4978, 300, 2935, 1039, 455, 1625, 10070, 1553, 7027, 604, 14217, 2607, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 48642, "start": 508.24, "end": 512.76, "text": " The text highlights a foundational piece of math here called the Berkhoff von Neumann theorem.", "tokens": [51456, 440, 2487, 14254, 257, 32195, 2522, 295, 5221, 510, 1219, 264, 5637, 74, 1289, 602, 2957, 1734, 449, 969, 20904, 13, 51682], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20006165504455567, "compression_ratio": 1.5819397993311037, "no_speech_prob": 1.5729647402304425e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 51276, "start": 512.76, "end": 514.38, "text": " Oh, that sounds serious.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 300, 3263, 3156, 13, 50446], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 51276, "start": 514.54, "end": 514.98, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50454, 467, 307, 13, 50476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 51276, "start": 515.22, "end": 517.24, "text": " But it proves something quite beautiful.", "tokens": [50488, 583, 309, 25019, 746, 1596, 2238, 13, 50589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 51276, "start": 517.88, "end": 524.18, "text": " It proves that this entire geometric space of bistochastic maps, a shape known as the Berkhoff", "tokens": [50621, 467, 25019, 300, 341, 2302, 33246, 1901, 295, 18209, 8997, 2750, 11317, 11, 257, 3909, 2570, 382, 264, 5637, 74, 1289, 602, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 51276, "start": 524.18, "end": 528.4399999999999, "text": " polytope, is completely defined by perfect permutations.", "tokens": [50936, 6754, 83, 1114, 11, 307, 2584, 7642, 538, 2176, 4784, 325, 763, 13, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 51276, "start": 528.8, "end": 529.36, "text": " Permutations.", "tokens": [51167, 41006, 325, 763, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 51276, "start": 529.56, "end": 531.78, "text": " Like shuffling a deck of cards.", "tokens": [51205, 1743, 402, 1245, 1688, 257, 9341, 295, 5632, 13, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 51276, "start": 531.9399999999999, "end": 532.84, "text": " Yes, exactly.", "tokens": [51324, 1079, 11, 2293, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 51276, "start": 533.3, "end": 535.34, "text": " Think about what happens when you shuffle a deck.", "tokens": [51392, 6557, 466, 437, 2314, 562, 291, 39426, 257, 9341, 13, 51494], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 51276, "start": 535.8, "end": 537.26, "text": " You aren't destroying any cards.", "tokens": [51517, 509, 3212, 380, 19926, 604, 5632, 13, 51590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 51276, "start": 537.36, "end": 539.74, "text": " You aren't cutting two cards in half and gluing them together.", "tokens": [51595, 509, 3212, 380, 6492, 732, 5632, 294, 1922, 293, 1563, 9635, 552, 1214, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 51276, "start": 539.84, "end": 540.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51719, 1779, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 51276, "start": 540.1, "end": 541.8, "text": " Just perfectly swapping their positions.", "tokens": [51732, 1449, 6239, 1693, 10534, 641, 8432, 13, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1635432944578283, "compression_ratio": 1.6539792387543253, "no_speech_prob": 1.9969095821359417e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 54180, "start": 541.8, "end": 543.4399999999999, "text": " It's entirely reversible.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 7696, 44788, 13, 50447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 54180, "start": 543.66, "end": 545.74, "text": " If I recorded the shuffle, I could just unshuffle it.", "tokens": [50458, 759, 286, 8287, 264, 39426, 11, 286, 727, 445, 2693, 71, 21665, 309, 13, 50562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 54180, "start": 546.0, "end": 546.4, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50575, 48746, 736, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 54180, "start": 546.7199999999999, "end": 551.0, "text": " The extreme points, the sharpest corners of this Berkhoff polytope shape we're talking", "tokens": [50611, 440, 8084, 2793, 11, 264, 8199, 377, 12413, 295, 341, 5637, 74, 1289, 602, 6754, 83, 1114, 3909, 321, 434, 1417, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 54180, "start": 551.0, "end": 555.52, "text": " about, are exactly these perfect reversible shuffles.", "tokens": [50825, 466, 11, 366, 2293, 613, 2176, 44788, 402, 1245, 904, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 54180, "start": 555.5799999999999, "end": 555.8199999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51054, 1033, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 54180, "start": 555.9799999999999, "end": 556.4599999999999, "text": " I'm with you.", "tokens": [51074, 286, 478, 365, 291, 13, 51098], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 54180, "start": 556.66, "end": 562.28, "text": " And any point inside the shape, any bistochastic map at all, can be mathematically expressed", "tokens": [51108, 400, 604, 935, 1854, 264, 3909, 11, 604, 18209, 8997, 2750, 4471, 412, 439, 11, 393, 312, 44003, 12675, 51389], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 54180, "start": 562.28, "end": 564.54, "text": " as a mixture of these perfect shuffles.", "tokens": [51389, 382, 257, 9925, 295, 613, 2176, 402, 1245, 904, 13, 51502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 54180, "start": 564.78, "end": 568.3199999999999, "text": " Let me try an analogy here to see if I'm grasping the physical consequence of this.", "tokens": [51514, 961, 385, 853, 364, 21663, 510, 281, 536, 498, 286, 478, 29444, 3381, 264, 4001, 18326, 295, 341, 13, 51691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12497102577267712, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671713059217662e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 56832, "start": 568.32, "end": 572.5200000000001, "text": " It sounds like the difference between mixing paint and just swapping sealed cans of paint.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 3263, 411, 264, 2649, 1296, 11983, 4225, 293, 445, 1693, 10534, 21514, 21835, 295, 4225, 13, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14332388242085775, "compression_ratio": 1.2421052631578948, "no_speech_prob": 1.5041932543286007e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 56832, "start": 572.6400000000001, "end": 573.58, "text": " I like where this is going.", "tokens": [50581, 286, 411, 689, 341, 307, 516, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14332388242085775, "compression_ratio": 1.2421052631578948, "no_speech_prob": 1.5041932543286007e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 57358, "start": 573.58, "end": 578.5, "text": " So let's say I have a sealed can of red paint and a sealed can of blue paint on a shelf.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 718, 311, 584, 286, 362, 257, 21514, 393, 295, 2182, 4225, 293, 257, 21514, 393, 295, 3344, 4225, 322, 257, 15222, 13, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442871190324613, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127115055371676e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 57358, "start": 579.0, "end": 581.5200000000001, "text": " If I swap their places, I haven't lost any information.", "tokens": [50636, 759, 286, 18135, 641, 3190, 11, 286, 2378, 380, 2731, 604, 1589, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442871190324613, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127115055371676e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 57358, "start": 581.7800000000001, "end": 582.5200000000001, "text": " That's a permutation.", "tokens": [50775, 663, 311, 257, 4784, 11380, 13, 50812], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442871190324613, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127115055371676e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 57358, "start": 582.7800000000001, "end": 582.86, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50825, 1779, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442871190324613, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127115055371676e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 57358, "start": 583.0200000000001, "end": 584.4000000000001, "text": " I can easily swap them back.", "tokens": [50837, 286, 393, 3612, 18135, 552, 646, 13, 50906], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442871190324613, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127115055371676e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 57358, "start": 584.46, "end": 586.86, "text": " I know exactly where the red is and exactly where the blue is.", "tokens": [50909, 286, 458, 2293, 689, 264, 2182, 307, 293, 2293, 689, 264, 3344, 307, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14442871190324613, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127115055371676e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 58686, "start": 586.86, "end": 593.98, "text": " But if I open the cans, pour the red paint and the blue paint into a single bucket and stir", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 286, 1269, 264, 21835, 11, 2016, 264, 2182, 4225, 293, 264, 3344, 4225, 666, 257, 2167, 13058, 293, 8946, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13224937148013358, "compression_ratio": 1.725868725868726, "no_speech_prob": 1.244782705731029e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 58686, "start": 593.98, "end": 596.14, "text": " them together, I've created purple.", "tokens": [50721, 552, 1214, 11, 286, 600, 2942, 9656, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13224937148013358, "compression_ratio": 1.725868725868726, "no_speech_prob": 1.244782705731029e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 58686, "start": 596.92, "end": 598.6, "text": " And can you unmix that bucket?", "tokens": [50868, 400, 393, 291, 19334, 970, 300, 13058, 30, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13224937148013358, "compression_ratio": 1.725868725868726, "no_speech_prob": 1.244782705731029e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 58686, "start": 598.88, "end": 599.28, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50966, 883, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13224937148013358, "compression_ratio": 1.725868725868726, "no_speech_prob": 1.244782705731029e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 58686, "start": 599.88, "end": 604.38, "text": " I can never, ever pull the pure red and pure blue back out of that purple bucket.", "tokens": [51016, 286, 393, 1128, 11, 1562, 2235, 264, 6075, 2182, 293, 6075, 3344, 646, 484, 295, 300, 9656, 13058, 13, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13224937148013358, "compression_ratio": 1.725868725868726, "no_speech_prob": 1.244782705731029e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 58686, "start": 604.76, "end": 606.3000000000001, "text": " I've coarse grained the system.", "tokens": [51260, 286, 600, 39312, 1295, 2001, 264, 1185, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13224937148013358, "compression_ratio": 1.725868725868726, "no_speech_prob": 1.244782705731029e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 58686, "start": 606.64, "end": 609.48, "text": " I've permanently lost the original distinct information.", "tokens": [51354, 286, 600, 24042, 2731, 264, 3380, 10644, 1589, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13224937148013358, "compression_ratio": 1.725868725868726, "no_speech_prob": 1.244782705731029e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 58686, "start": 609.76, "end": 611.3000000000001, "text": " That is a brilliant analogy.", "tokens": [51510, 663, 307, 257, 10248, 21663, 13, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13224937148013358, "compression_ratio": 1.725868725868726, "no_speech_prob": 1.244782705731029e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 58686, "start": 611.78, "end": 615.5, "text": " Mixing the paint is what happens when you blend those perfect permutations together.", "tokens": [51611, 12769, 278, 264, 4225, 307, 437, 2314, 562, 291, 10628, 729, 2176, 4784, 325, 763, 1214, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13224937148013358, "compression_ratio": 1.725868725868726, "no_speech_prob": 1.244782705731029e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 61550, "start": 615.5, "end": 619.76, "text": " And this leads directly to a profound physical consequence involving entropy.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 6689, 3838, 281, 257, 14382, 4001, 18326, 17030, 30867, 13, 50578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 61550, "start": 620.34, "end": 620.5, "text": " Entropy.", "tokens": [50607, 3951, 27514, 13, 50615], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 61550, "start": 620.78, "end": 621.92, "text": " The measurement of disorder.", "tokens": [50629, 440, 13160, 295, 13399, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 61550, "start": 622.08, "end": 622.44, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50694, 7587, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 61550, "start": 622.82, "end": 625.66, "text": " The text leans on a mathematical concept called majorization.", "tokens": [50731, 440, 2487, 476, 599, 322, 257, 18894, 3410, 1219, 2563, 2144, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 61550, "start": 626.04, "end": 629.84, "text": " I won't drag us through the dense equations, but essentially, majorization proves that if", "tokens": [50892, 286, 1582, 380, 5286, 505, 807, 264, 18011, 11787, 11, 457, 4476, 11, 2563, 2144, 25019, 300, 498, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 61550, "start": 629.84, "end": 635.06, "text": " you evolve a system using a bistochastic map, if you mix those paint cans, you can never,", "tokens": [51082, 291, 16693, 257, 1185, 1228, 257, 18209, 8997, 2750, 4471, 11, 498, 291, 2890, 729, 4225, 21835, 11, 291, 393, 1128, 11, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 61550, "start": 635.38, "end": 637.9, "text": " ever decrease the Shannon entropy of your knowledge.", "tokens": [51359, 1562, 11514, 264, 28974, 30867, 295, 428, 3601, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 61550, "start": 638.12, "end": 638.36, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51496, 1033, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 61550, "start": 638.52, "end": 640.42, "text": " Let's pause on Shannon entropy for a second.", "tokens": [51516, 961, 311, 10465, 322, 28974, 30867, 337, 257, 1150, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1628989521254841, "compression_ratio": 1.6549295774647887, "no_speech_prob": 1.675158492822626e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 64042, "start": 640.42, "end": 645.18, "text": " For someone listening who hasn't taken an information theory class, what does that actually", "tokens": [50365, 1171, 1580, 4764, 567, 6132, 380, 2726, 364, 1589, 5261, 1508, 11, 437, 775, 300, 767, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545970916748046, "compression_ratio": 1.606425702811245, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 64042, "start": 645.18, "end": 646.9599999999999, "text": " mean in the context of our paint bucket?", "tokens": [50603, 914, 294, 264, 4319, 295, 527, 4225, 13058, 30, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545970916748046, "compression_ratio": 1.606425702811245, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 64042, "start": 647.52, "end": 651.4799999999999, "text": " Shannon entropy is essentially a measure of your surprise or your uncertainty.", "tokens": [50720, 28974, 30867, 307, 4476, 257, 3481, 295, 428, 6365, 420, 428, 15697, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545970916748046, "compression_ratio": 1.606425702811245, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 64042, "start": 651.8199999999999, "end": 651.9599999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50935, 1033, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545970916748046, "compression_ratio": 1.606425702811245, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 64042, "start": 652.04, "end": 657.16, "text": " If you know for a fact the can contains pure red paint, your uncertainty is zero.", "tokens": [50946, 759, 291, 458, 337, 257, 1186, 264, 393, 8306, 6075, 2182, 4225, 11, 428, 15697, 307, 4018, 13, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545970916748046, "compression_ratio": 1.606425702811245, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 64042, "start": 657.4399999999999, "end": 658.9599999999999, "text": " You aren't surprised when you open it.", "tokens": [51216, 509, 3212, 380, 6100, 562, 291, 1269, 309, 13, 51292], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545970916748046, "compression_ratio": 1.606425702811245, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 64042, "start": 659.06, "end": 660.1999999999999, "text": " The entropy is zero.", "tokens": [51297, 440, 30867, 307, 4018, 13, 51354], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545970916748046, "compression_ratio": 1.606425702811245, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 64042, "start": 660.26, "end": 660.42, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51357, 1779, 13, 51365], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545970916748046, "compression_ratio": 1.606425702811245, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 64042, "start": 660.4799999999999, "end": 662.0799999999999, "text": " Because I have perfect knowledge.", "tokens": [51368, 1436, 286, 362, 2176, 3601, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13545970916748046, "compression_ratio": 1.606425702811245, "no_speech_prob": 1.6815741507580917e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 66208, "start": 662.08, "end": 667.7800000000001, "text": " But if you pour red, blue, and yellow into a bucket and stir, and I ask you to pull out", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 291, 2016, 2182, 11, 3344, 11, 293, 5566, 666, 257, 13058, 293, 8946, 11, 293, 286, 1029, 291, 281, 2235, 484, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11257371115028311, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898011210101592e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 66208, "start": 667.7800000000001, "end": 673.1800000000001, "text": " a single drop and tell me what color the original pigments were, your uncertainty is massive.", "tokens": [50650, 257, 2167, 3270, 293, 980, 385, 437, 2017, 264, 3380, 8120, 1117, 645, 11, 428, 15697, 307, 5994, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11257371115028311, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898011210101592e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 66208, "start": 673.5400000000001, "end": 673.76, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50938, 865, 13, 50949], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11257371115028311, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898011210101592e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 66208, "start": 673.84, "end": 674.58, "text": " I have no idea.", "tokens": [50953, 286, 362, 572, 1558, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11257371115028311, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898011210101592e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 66208, "start": 674.82, "end": 674.98, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51002, 1779, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11257371115028311, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898011210101592e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 66208, "start": 675.0600000000001, "end": 676.38, "text": " So the entropy has increased.", "tokens": [51014, 407, 264, 30867, 575, 6505, 13, 51080], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11257371115028311, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898011210101592e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 66208, "start": 676.9000000000001, "end": 682.0, "text": " The math of majorization proves that under bistochastic evolution, your uncertainty can", "tokens": [51106, 440, 5221, 295, 2563, 2144, 25019, 300, 833, 18209, 8997, 2750, 9303, 11, 428, 15697, 393, 51361], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11257371115028311, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898011210101592e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 66208, "start": 682.0, "end": 683.86, "text": " only stay the same or go up.", "tokens": [51361, 787, 1754, 264, 912, 420, 352, 493, 13, 51454], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11257371115028311, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898011210101592e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 66208, "start": 684.0, "end": 686.0200000000001, "text": " Meaning things can only get more purple.", "tokens": [51461, 19948, 721, 393, 787, 483, 544, 9656, 13, 51562], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11257371115028311, "compression_ratio": 1.5793650793650793, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898011210101592e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 68602, "start": 686.02, "end": 692.12, "text": " The universe can never spontaneously unmix the bucket back into perfect red and perfect blue.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 6445, 393, 1128, 47632, 19334, 970, 264, 13058, 646, 666, 2176, 2182, 293, 2176, 3344, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 68602, "start": 692.1999999999999, "end": 692.6, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50674, 7587, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 68602, "start": 692.96, "end": 695.36, "text": " And let's consider the broader implications of that.", "tokens": [50712, 400, 718, 311, 1949, 264, 13227, 16602, 295, 300, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 68602, "start": 695.54, "end": 697.12, "text": " Notice what the author didn't do here.", "tokens": [50841, 13428, 437, 264, 3793, 994, 380, 360, 510, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 68602, "start": 697.1999999999999, "end": 697.78, "text": " What didn't they do?", "tokens": [50924, 708, 994, 380, 436, 360, 30, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 68602, "start": 697.9399999999999, "end": 701.06, "text": " They didn't import the second law of thermodynamics.", "tokens": [50961, 814, 994, 380, 974, 264, 1150, 2101, 295, 8810, 35483, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 68602, "start": 701.4, "end": 707.0, "text": " They didn't borrow concepts from like 19th century steam engine physics to force the universe", "tokens": [51134, 814, 994, 380, 11172, 10392, 490, 411, 1294, 392, 4901, 11952, 2848, 10649, 281, 3464, 264, 6445, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 68602, "start": 707.0, "end": 708.24, "text": " to behave a certain way.", "tokens": [51414, 281, 15158, 257, 1629, 636, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 68602, "start": 708.36, "end": 708.74, "text": " Oh, why?", "tokens": [51482, 876, 11, 983, 30, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 68602, "start": 708.74, "end": 714.74, "text": " They proved that entropy must increase as a purely structural geometric consequence of the", "tokens": [51501, 814, 14617, 300, 30867, 1633, 3488, 382, 257, 17491, 15067, 33246, 18326, 295, 264, 51801], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1530585369821322, "compression_ratio": 1.6342281879194631, "no_speech_prob": 1.5856375457437566e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 71474, "start": 714.74, "end": 715.72, "text": " Burkhoff polytope.", "tokens": [50365, 7031, 74, 1289, 602, 6754, 83, 1114, 13, 50414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 71474, "start": 716.58, "end": 719.4, "text": " The geometry forces the physics to exist.", "tokens": [50457, 440, 18426, 5874, 264, 10649, 281, 2514, 13, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 71474, "start": 719.76, "end": 720.9, "text": " That is incredibly cool.", "tokens": [50616, 663, 307, 6252, 1627, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 71474, "start": 721.04, "end": 726.48, "text": " We've derived the arrow of time, essentially, just from drawing a shape with rows and columns", "tokens": [50680, 492, 600, 18949, 264, 11610, 295, 565, 11, 4476, 11, 445, 490, 6316, 257, 3909, 365, 13241, 293, 13766, 50952], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 71474, "start": 726.48, "end": 727.32, "text": " that add up to one.", "tokens": [50952, 300, 909, 493, 281, 472, 13, 50994], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 71474, "start": 727.44, "end": 728.74, "text": " It's elegant, isn't it?", "tokens": [51000, 467, 311, 21117, 11, 1943, 380, 309, 30, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 71474, "start": 728.82, "end": 729.46, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [51069, 467, 534, 307, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 71474, "start": 729.8, "end": 731.82, "text": " But I have to push back here a little bit.", "tokens": [51118, 583, 286, 362, 281, 2944, 646, 510, 257, 707, 857, 13, 51219], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 71474, "start": 731.9, "end": 735.3, "text": " This all sounds like classical high school level probability.", "tokens": [51223, 639, 439, 3263, 411, 13735, 1090, 1395, 1496, 8482, 13, 51393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 71474, "start": 735.46, "end": 736.32, "text": " We're shuffling cards.", "tokens": [51401, 492, 434, 402, 1245, 1688, 5632, 13, 51444], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 71474, "start": 736.42, "end": 737.12, "text": " We're mixing paint.", "tokens": [51449, 492, 434, 11983, 4225, 13, 51484], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 71474, "start": 737.2, "end": 737.44, "text": " Sure.", "tokens": [51488, 4894, 13, 51500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 71474, "start": 737.54, "end": 738.48, "text": " When does it get weird?", "tokens": [51505, 1133, 775, 309, 483, 3657, 30, 51552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 71474, "start": 739.3, "end": 742.88, "text": " The whole premise of this deep dive was about quantum mechanics and complex numbers.", "tokens": [51593, 440, 1379, 22045, 295, 341, 2452, 9192, 390, 466, 13018, 12939, 293, 3997, 3547, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15609443187713623, "compression_ratio": 1.5384615384615385, "no_speech_prob": 1.7555645522374097e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 74288, "start": 742.88, "end": 748.28, "text": " Why can't we just build the universe out of these regular classical real number of probabilities?", "tokens": [50365, 1545, 393, 380, 321, 445, 1322, 264, 6445, 484, 295, 613, 3890, 13735, 957, 1230, 295, 33783, 30, 50635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.173373776390439, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.3990265109592448e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 74288, "start": 748.68, "end": 750.7, "text": " The author asks that exact same question.", "tokens": [50655, 440, 3793, 8962, 300, 1900, 912, 1168, 13, 50756], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.173373776390439, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.3990265109592448e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 74288, "start": 751.16, "end": 755.92, "text": " And to answer it, we have to look at how we lift these bare classical probabilities into", "tokens": [50779, 400, 281, 1867, 309, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 577, 321, 5533, 613, 6949, 13735, 33783, 666, 51017], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.173373776390439, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.3990265109592448e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 74288, "start": 755.92, "end": 757.12, "text": " something more fundamental.", "tokens": [51017, 746, 544, 8088, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.173373776390439, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.3990265109592448e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 74288, "start": 757.52, "end": 757.8, "text": " Lift them.", "tokens": [51097, 26148, 552, 13, 51111], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.173373776390439, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.3990265109592448e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 74288, "start": 757.96, "end": 758.32, "text": " How do you mean?", "tokens": [51119, 1012, 360, 291, 914, 30, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.173373776390439, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.3990265109592448e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 74288, "start": 758.84, "end": 762.2, "text": " Well, in quantum mechanics, probabilities don't just exist on their own.", "tokens": [51163, 1042, 11, 294, 13018, 12939, 11, 33783, 500, 380, 445, 2514, 322, 641, 1065, 13, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.173373776390439, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.3990265109592448e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 74288, "start": 762.46, "end": 764.82, "text": " They are the squares of underlying amplitudes.", "tokens": [51344, 814, 366, 264, 19368, 295, 14217, 9731, 16451, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.173373776390439, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.3990265109592448e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 74288, "start": 765.18, "end": 766.22, "text": " Ah, amplitudes.", "tokens": [51480, 2438, 11, 9731, 16451, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.173373776390439, "compression_ratio": 1.6342412451361867, "no_speech_prob": 1.3990265109592448e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 76622, "start": 766.22, "end": 766.78, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50393], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 76622, "start": 767.2, "end": 772.36, "text": " The text defines a transition matrix built out of these amplitudes as a unistochastic", "tokens": [50414, 440, 2487, 23122, 257, 6034, 8141, 3094, 484, 295, 613, 9731, 16451, 382, 257, 517, 468, 8997, 2750, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 76622, "start": 772.36, "end": 775.24, "text": " matrix, which is basically built from a unitary matrix.", "tokens": [50672, 8141, 11, 597, 307, 1936, 3094, 490, 257, 517, 4109, 8141, 13, 50816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 76622, "start": 775.64, "end": 780.34, "text": " And unitary matrices are where complex numbers, the imaginary eye, where they live.", "tokens": [50836, 400, 517, 4109, 32284, 366, 689, 3997, 3547, 11, 264, 26164, 3313, 11, 689, 436, 1621, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 76622, "start": 780.4200000000001, "end": 780.6, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51075, 1033, 13, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 76622, "start": 780.7, "end": 785.48, "text": " So a unistochastic matrix relies on the complex math we currently use in standard physics.", "tokens": [51089, 407, 257, 517, 468, 8997, 2750, 8141, 30910, 322, 264, 3997, 5221, 321, 4362, 764, 294, 3832, 10649, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 76622, "start": 785.7, "end": 786.02, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51339, 1079, 13, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 76622, "start": 786.6600000000001, "end": 790.82, "text": " The alternative, if we want to completely banish imaginary numbers and just use real numbers,", "tokens": [51387, 440, 8535, 11, 498, 321, 528, 281, 2584, 5643, 742, 26164, 3547, 293, 445, 764, 957, 3547, 11, 51595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 76622, "start": 790.82, "end": 793.22, "text": " is to build an orthostochastic matrix.", "tokens": [51595, 307, 281, 1322, 364, 19052, 555, 8997, 2750, 8141, 13, 51715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 76622, "start": 793.62, "end": 794.1800000000001, "text": " Orthostochastic.", "tokens": [51735, 27554, 555, 8997, 2750, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15276148938757228, "compression_ratio": 1.8615384615384616, "no_speech_prob": 1.4262261077008231e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 79418, "start": 794.18, "end": 796.8399999999999, "text": " Which is built purely out of real numbers, real amplitudes.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 3094, 17491, 484, 295, 957, 3547, 11, 957, 9731, 16451, 13, 50498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09684272110462189, "compression_ratio": 1.6763754045307444, "no_speech_prob": 1.2250342884198573e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 79418, "start": 797.16, "end": 801.4799999999999, "text": " So the entire fate of the universe basically boils down to this one question.", "tokens": [50514, 407, 264, 2302, 12738, 295, 264, 6445, 1936, 35049, 760, 281, 341, 472, 1168, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09684272110462189, "compression_ratio": 1.6763754045307444, "no_speech_prob": 1.2250342884198573e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 79418, "start": 802.04, "end": 807.0799999999999, "text": " Can every single unistochastic matrix be flawlessly reproduced by an orthostochastic one?", "tokens": [50758, 1664, 633, 2167, 517, 468, 8997, 2750, 8141, 312, 13717, 12048, 11408, 1232, 538, 364, 19052, 555, 8997, 2750, 472, 30, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09684272110462189, "compression_ratio": 1.6763754045307444, "no_speech_prob": 1.2250342884198573e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 79418, "start": 807.2399999999999, "end": 810.9399999999999, "text": " Meaning, can real numbers do absolutely everything complex numbers can do?", "tokens": [51018, 19948, 11, 393, 957, 3547, 360, 3122, 1203, 3997, 3547, 393, 360, 30, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09684272110462189, "compression_ratio": 1.6763754045307444, "no_speech_prob": 1.2250342884198573e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 79418, "start": 811.1999999999999, "end": 811.7199999999999, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51216, 7587, 13, 51242], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09684272110462189, "compression_ratio": 1.6763754045307444, "no_speech_prob": 1.2250342884198573e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 79418, "start": 812.12, "end": 815.8199999999999, "text": " Well, based on the fact that we use complex numbers to run our computers, I'm going to", "tokens": [51262, 1042, 11, 2361, 322, 264, 1186, 300, 321, 764, 3997, 3547, 281, 1190, 527, 10807, 11, 286, 478, 516, 281, 51447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09684272110462189, "compression_ratio": 1.6763754045307444, "no_speech_prob": 1.2250342884198573e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 79418, "start": 815.8199999999999, "end": 817.3199999999999, "text": " guess the answer is a hard no.", "tokens": [51447, 2041, 264, 1867, 307, 257, 1152, 572, 13, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09684272110462189, "compression_ratio": 1.6763754045307444, "no_speech_prob": 1.2250342884198573e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 79418, "start": 817.3199999999999, "end": 822.54, "text": " It's actually a bit of a mathematical trap, because if your system only has two possible", "tokens": [51522, 467, 311, 767, 257, 857, 295, 257, 18894, 11487, 11, 570, 498, 428, 1185, 787, 575, 732, 1944, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09684272110462189, "compression_ratio": 1.6763754045307444, "no_speech_prob": 1.2250342884198573e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 82254, "start": 822.54, "end": 826.0999999999999, "text": " outcomes, what physicists call n equals two, the answer is yes.", "tokens": [50365, 10070, 11, 437, 48716, 818, 297, 6915, 732, 11, 264, 1867, 307, 2086, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 82254, "start": 826.2199999999999, "end": 826.86, "text": " Wait, really?", "tokens": [50549, 3802, 11, 534, 30, 50581], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 82254, "start": 826.92, "end": 827.14, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50584, 865, 13, 50595], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 82254, "start": 827.4, "end": 830.48, "text": " At n equals two, the math shows a perfect degeneracy.", "tokens": [50608, 1711, 297, 6915, 732, 11, 264, 5221, 3110, 257, 2176, 40520, 2551, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 82254, "start": 830.9599999999999, "end": 832.74, "text": " Real numbers work flawlessly.", "tokens": [50786, 8467, 3547, 589, 13717, 12048, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 82254, "start": 833.24, "end": 834.66, "text": " So just a simple coin flip.", "tokens": [50900, 407, 445, 257, 2199, 11464, 7929, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 82254, "start": 835.28, "end": 835.9, "text": " Heads or tails?", "tokens": [51002, 634, 5834, 420, 28537, 30, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 82254, "start": 836.14, "end": 836.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51045, 1779, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 82254, "start": 836.68, "end": 842.3399999999999, "text": " If you observe a single two-outcome system, a single coin flip, you cannot tell whether the", "tokens": [51072, 759, 291, 11441, 257, 2167, 732, 12, 346, 1102, 1185, 11, 257, 2167, 11464, 7929, 11, 291, 2644, 980, 1968, 264, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 82254, "start": 842.3399999999999, "end": 845.7199999999999, "text": " underlying reality is running on real numbers or complex numbers.", "tokens": [51355, 14217, 4103, 307, 2614, 322, 957, 3547, 420, 3997, 3547, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19883761896151247, "compression_ratio": 1.606837606837607, "no_speech_prob": 1.5794567259988512e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 84572, "start": 845.72, "end": 848.4, "text": " The math overlaps perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5221, 15986, 2382, 6239, 13, 50499], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 84572, "start": 848.7, "end": 849.0400000000001, "text": " Oh, wow.", "tokens": [50514, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 50531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 84572, "start": 849.1600000000001, "end": 855.14, "text": " So if the universe only consisted of simple yes or no binary particles, real numbers would", "tokens": [50537, 407, 498, 264, 6445, 787, 38227, 295, 2199, 2086, 420, 572, 17434, 10007, 11, 957, 3547, 576, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 84572, "start": 855.14, "end": 856.12, "text": " be totally sufficient.", "tokens": [50836, 312, 3879, 11563, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 84572, "start": 856.26, "end": 857.9200000000001, "text": " We wouldn't need imaginary math at all.", "tokens": [50892, 492, 2759, 380, 643, 26164, 5221, 412, 439, 13, 50975], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 84572, "start": 858.0400000000001, "end": 858.52, "text": " That's right.", "tokens": [50981, 663, 311, 558, 13, 51005], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 84572, "start": 859.0600000000001, "end": 864.5, "text": " But the moment you add a third outcome at n equals three, like a three-sided die or a", "tokens": [51032, 583, 264, 1623, 291, 909, 257, 2636, 9700, 412, 297, 6915, 1045, 11, 411, 257, 1045, 12, 30941, 978, 420, 257, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 84572, "start": 864.5, "end": 867.6, "text": " particle that can spin up, down, or sideways, everything breaks.", "tokens": [51304, 12359, 300, 393, 6060, 493, 11, 760, 11, 420, 26092, 11, 1203, 9857, 13, 51459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 84572, "start": 867.7, "end": 868.64, "text": " Everything breaks at three.", "tokens": [51464, 5471, 9857, 412, 1045, 13, 51511], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 84572, "start": 868.72, "end": 869.34, "text": " How does it break?", "tokens": [51515, 1012, 775, 309, 1821, 30, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 84572, "start": 869.46, "end": 870.0, "text": " Walk me through it.", "tokens": [51552, 10818, 385, 807, 309, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 84572, "start": 870.12, "end": 873.1800000000001, "text": " The author provides a devastatingly simple counterexample.", "tokens": [51585, 440, 3793, 6417, 257, 21280, 356, 2199, 1207, 323, 87, 335, 781, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12681632651422256, "compression_ratio": 1.6066666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735387168605564e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 87318, "start": 873.18, "end": 877.26, "text": " It's called the discrete Fourier transform matrix, or DFT.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 1219, 264, 27706, 36810, 4088, 8141, 11, 420, 413, 25469, 13, 50569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 87318, "start": 877.62, "end": 878.68, "text": " Okay, a Fourier transform.", "tokens": [50587, 1033, 11, 257, 36810, 4088, 13, 50640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 87318, "start": 878.8199999999999, "end": 880.3199999999999, "text": " I know that's used in audio engineering, right?", "tokens": [50647, 286, 458, 300, 311, 1143, 294, 6278, 7043, 11, 558, 30, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 87318, "start": 880.4, "end": 882.8399999999999, "text": " Like to break down sound waves into different frequencies.", "tokens": [50726, 1743, 281, 1821, 760, 1626, 9417, 666, 819, 20250, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 87318, "start": 883.0, "end": 883.14, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50856, 1079, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 87318, "start": 883.2199999999999, "end": 886.3599999999999, "text": " It's a very standard, highly symmetric mathematical operation.", "tokens": [50867, 467, 311, 257, 588, 3832, 11, 5405, 32330, 18894, 6916, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 87318, "start": 886.7199999999999, "end": 890.78, "text": " And in quantum mechanics, a three-by-three DFT matrix is used all the time.", "tokens": [51042, 400, 294, 13018, 12939, 11, 257, 1045, 12, 2322, 12, 27583, 413, 25469, 8141, 307, 1143, 439, 264, 565, 13, 51245], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 87318, "start": 891.14, "end": 893.5799999999999, "text": " The probabilities it generates are totally uniform.", "tokens": [51263, 440, 33783, 309, 23815, 366, 3879, 9452, 13, 51385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 87318, "start": 893.7399999999999, "end": 894.5999999999999, "text": " They're perfectly flat.", "tokens": [51393, 814, 434, 6239, 4962, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 87318, "start": 895.0799999999999, "end": 900.5999999999999, "text": " But if you try to build that exact same uniform probability transition using only real numbers,", "tokens": [51460, 583, 498, 291, 853, 281, 1322, 300, 1900, 912, 9452, 8482, 6034, 1228, 787, 957, 3547, 11, 51736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 87318, "start": 900.78, "end": 902.7199999999999, "text": " using an orthostochastic matrix.", "tokens": [51745, 1228, 364, 19052, 555, 8997, 2750, 8141, 13, 51842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 87318, "start": 902.92, "end": 903.02, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51852, 865, 13, 51857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1819252760513969, "compression_ratio": 1.6328358208955225, "no_speech_prob": 1.6228930092149207e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 90318, "start": 903.18, "end": 907.8399999999999, "text": " The math demands that you find a three-by-three matrix made entirely of positive and negative", "tokens": [50365, 440, 5221, 15107, 300, 291, 915, 257, 1045, 12, 2322, 12, 27583, 8141, 1027, 7696, 295, 3353, 293, 3671, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 90318, "start": 907.8399999999999, "end": 911.04, "text": " ones, whose rows are all perfectly perpendicular to each other.", "tokens": [50598, 2306, 11, 6104, 13241, 366, 439, 6239, 26734, 281, 1184, 661, 13, 50758], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 90318, "start": 911.14, "end": 912.38, "text": " Wait, I'm trying to visualize this.", "tokens": [50763, 3802, 11, 286, 478, 1382, 281, 23273, 341, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 90318, "start": 912.66, "end": 913.78, "text": " A three-by-three grid.", "tokens": [50839, 316, 1045, 12, 2322, 12, 27583, 10748, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 90318, "start": 914.4599999999999, "end": 915.66, "text": " Nine boxes total.", "tokens": [50929, 18939, 9002, 3217, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 90318, "start": 916.04, "end": 919.92, "text": " And the only numbers I'm allowed to put in those boxes are a positive one or a negative", "tokens": [51008, 400, 264, 787, 3547, 286, 478, 4350, 281, 829, 294, 729, 9002, 366, 257, 3353, 472, 420, 257, 3671, 51202], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 90318, "start": 919.92, "end": 920.2199999999999, "text": " one.", "tokens": [51202, 472, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 90318, "start": 920.3, "end": 920.5799999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51221, 1079, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 90318, "start": 920.5799999999999, "end": 926.5, "text": " And every row must be mathematically orthogonal, meaning perpendicular, to every other row.", "tokens": [51235, 400, 633, 5386, 1633, 312, 44003, 41488, 11, 3620, 26734, 11, 281, 633, 661, 5386, 13, 51531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 90318, "start": 926.64, "end": 927.04, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51538, 7587, 13, 51558], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1535324594248896, "compression_ratio": 1.6590038314176245, "no_speech_prob": 2.9854519464217466e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 92704, "start": 927.04, "end": 931.4, "text": " This specific structure is known in mathematics as a Hadamard matrix.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 2685, 3877, 307, 2570, 294, 18666, 382, 257, 12298, 335, 515, 8141, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21075412962171766, "compression_ratio": 0.971830985915493, "no_speech_prob": 1.5674041925484161e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 93140, "start": 931.4, "end": 932.8199999999999, "text": " And here is the punchline.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 510, 307, 264, 8135, 1889, 13, 50436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23272668747674852, "compression_ratio": 1.190909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.2804993570629817e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 93140, "start": 932.8199999999999, "end": 936.68, "text": " A three-by-three real Hadamard matrix simply does not exist.", "tokens": [50436, 316, 1045, 12, 2322, 12, 27583, 957, 12298, 335, 515, 8141, 2935, 775, 406, 2514, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23272668747674852, "compression_ratio": 1.190909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.2804993570629817e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 93140, "start": 937.18, "end": 938.84, "text": " It is a mathematical impossibility.", "tokens": [50654, 467, 307, 257, 18894, 38802, 2841, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23272668747674852, "compression_ratio": 1.190909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.2804993570629817e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 93140, "start": 939.16, "end": 939.4399999999999, "text": " Period.", "tokens": [50753, 34976, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23272668747674852, "compression_ratio": 1.190909090909091, "no_speech_prob": 2.2804993570629817e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 93944, "start": 939.44, "end": 944.32, "text": " Like, we know for a fact it doesn't exist, or we just haven't found a clever way to arrange", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 321, 458, 337, 257, 1186, 309, 1177, 380, 2514, 11, 420, 321, 445, 2378, 380, 1352, 257, 13494, 636, 281, 9424, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13272225856781006, "compression_ratio": 1.5045045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796947083757118e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 93944, "start": 944.32, "end": 945.62, "text": " the ones and negative ones yet.", "tokens": [50609, 264, 2306, 293, 3671, 2306, 1939, 13, 50674], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13272225856781006, "compression_ratio": 1.5045045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796947083757118e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 93944, "start": 945.6800000000001, "end": 945.96, "text": " Period.", "tokens": [50677, 34976, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13272225856781006, "compression_ratio": 1.5045045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796947083757118e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 93944, "start": 946.1400000000001, "end": 947.1400000000001, "text": " It's a finite problem.", "tokens": [50700, 467, 311, 257, 19362, 1154, 13, 50750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13272225856781006, "compression_ratio": 1.5045045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796947083757118e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 93944, "start": 947.2600000000001, "end": 953.5200000000001, "text": " You can literally program a computer to exhaustively check all 512 possible combinations of plus and", "tokens": [50756, 509, 393, 3736, 1461, 257, 3820, 281, 14687, 3413, 1520, 439, 1025, 4762, 1944, 21267, 295, 1804, 293, 51069], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13272225856781006, "compression_ratio": 1.5045045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796947083757118e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 93944, "start": 953.5200000000001, "end": 955.44, "text": " minus ones in a three-by-three grid.", "tokens": [51069, 3175, 2306, 294, 257, 1045, 12, 2322, 12, 27583, 10748, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13272225856781006, "compression_ratio": 1.5045045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796947083757118e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 93944, "start": 955.5200000000001, "end": 956.3000000000001, "text": " And none of them work.", "tokens": [51169, 400, 6022, 295, 552, 589, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13272225856781006, "compression_ratio": 1.5045045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796947083757118e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 93944, "start": 956.5400000000001, "end": 957.3800000000001, "text": " None of them work.", "tokens": [51220, 14492, 295, 552, 589, 13, 51262], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13272225856781006, "compression_ratio": 1.5045045045045045, "no_speech_prob": 1.5796947083757118e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 95738, "start": 957.38, "end": 961.52, "text": " They simply cannot satisfy the structural requirement to be perpendicular.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 2935, 2644, 19319, 264, 15067, 11695, 281, 312, 26734, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525289473995086, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942083165047192e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 95738, "start": 962.32, "end": 966.68, "text": " So, just to be absolutely clear on what we're proving here for the listener, for a three-outcome", "tokens": [50612, 407, 11, 445, 281, 312, 3122, 1850, 322, 437, 321, 434, 27221, 510, 337, 264, 31569, 11, 337, 257, 1045, 12, 346, 1102, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525289473995086, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942083165047192e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 95738, "start": 966.68, "end": 972.8, "text": " system, there is a specific, perfectly valid, uniform set of quantum transition probabilities.", "tokens": [50830, 1185, 11, 456, 307, 257, 2685, 11, 6239, 7363, 11, 9452, 992, 295, 13018, 6034, 33783, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525289473995086, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942083165047192e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 95738, "start": 973.04, "end": 973.4, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51148, 1079, 13, 51166], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525289473995086, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942083165047192e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 95738, "start": 973.72, "end": 978.98, "text": " But if you restrict the universe to only using real numbers, you simply do not have the geometric", "tokens": [51182, 583, 498, 291, 7694, 264, 6445, 281, 787, 1228, 957, 3547, 11, 291, 2935, 360, 406, 362, 264, 33246, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525289473995086, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942083165047192e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 95738, "start": 978.98, "end": 981.2, "text": " parts you need to build that transition.", "tokens": [51445, 3166, 291, 643, 281, 1322, 300, 6034, 13, 51556], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525289473995086, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942083165047192e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 95738, "start": 981.42, "end": 982.84, "text": " That's a great way to summarize it.", "tokens": [51567, 663, 311, 257, 869, 636, 281, 20858, 309, 13, 51638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525289473995086, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942083165047192e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 95738, "start": 982.84, "end": 987.02, "text": " It's like trying to build an equilateral triangle using two straight lines in a circle.", "tokens": [51638, 467, 311, 411, 1382, 281, 1322, 364, 1267, 37751, 13369, 1228, 732, 2997, 3876, 294, 257, 6329, 13, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11525289473995086, "compression_ratio": 1.6481481481481481, "no_speech_prob": 1.3942083165047192e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 98738, "start": 987.38, "end": 988.9399999999999, "text": " You just, you don't have the materials.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 445, 11, 291, 500, 380, 362, 264, 5319, 13, 50443], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14137206118330997, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106118175263084e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 98738, "start": 989.28, "end": 991.02, "text": " The real numbers fail the test.", "tokens": [50460, 440, 957, 3547, 3061, 264, 1500, 13, 50547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14137206118330997, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106118175263084e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 98738, "start": 991.74, "end": 997.52, "text": " Complex amplitudes become structurally necessary to realize this specific uniform matrix.", "tokens": [50583, 41184, 9731, 16451, 1813, 6594, 6512, 4818, 281, 4325, 341, 2685, 9452, 8141, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14137206118330997, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106118175263084e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 98738, "start": 997.68, "end": 1001.86, "text": " Okay, so real numbers fail on a single isolated matrix when we hit three outcomes.", "tokens": [50880, 1033, 11, 370, 957, 3547, 3061, 322, 257, 2167, 14621, 8141, 562, 321, 2045, 1045, 10070, 13, 51089], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14137206118330997, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106118175263084e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 98738, "start": 1002.74, "end": 1004.52, "text": " But that feels like a local glitch, right?", "tokens": [51133, 583, 300, 3417, 411, 257, 2654, 23552, 11, 558, 30, 51222], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14137206118330997, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106118175263084e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 98738, "start": 1004.54, "end": 1006.28, "text": " Like a specific bug in the math.", "tokens": [51223, 1743, 257, 2685, 7426, 294, 264, 5221, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14137206118330997, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106118175263084e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 98738, "start": 1006.38, "end": 1007.7, "text": " It does feel localized, yes.", "tokens": [51315, 467, 775, 841, 44574, 11, 2086, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14137206118330997, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106118175263084e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 98738, "start": 1007.84, "end": 1010.54, "text": " But we don't live in a universe of isolated single measurements.", "tokens": [51388, 583, 321, 500, 380, 1621, 294, 257, 6445, 295, 14621, 2167, 15383, 13, 51523], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14137206118330997, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106118175263084e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 98738, "start": 1011.04, "end": 1014.0, "text": " What happens when we try to stitch multiple measurements together?", "tokens": [51548, 708, 2314, 562, 321, 853, 281, 5635, 3866, 15383, 1214, 30, 51696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14137206118330997, "compression_ratio": 1.693661971830986, "no_speech_prob": 1.6106118175263084e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 101400, "start": 1014.0, "end": 1018.36, "text": " Well, if I understand the text correctly, this brings us to a whole new level of the deep", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 498, 286, 1223, 264, 2487, 8944, 11, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 257, 1379, 777, 1496, 295, 264, 2452, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 101400, "start": 1018.36, "end": 1020.14, "text": " dive, the cycle obstruction.", "tokens": [50583, 9192, 11, 264, 6586, 49711, 13, 50672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 101400, "start": 1020.5, "end": 1021.6, "text": " The cycle obstruction.", "tokens": [50690, 440, 6586, 49711, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 101400, "start": 1022.44, "end": 1023.44, "text": " That sounds ominous.", "tokens": [50787, 663, 3263, 46812, 563, 13, 50837], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 101400, "start": 1023.84, "end": 1028.58, "text": " This is where we move from a single snapshot to a sequence, a network of measurements.", "tokens": [50857, 639, 307, 689, 321, 1286, 490, 257, 2167, 30163, 281, 257, 8310, 11, 257, 3209, 295, 15383, 13, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 101400, "start": 1029.38, "end": 1032.98, "text": " Let's explore what the text calls the composition obstruction.", "tokens": [51134, 961, 311, 6839, 437, 264, 2487, 5498, 264, 12686, 49711, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 101400, "start": 1033.4, "end": 1033.66, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51335, 1033, 13, 51348], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 101400, "start": 1033.8, "end": 1039.24, "text": " When you compose classical probabilities, when you chain our paint-mixing stochastic maps together,", "tokens": [51355, 1133, 291, 35925, 13735, 33783, 11, 562, 291, 5021, 527, 4225, 12, 76, 970, 278, 342, 8997, 2750, 11317, 1214, 11, 51627], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 101400, "start": 1039.46, "end": 1041.48, "text": " you inevitably lose information.", "tokens": [51638, 291, 28171, 3624, 1589, 13, 51739], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 101400, "start": 1041.7, "end": 1042.54, "text": " We talked about that.", "tokens": [51750, 492, 2825, 466, 300, 13, 51792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16916058644527146, "compression_ratio": 1.6713780918727916, "no_speech_prob": 1.4898031809942869e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 104254, "start": 1042.54, "end": 1043.58, "text": " Right, it gets more purple.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 309, 2170, 544, 9656, 13, 50417], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 104254, "start": 1043.8999999999999, "end": 1047.24, "text": " But in quantum mechanics, we don't chain probabilities.", "tokens": [50433, 583, 294, 13018, 12939, 11, 321, 500, 380, 5021, 33783, 13, 50600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 104254, "start": 1047.6399999999999, "end": 1048.7, "text": " We chain amplitudes.", "tokens": [50620, 492, 5021, 9731, 16451, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 104254, "start": 1049.02, "end": 1050.92, "text": " And amplitudes have cross terms.", "tokens": [50689, 400, 9731, 16451, 362, 3278, 2115, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 104254, "start": 1051.3, "end": 1052.48, "text": " They allow for interference.", "tokens": [50803, 814, 2089, 337, 24497, 13, 50862], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 104254, "start": 1052.78, "end": 1053.58, "text": " Ah, interference.", "tokens": [50877, 2438, 11, 24497, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 104254, "start": 1054.1399999999999, "end": 1056.2, "text": " The classic quantum weirdness.", "tokens": [50945, 440, 7230, 13018, 3657, 1287, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 104254, "start": 1056.7, "end": 1060.28, "text": " For anyone who has seen that famous double-slit experiment video on YouTube,", "tokens": [51073, 1171, 2878, 567, 575, 1612, 300, 4618, 3834, 12, 10418, 270, 5120, 960, 322, 3088, 11, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 104254, "start": 1061.04, "end": 1065.82, "text": " this is where the waves of probability ripple out and either cancel each other out,", "tokens": [51290, 341, 307, 689, 264, 9417, 295, 8482, 40688, 484, 293, 2139, 10373, 1184, 661, 484, 11, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 104254, "start": 1066.1399999999999, "end": 1070.24, "text": " leaving a dark spot, or they amplify each other, leaving a bright spot on the wall.", "tokens": [51545, 5012, 257, 2877, 4008, 11, 420, 436, 41174, 1184, 661, 11, 5012, 257, 4730, 4008, 322, 264, 2929, 13, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 104254, "start": 1070.32, "end": 1071.44, "text": " That's the exact one.", "tokens": [51754, 663, 311, 264, 1900, 472, 13, 51810], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15829959748283265, "compression_ratio": 1.6736111111111112, "no_speech_prob": 1.1024151426800022e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 107144, "start": 1071.44, "end": 1076.66, "text": " If you compose things blindly at the classical probability level, you discard those interference", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 35925, 721, 47744, 412, 264, 13735, 8482, 1496, 11, 291, 31597, 729, 24497, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15975232124328614, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310911176055764e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 107144, "start": 1076.66, "end": 1077.4, "text": " cross terms.", "tokens": [50626, 3278, 2115, 13, 50663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15975232124328614, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310911176055764e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 107144, "start": 1077.92, "end": 1082.48, "text": " The text formally proves that probability level composition is not a homomorphism.", "tokens": [50689, 440, 2487, 25983, 25019, 300, 8482, 1496, 12686, 307, 406, 257, 3655, 32702, 1434, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15975232124328614, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310911176055764e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 107144, "start": 1082.6000000000001, "end": 1083.8600000000001, "text": " Let's translate homomorphism.", "tokens": [50923, 961, 311, 13799, 3655, 32702, 1434, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15975232124328614, "compression_ratio": 1.5, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310911176055764e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 108386, "start": 1083.86, "end": 1087.4199999999998, "text": " It just means it doesn't preserve the structural integrity of the transitions.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 445, 1355, 309, 1177, 380, 15665, 264, 15067, 16000, 295, 264, 23767, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611262939788483, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.2110265047715618e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 108386, "start": 1087.8999999999999, "end": 1092.34, "text": " It's a lossy compression, like saving an image as a low-quality JPEG.", "tokens": [50567, 467, 311, 257, 4470, 88, 19355, 11, 411, 6816, 364, 3256, 382, 257, 2295, 12, 11286, 508, 5208, 38, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611262939788483, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.2110265047715618e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 108386, "start": 1092.4199999999998, "end": 1093.26, "text": " Okay, I get that.", "tokens": [50793, 1033, 11, 286, 483, 300, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611262939788483, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.2110265047715618e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 108386, "start": 1093.4799999999998, "end": 1098.62, "text": " To keep the structure intact, to allow for that double-slit interference, you have to retain", "tokens": [50846, 1407, 1066, 264, 3877, 23493, 11, 281, 2089, 337, 300, 3834, 12, 10418, 270, 24497, 11, 291, 362, 281, 18340, 51103], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611262939788483, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.2110265047715618e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 108386, "start": 1098.62, "end": 1099.28, "text": " the amplitudes.", "tokens": [51103, 264, 9731, 16451, 13, 51136], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611262939788483, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.2110265047715618e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 108386, "start": 1099.6399999999999, "end": 1104.74, "text": " You need a coherent mathematical lift from probability back up to amplitude.", "tokens": [51154, 509, 643, 257, 36239, 18894, 5533, 490, 8482, 646, 493, 281, 27433, 13, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1611262939788483, "compression_ratio": 1.5172413793103448, "no_speech_prob": 1.2110265047715618e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 110474, "start": 1104.74, "end": 1108.22, "text": " But wait, earlier you said that real numbers can have amplitudes.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 1699, 11, 3071, 291, 848, 300, 957, 3547, 393, 362, 9731, 16451, 13, 50539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16582784759864377, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779769205372495e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 110474, "start": 1108.38, "end": 1112.0, "text": " They can be causative or negative, which means a positive one and a negative one can cancel", "tokens": [50547, 814, 393, 312, 3302, 1166, 420, 3671, 11, 597, 1355, 257, 3353, 472, 293, 257, 3671, 472, 393, 10373, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16582784759864377, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779769205372495e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 110474, "start": 1112.0, "end": 1112.54, "text": " each other out.", "tokens": [50728, 1184, 661, 484, 13, 50755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16582784759864377, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779769205372495e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 110474, "start": 1112.92, "end": 1113.96, "text": " That is interference.", "tokens": [50774, 663, 307, 24497, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16582784759864377, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779769205372495e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 110474, "start": 1114.36, "end": 1114.88, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50846, 467, 307, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16582784759864377, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779769205372495e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 110474, "start": 1114.94, "end": 1118.96, "text": " So does this composition obstruction actually rule out real numbers?", "tokens": [50875, 407, 775, 341, 12686, 49711, 767, 4978, 484, 957, 3547, 30, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16582784759864377, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779769205372495e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 110474, "start": 1119.16, "end": 1119.42, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51086, 865, 13, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16582784759864377, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779769205372495e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 110474, "start": 1119.6, "end": 1120.92, "text": " Because they can do interference.", "tokens": [51108, 1436, 436, 393, 360, 24497, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16582784759864377, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779769205372495e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 110474, "start": 1121.08, "end": 1122.46, "text": " That is a vital clarification.", "tokens": [51182, 663, 307, 257, 11707, 34449, 13, 51251], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16582784759864377, "compression_ratio": 1.6363636363636365, "no_speech_prob": 1.4779769205372495e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 112246, "start": 1122.46, "end": 1128.16, "text": " And the Assumption Ledger points it out explicitly, real numbers can handle interference perfectly", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 6281, 449, 1695, 39367, 1321, 2793, 309, 484, 20803, 11, 957, 3547, 393, 4813, 24497, 6239, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 112246, "start": 1128.16, "end": 1128.56, "text": " well.", "tokens": [50650, 731, 13, 50670], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 112246, "start": 1128.72, "end": 1128.94, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50678, 1033, 13, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 112246, "start": 1129.16, "end": 1134.6000000000001, "text": " To truly break real numbers at the network level, we need something more complex than", "tokens": [50700, 1407, 4908, 1821, 957, 3547, 412, 264, 3209, 1496, 11, 321, 643, 746, 544, 3997, 813, 50972], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 112246, "start": 1134.6000000000001, "end": 1136.46, "text": " just a linear sequence of measurements.", "tokens": [50972, 445, 257, 8213, 8310, 295, 15383, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 112246, "start": 1136.82, "end": 1138.3400000000001, "text": " We need a closed loop.", "tokens": [51083, 492, 643, 257, 5395, 6367, 13, 51159], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 112246, "start": 1138.54, "end": 1141.1200000000001, "text": " We need to introduce context graphs.", "tokens": [51169, 492, 643, 281, 5366, 4319, 24877, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 112246, "start": 1141.56, "end": 1142.1000000000001, "text": " Context graphs.", "tokens": [51320, 4839, 3828, 24877, 13, 51347], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 112246, "start": 1142.42, "end": 1144.5, "text": " Okay, let's try to paint a mental picture for the listener.", "tokens": [51363, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 853, 281, 4225, 257, 4973, 3036, 337, 264, 31569, 13, 51467], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 112246, "start": 1145.28, "end": 1149.5, "text": " Imagine a graph like a web of dots connected by lines on a whiteboard.", "tokens": [51506, 11739, 257, 4295, 411, 257, 3670, 295, 15026, 4582, 538, 3876, 322, 257, 2418, 3787, 13, 51717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 112246, "start": 1149.64, "end": 1150.96, "text": " A standard network graph, yeah.", "tokens": [51724, 316, 3832, 3209, 4295, 11, 1338, 13, 51790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17900449861355913, "compression_ratio": 1.643598615916955, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682303325202263e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 115096, "start": 1150.96, "end": 1154.88, "text": " In this case, every dot, every vertex is a measurement context.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 341, 1389, 11, 633, 5893, 11, 633, 28162, 307, 257, 13160, 4319, 13, 50561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 115096, "start": 1155.08, "end": 1155.64, "text": " Let's define that.", "tokens": [50571, 961, 311, 6964, 300, 13, 50599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 115096, "start": 1156.14, "end": 1160.3400000000001, "text": " A measurement context is essentially a specific setup of your laboratory apparatus.", "tokens": [50624, 316, 13160, 4319, 307, 4476, 257, 2685, 8657, 295, 428, 16523, 38573, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 115096, "start": 1160.7, "end": 1163.44, "text": " It's a specific question you are asking the universe.", "tokens": [50852, 467, 311, 257, 2685, 1168, 291, 366, 3365, 264, 6445, 13, 50989], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 115096, "start": 1163.68, "end": 1164.24, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51001, 48746, 736, 13, 51029], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 115096, "start": 1164.5, "end": 1168.92, "text": " And the lines connecting the dots are the transitions between those setups.", "tokens": [51042, 400, 264, 3876, 11015, 264, 15026, 366, 264, 23767, 1296, 729, 46832, 13, 51263], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 115096, "start": 1168.94, "end": 1169.14, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51264, 1779, 13, 51274], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 115096, "start": 1169.4, "end": 1169.6200000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51287, 1033, 13, 51298], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 115096, "start": 1169.8600000000001, "end": 1172.08, "text": " Now, imagine your graph has no loops.", "tokens": [51310, 823, 11, 3811, 428, 4295, 575, 572, 16121, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 115096, "start": 1172.4, "end": 1173.6000000000001, "text": " It's just a branching tree.", "tokens": [51437, 467, 311, 445, 257, 9819, 278, 4230, 13, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 115096, "start": 1174.0, "end": 1179.98, "text": " You start at one dot and you can follow lines outwards to other dots, but no path ever circles", "tokens": [51517, 509, 722, 412, 472, 5893, 293, 291, 393, 1524, 3876, 484, 2015, 281, 661, 15026, 11, 457, 572, 3100, 1562, 13040, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 115096, "start": 1179.98, "end": 1180.82, "text": " back on itself.", "tokens": [51816, 646, 322, 2564, 13, 51858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16945772904616135, "compression_ratio": 1.679054054054054, "no_speech_prob": 1.211205398130022e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 118096, "start": 1180.96, "end": 1181.8600000000001, "text": " Like a family tree.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 257, 1605, 4230, 13, 50410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 118096, "start": 1182.04, "end": 1182.3600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50419, 1779, 13, 50435], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 118096, "start": 1182.7, "end": 1185.6000000000001, "text": " If your graph is a tree, there are no independent constraints.", "tokens": [50452, 759, 428, 4295, 307, 257, 4230, 11, 456, 366, 572, 6695, 18491, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 118096, "start": 1185.8, "end": 1192.68, "text": " You can always assign a perfectly consistent set of real number frames to every single", "tokens": [50607, 509, 393, 1009, 6269, 257, 6239, 8398, 992, 295, 957, 1230, 12083, 281, 633, 2167, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 118096, "start": 1192.68, "end": 1193.8600000000001, "text": " measurement context.", "tokens": [50951, 13160, 4319, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 118096, "start": 1194.1000000000001, "end": 1196.06, "text": " Because you never have to reconcile with where you started.", "tokens": [51022, 1436, 291, 1128, 362, 281, 41059, 365, 689, 291, 1409, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 118096, "start": 1196.32, "end": 1196.8, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51133, 7587, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 118096, "start": 1197.04, "end": 1201.42, "text": " You just pick a starting point, assign it a real number frame, and walk along the branches", "tokens": [51169, 509, 445, 1888, 257, 2891, 935, 11, 6269, 309, 257, 957, 1230, 3920, 11, 293, 1792, 2051, 264, 14770, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 118096, "start": 1201.42, "end": 1202.9, "text": " updating your math as you go.", "tokens": [51388, 25113, 428, 5221, 382, 291, 352, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 118096, "start": 1202.98, "end": 1205.94, "text": " Because there are no loops, you never contradict yourself.", "tokens": [51466, 1436, 456, 366, 572, 16121, 11, 291, 1128, 28900, 1803, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 118096, "start": 1206.06, "end": 1208.18, "text": " Because you never run into your own past.", "tokens": [51620, 1436, 291, 1128, 1190, 666, 428, 1065, 1791, 13, 51726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16102760882417033, "compression_ratio": 1.7491039426523298, "no_speech_prob": 1.3303686494450795e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 120818, "start": 1208.18, "end": 1210.18, "text": " You're always moving into new territory.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 434, 1009, 2684, 666, 777, 11360, 13, 50465], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14055884830535403, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 120818, "start": 1210.64, "end": 1213.3600000000001, "text": " But a cycle changes the rules of the game completely.", "tokens": [50488, 583, 257, 6586, 2962, 264, 4474, 295, 264, 1216, 2584, 13, 50624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14055884830535403, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 120818, "start": 1213.96, "end": 1219.28, "text": " A cycle means you can start at context A, transition to context B, transition to context", "tokens": [50654, 316, 6586, 1355, 291, 393, 722, 412, 4319, 316, 11, 6034, 281, 4319, 363, 11, 6034, 281, 4319, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14055884830535403, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 120818, "start": 1219.28, "end": 1221.92, "text": " C, and then transition back to context A.", "tokens": [50920, 383, 11, 293, 550, 6034, 646, 281, 4319, 316, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14055884830535403, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 120818, "start": 1222.0600000000002, "end": 1222.8600000000001, "text": " A closed loop.", "tokens": [51059, 316, 5395, 6367, 13, 51099], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14055884830535403, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881592694931169e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 122286, "start": 1222.86, "end": 1226.28, "text": " And when you arrive back at A, the math is entirely unforgiving.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 562, 291, 8881, 646, 412, 316, 11, 264, 5221, 307, 7696, 31411, 15441, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14518349591423482, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555071116058917e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 122286, "start": 1226.4399999999998, "end": 1227.76, "text": " You must have cycle consistency.", "tokens": [50544, 509, 1633, 362, 6586, 14416, 13, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14518349591423482, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555071116058917e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 122286, "start": 1227.9199999999998, "end": 1229.4599999999998, "text": " You must be exactly where you started.", "tokens": [50618, 509, 1633, 312, 2293, 689, 291, 1409, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14518349591423482, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555071116058917e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 122286, "start": 1229.9399999999998, "end": 1231.1399999999999, "text": " It sounds like a Penrose staircase.", "tokens": [50719, 467, 3263, 411, 257, 10571, 37841, 35359, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14518349591423482, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555071116058917e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 122286, "start": 1231.84, "end": 1238.26, "text": " Or one of those mind-bending M.C. Escher drawings of the monks walking up the stairs in", "tokens": [50814, 1610, 472, 295, 729, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 376, 13, 34, 13, 2313, 6759, 18618, 295, 264, 32201, 4494, 493, 264, 13471, 294, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14518349591423482, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555071116058917e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 122286, "start": 1238.26, "end": 1238.6399999999999, "text": " a square.", "tokens": [51135, 257, 3732, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14518349591423482, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555071116058917e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 122286, "start": 1238.8999999999999, "end": 1240.26, "text": " That is the perfect analogy.", "tokens": [51167, 663, 307, 264, 2176, 21663, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14518349591423482, "compression_ratio": 1.4375, "no_speech_prob": 1.6555071116058917e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 124026, "start": 1240.26, "end": 1245.1, "text": " If you just look at one individual step in the drawing, or one straight edge of a triangle,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 445, 574, 412, 472, 2609, 1823, 294, 264, 6316, 11, 420, 472, 2997, 4691, 295, 257, 13369, 11, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13195673357538817, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355757472188756e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 124026, "start": 1245.42, "end": 1246.92, "text": " it looks totally flat and normal.", "tokens": [50623, 309, 1542, 3879, 4962, 293, 2710, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13195673357538817, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355757472188756e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 124026, "start": 1247.08, "end": 1248.54, "text": " It obeys all the rules of perspective.", "tokens": [50706, 467, 36346, 749, 439, 264, 4474, 295, 4585, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13195673357538817, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355757472188756e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 124026, "start": 1248.96, "end": 1254.84, "text": " But when your eye follows the steps all the way around and completes the loop, your brain", "tokens": [50800, 583, 562, 428, 3313, 10002, 264, 4439, 439, 264, 636, 926, 293, 36362, 264, 6367, 11, 428, 3567, 51094], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13195673357538817, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355757472188756e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 124026, "start": 1254.84, "end": 1255.24, "text": " breaks.", "tokens": [51094, 9857, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13195673357538817, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355757472188756e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 124026, "start": 1255.3799999999999, "end": 1258.32, "text": " Because you find yourself somehow walking upside down on the ceiling.", "tokens": [51121, 1436, 291, 915, 1803, 6063, 4494, 14119, 760, 322, 264, 13655, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13195673357538817, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355757472188756e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 124026, "start": 1258.78, "end": 1262.66, "text": " The Escher staircase is a mathematically exact analogy for what happens here.", "tokens": [51291, 440, 2313, 6759, 35359, 307, 257, 44003, 1900, 21663, 337, 437, 2314, 510, 13, 51485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13195673357538817, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355757472188756e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 124026, "start": 1263.04, "end": 1265.9, "text": " The text proves something called the triangle gluing theorem.", "tokens": [51504, 440, 2487, 25019, 746, 1219, 264, 13369, 1563, 9635, 20904, 13, 51647], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13195673357538817, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355757472188756e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 124026, "start": 1266.04, "end": 1267.54, "text": " The triangle gluing theorem.", "tokens": [51654, 440, 13369, 1563, 9635, 20904, 13, 51729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13195673357538817, "compression_ratio": 1.7040816326530612, "no_speech_prob": 1.3355757472188756e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 126754, "start": 1267.54, "end": 1268.6, "text": " Okay, break that down.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 1821, 300, 760, 13, 50418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 126754, "start": 1268.8, "end": 1271.28, "text": " Let's look at two-dimensional system, D equals 2.", "tokens": [50428, 961, 311, 574, 412, 732, 12, 18759, 1185, 11, 413, 6915, 568, 13, 50552], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 126754, "start": 1271.72, "end": 1274.68, "text": " Remember how D equals 2 was perfectly safe for single matrices?", "tokens": [50574, 5459, 577, 413, 6915, 568, 390, 6239, 3273, 337, 2167, 32284, 30, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 126754, "start": 1275.04, "end": 1276.8799999999999, "text": " We couldn't tell real from complex.", "tokens": [50740, 492, 2809, 380, 980, 957, 490, 3997, 13, 50832], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 126754, "start": 1277.3999999999999, "end": 1277.6599999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50858, 1779, 13, 50871], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 126754, "start": 1277.78, "end": 1278.6599999999999, "text": " The coin flip was safe.", "tokens": [50877, 440, 11464, 7929, 390, 3273, 13, 50921], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 126754, "start": 1278.76, "end": 1280.46, "text": " We said real numbers were fine for that.", "tokens": [50926, 492, 848, 957, 3547, 645, 2489, 337, 300, 13, 51011], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 126754, "start": 1280.72, "end": 1285.2, "text": " Well, let's arrange three D equals 2 measurement contexts into a triangle loop.", "tokens": [51024, 1042, 11, 718, 311, 9424, 1045, 413, 6915, 568, 13160, 30628, 666, 257, 13369, 6367, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 126754, "start": 1285.74, "end": 1291.0, "text": " Specifically, we use three mutually unbiased bases, or MUBs.", "tokens": [51275, 26058, 11, 321, 764, 1045, 39144, 517, 5614, 1937, 17949, 11, 420, 17935, 33, 82, 13, 51538], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 126754, "start": 1291.06, "end": 1292.3799999999999, "text": " Mutually unbiased bases.", "tokens": [51541, 18517, 671, 517, 5614, 1937, 17949, 13, 51607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 126754, "start": 1292.5, "end": 1293.28, "text": " I've heard this term.", "tokens": [51613, 286, 600, 2198, 341, 1433, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 126754, "start": 1293.44, "end": 1296.08, "text": " This is tied to Heisenberg's uncertainty principle, right?", "tokens": [51660, 639, 307, 9601, 281, 634, 11106, 6873, 311, 15697, 8665, 11, 558, 30, 51792], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 126754, "start": 1296.1, "end": 1296.6599999999999, "text": " It is, yeah.", "tokens": [51793, 467, 307, 11, 1338, 13, 51821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15749601766365726, "compression_ratio": 1.605095541401274, "no_speech_prob": 1.8834241891779735e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 129666, "start": 1296.66, "end": 1303.68, "text": " Meaning, if you are absolutely certain about your particle's state in context A, say, you", "tokens": [50365, 19948, 11, 498, 291, 366, 3122, 1629, 466, 428, 12359, 311, 1785, 294, 4319, 316, 11, 584, 11, 291, 50716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 129666, "start": 1303.68, "end": 1309.5600000000002, "text": " know its exact position, you are maximally uncertain about its state in context B, which", "tokens": [50716, 458, 1080, 1900, 2535, 11, 291, 366, 5138, 379, 11308, 466, 1080, 1785, 294, 4319, 363, 11, 597, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 129666, "start": 1309.5600000000002, "end": 1310.6000000000001, "text": " might be its momentum.", "tokens": [51010, 1062, 312, 1080, 11244, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 129666, "start": 1310.92, "end": 1311.2, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51078, 1779, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 129666, "start": 1311.3000000000002, "end": 1313.28, "text": " The two contexts are mutually unbiased.", "tokens": [51097, 440, 732, 30628, 366, 39144, 517, 5614, 1937, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 129666, "start": 1313.3400000000001, "end": 1313.46, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51199, 1779, 13, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 129666, "start": 1313.46, "end": 1314.7, "text": " They don't share any certainty.", "tokens": [51205, 814, 500, 380, 2073, 604, 27022, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 129666, "start": 1314.9, "end": 1315.3600000000001, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51277, 7587, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 129666, "start": 1315.98, "end": 1319.5600000000002, "text": " And in a two-dimensional system, you can have three of these contexts.", "tokens": [51331, 400, 294, 257, 732, 12, 18759, 1185, 11, 291, 393, 362, 1045, 295, 613, 30628, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 129666, "start": 1319.8600000000001, "end": 1323.8000000000002, "text": " Think of measuring a particle's spin along the x, y, and z axes.", "tokens": [51525, 6557, 295, 13389, 257, 12359, 311, 6060, 2051, 264, 2031, 11, 288, 11, 293, 710, 35387, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 129666, "start": 1323.98, "end": 1324.8400000000001, "text": " Okay, x, y, and z.", "tokens": [51731, 1033, 11, 2031, 11, 288, 11, 293, 710, 13, 51774], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12799585782564604, "compression_ratio": 1.748062015503876, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130255989065367e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 132484, "start": 1324.84, "end": 1328.4399999999998, "text": " If you form a triangle out of these three contexts, the real numbers shatter.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 1254, 257, 13369, 484, 295, 613, 1045, 30628, 11, 264, 957, 3547, 402, 1161, 13, 50545], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14276401563124222, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551221977510356e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 132484, "start": 1328.6599999999999, "end": 1328.8799999999999, "text": " Why?", "tokens": [50556, 1545, 30, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14276401563124222, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551221977510356e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 132484, "start": 1329.1999999999998, "end": 1331.1399999999999, "text": " Why do they shatter if the individual parts are fine?", "tokens": [50583, 1545, 360, 436, 402, 1161, 498, 264, 2609, 3166, 366, 2489, 30, 50680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14276401563124222, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551221977510356e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 132484, "start": 1331.28, "end": 1335.1799999999998, "text": " Because each edge of the triangle works perfectly fine in real numbers on its own.", "tokens": [50687, 1436, 1184, 4691, 295, 264, 13369, 1985, 6239, 2489, 294, 957, 3547, 322, 1080, 1065, 13, 50882], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14276401563124222, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551221977510356e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 132484, "start": 1335.58, "end": 1337.74, "text": " It's what the author calls edgewise admissible.", "tokens": [50902, 467, 311, 437, 264, 3793, 5498, 4691, 3711, 5910, 41073, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14276401563124222, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551221977510356e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 132484, "start": 1338.02, "end": 1340.54, "text": " Just like looking at one step on the Escher staircase.", "tokens": [51024, 1449, 411, 1237, 412, 472, 1823, 322, 264, 2313, 6759, 35359, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14276401563124222, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551221977510356e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 132484, "start": 1340.9399999999998, "end": 1341.4599999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51170, 7587, 13, 51196], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14276401563124222, "compression_ratio": 1.5395348837209302, "no_speech_prob": 1.7551221977510356e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 134146, "start": 1341.46, "end": 1347.66, "text": " But if you try to globally glue all three edges together to complete the triangle, the real", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 291, 853, 281, 18958, 8998, 439, 1045, 8819, 1214, 281, 3566, 264, 13369, 11, 264, 957, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12703824493120303, "compression_ratio": 1.6891385767790261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359704389790064e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 134146, "start": 1347.66, "end": 1350.04, "text": " number math spits out a contradiction.", "tokens": [50675, 1230, 5221, 637, 1208, 484, 257, 34937, 13, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12703824493120303, "compression_ratio": 1.6891385767790261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359704389790064e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 134146, "start": 1350.48, "end": 1351.38, "text": " What kind of contradiction?", "tokens": [50816, 708, 733, 295, 34937, 30, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12703824493120303, "compression_ratio": 1.6891385767790261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359704389790064e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 134146, "start": 1351.88, "end": 1356.8600000000001, "text": " It essentially demands that a geometric angle equals itself plus a 90-degree twist.", "tokens": [50886, 467, 4476, 15107, 300, 257, 33246, 5802, 6915, 2564, 1804, 257, 4289, 12, 34368, 8203, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12703824493120303, "compression_ratio": 1.6891385767790261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359704389790064e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 134146, "start": 1357.4, "end": 1358.8, "text": " It's a literal paradox.", "tokens": [51162, 467, 311, 257, 20411, 26221, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12703824493120303, "compression_ratio": 1.6891385767790261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359704389790064e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 134146, "start": 1359.3400000000001, "end": 1362.88, "text": " The real numbers cannot glue the triangle together without snapping.", "tokens": [51259, 440, 957, 3547, 2644, 8998, 264, 13369, 1214, 1553, 42727, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12703824493120303, "compression_ratio": 1.6891385767790261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359704389790064e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 134146, "start": 1363.14, "end": 1365.8, "text": " So the Escher staircase actually breaks the universe.", "tokens": [51449, 407, 264, 2313, 6759, 35359, 767, 9857, 264, 6445, 13, 51582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12703824493120303, "compression_ratio": 1.6891385767790261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359704389790064e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 134146, "start": 1366.3600000000001, "end": 1369.72, "text": " If reality runs on real numbers, you can't walk the triangle.", "tokens": [51610, 759, 4103, 6676, 322, 957, 3547, 11, 291, 393, 380, 1792, 264, 13369, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12703824493120303, "compression_ratio": 1.6891385767790261, "no_speech_prob": 1.6359704389790064e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 136972, "start": 1369.72, "end": 1370.32, "text": " You cannot.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 2644, 13, 50395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 136972, "start": 1370.88, "end": 1375.34, "text": " And the author goes a step further to provide a sharp density result at the end of this chapter.", "tokens": [50423, 400, 264, 3793, 1709, 257, 1823, 3052, 281, 2893, 257, 8199, 10305, 1874, 412, 264, 917, 295, 341, 7187, 13, 50646], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 136972, "start": 1375.44, "end": 1376.72, "text": " What's a sharp density result?", "tokens": [50651, 708, 311, 257, 8199, 10305, 1874, 30, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 136972, "start": 1376.84, "end": 1383.1200000000001, "text": " Well, you might be listening to this and thinking, okay, so this one, very specific, highly symmetric", "tokens": [50721, 1042, 11, 291, 1062, 312, 4764, 281, 341, 293, 1953, 11, 1392, 11, 370, 341, 472, 11, 588, 2685, 11, 5405, 32330, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 136972, "start": 1383.1200000000001, "end": 1385.18, "text": " MUB triangle fails.", "tokens": [51035, 17935, 33, 13369, 18199, 13, 51138], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 136972, "start": 1385.3600000000001, "end": 1386.38, "text": " But that's a special case.", "tokens": [51147, 583, 300, 311, 257, 2121, 1389, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 136972, "start": 1386.72, "end": 1389.18, "text": " Surely most random triangles you could draw are fine.", "tokens": [51215, 29803, 881, 4974, 29896, 291, 727, 2642, 366, 2489, 13, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 136972, "start": 1389.28, "end": 1390.66, "text": " Yeah, that's exactly what I was thinking.", "tokens": [51343, 865, 11, 300, 311, 2293, 437, 286, 390, 1953, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 136972, "start": 1390.76, "end": 1396.02, "text": " What if I just arbitrarily pick three random contexts that aren't perfectly mutually unbiased?", "tokens": [51417, 708, 498, 286, 445, 19071, 3289, 1888, 1045, 4974, 30628, 300, 3212, 380, 6239, 39144, 517, 5614, 1937, 30, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 136972, "start": 1396.5, "end": 1398.32, "text": " What if the triangle is just a little lopsided?", "tokens": [51704, 708, 498, 264, 13369, 307, 445, 257, 707, 287, 3370, 2112, 30, 51795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12103893809074903, "compression_ratio": 1.7055016181229774, "no_speech_prob": 1.7011236169706123e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 139832, "start": 1398.32, "end": 1401.06, "text": " The author proves that this failure isn't a rare exception.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 25019, 300, 341, 7763, 1943, 380, 257, 5892, 11183, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 139832, "start": 1401.54, "end": 1403.1, "text": " It is the inescapable rule.", "tokens": [50526, 467, 307, 264, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 4978, 13, 50604], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 139832, "start": 1403.5, "end": 1410.4399999999998, "text": " The moment a graph has even one single cycle, even one loop, no matter how lopsided, the", "tokens": [50624, 440, 1623, 257, 4295, 575, 754, 472, 2167, 6586, 11, 754, 472, 6367, 11, 572, 1871, 577, 287, 3370, 2112, 11, 264, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 139832, "start": 1410.4399999999998, "end": 1416.02, "text": " probability of finding a globally valid real number realization drops to exactly zero.", "tokens": [50971, 8482, 295, 5006, 257, 18958, 7363, 957, 1230, 25138, 11438, 281, 2293, 4018, 13, 51250], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 139832, "start": 1416.36, "end": 1417.5, "text": " Wait, zero?", "tokens": [51267, 3802, 11, 4018, 30, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 139832, "start": 1417.8999999999999, "end": 1419.3799999999999, "text": " Like literally zero probability?", "tokens": [51344, 1743, 3736, 4018, 8482, 30, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 139832, "start": 1419.58, "end": 1420.1799999999998, "text": " Exactly zero.", "tokens": [51428, 7587, 4018, 13, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 139832, "start": 1420.3, "end": 1422.34, "text": " It is perfectly exactly zero.", "tokens": [51464, 467, 307, 6239, 2293, 4018, 13, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 139832, "start": 1422.5, "end": 1424.8799999999999, "text": " In mathematics, we call it a measure zero set.", "tokens": [51574, 682, 18666, 11, 321, 818, 309, 257, 3481, 4018, 992, 13, 51693], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 139832, "start": 1425.0, "end": 1426.02, "text": " So it's not just unlikely.", "tokens": [51699, 407, 309, 311, 406, 445, 17518, 13, 51750], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14485186701235564, "compression_ratio": 1.6259541984732824, "no_speech_prob": 1.8393455161747063e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 142602, "start": 1426.02, "end": 1428.26, "text": " No, it's not an asymptotic threshold.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 11, 309, 311, 406, 364, 35114, 9411, 14678, 13, 50477], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 142602, "start": 1428.42, "end": 1431.8799999999999, "text": " It's not that it just gets progressively harder to find real numbers as you add more", "tokens": [50485, 467, 311, 406, 300, 309, 445, 2170, 46667, 6081, 281, 915, 957, 3547, 382, 291, 909, 544, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 142602, "start": 1431.8799999999999, "end": 1432.18, "text": " edges.", "tokens": [50658, 8819, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 142602, "start": 1432.74, "end": 1436.92, "text": " The continuous measure of valid real number solutions collapses entirely.", "tokens": [50701, 440, 10957, 3481, 295, 7363, 957, 1230, 6547, 48765, 7696, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 142602, "start": 1437.12, "end": 1438.02, "text": " Give me a visual for that.", "tokens": [50920, 5303, 385, 257, 5056, 337, 300, 13, 50965], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 142602, "start": 1438.32, "end": 1439.32, "text": " Think of a dartboard.", "tokens": [50980, 6557, 295, 257, 39010, 3787, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 142602, "start": 1439.7, "end": 1442.98, "text": " Every point on the dartboard represents a complex number solution.", "tokens": [51049, 2048, 935, 322, 264, 39010, 3787, 8855, 257, 3997, 1230, 3827, 13, 51213], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 142602, "start": 1443.22, "end": 1443.48, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51225, 1033, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 142602, "start": 1443.72, "end": 1448.84, "text": " The valid real number solutions are represented by a single, infinitely thin line drawn across", "tokens": [51250, 440, 7363, 957, 1230, 6547, 366, 10379, 538, 257, 2167, 11, 36227, 5862, 1622, 10117, 2108, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 142602, "start": 1448.84, "end": 1449.3, "text": " the board.", "tokens": [51506, 264, 3150, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 142602, "start": 1449.78, "end": 1454.8799999999999, "text": " If you throw a dart blindly, what is the probability you hit a line with zero width?", "tokens": [51553, 759, 291, 3507, 257, 39010, 47744, 11, 437, 307, 264, 8482, 291, 2045, 257, 1622, 365, 4018, 11402, 30, 51808], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13422890596611556, "compression_ratio": 1.7373737373737375, "no_speech_prob": 1.3302484114241508e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 145488, "start": 1454.88, "end": 1455.5600000000002, "text": " It's zero.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 4018, 13, 50399], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 145488, "start": 1455.8000000000002, "end": 1457.44, "text": " You will always, always miss.", "tokens": [50411, 509, 486, 1009, 11, 1009, 1713, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 145488, "start": 1458.0600000000002, "end": 1460.0800000000002, "text": " Realizability is not the rule for real numbers.", "tokens": [50524, 8467, 590, 2310, 307, 406, 264, 4978, 337, 957, 3547, 13, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 145488, "start": 1460.22, "end": 1461.5600000000002, "text": " It is a measure zero exception.", "tokens": [50632, 467, 307, 257, 3481, 4018, 11183, 13, 50699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 145488, "start": 1462.1200000000001, "end": 1465.46, "text": " The geometry fundamentally resists real numbers once you close a loop.", "tokens": [50727, 440, 18426, 17879, 725, 1751, 957, 3547, 1564, 291, 1998, 257, 6367, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 145488, "start": 1465.64, "end": 1465.8600000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50903, 1033, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 145488, "start": 1465.96, "end": 1469.8400000000001, "text": " My mind is slightly melting right now, but in the best way possible.", "tokens": [50919, 1222, 1575, 307, 4748, 20493, 558, 586, 11, 457, 294, 264, 1151, 636, 1944, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 145488, "start": 1470.0800000000002, "end": 1475.24, "text": " So single systems can't form closed loops in real numbers because the geometry literally", "tokens": [51125, 407, 2167, 3652, 393, 380, 1254, 5395, 16121, 294, 957, 3547, 570, 264, 18426, 3736, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 145488, "start": 1475.24, "end": 1476.1200000000001, "text": " contradicts itself.", "tokens": [51383, 28900, 82, 2564, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 145488, "start": 1476.22, "end": 1477.1000000000001, "text": " The stairs don't connect.", "tokens": [51432, 440, 13471, 500, 380, 1745, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 145488, "start": 1477.22, "end": 1477.3600000000001, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51482, 1779, 13, 51489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 145488, "start": 1477.6000000000001, "end": 1480.8600000000001, "text": " But what happens if we look at two distinct systems interacting with each other?", "tokens": [51501, 583, 437, 2314, 498, 321, 574, 412, 732, 10644, 3652, 18017, 365, 1184, 661, 30, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 145488, "start": 1481.5600000000002, "end": 1483.6200000000001, "text": " We've talked about a single particle moving through a network.", "tokens": [51699, 492, 600, 2825, 466, 257, 2167, 12359, 2684, 807, 257, 3209, 13, 51802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14045241876696865, "compression_ratio": 1.6477611940298507, "no_speech_prob": 1.0358459966511302e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 148362, "start": 1483.62, "end": 1484.9799999999998, "text": " What about a network of particles?", "tokens": [50365, 708, 466, 257, 3209, 295, 10007, 30, 50433], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2294329358385755, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682374882545647e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 148362, "start": 1485.2399999999998, "end": 1490.5, "text": " Ah, this brings us to a huge pillar of the text, system composition.", "tokens": [50446, 2438, 11, 341, 5607, 505, 281, 257, 2603, 27592, 295, 264, 2487, 11, 1185, 12686, 13, 50709], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2294329358385755, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682374882545647e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 148362, "start": 1490.8999999999999, "end": 1491.78, "text": " System composition.", "tokens": [50729, 8910, 12686, 13, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2294329358385755, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682374882545647e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 148362, "start": 1491.9399999999998, "end": 1495.1599999999999, "text": " This is where the physics gets incredibly tangible.", "tokens": [50781, 639, 307, 689, 264, 10649, 2170, 6252, 27094, 13, 50942], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2294329358385755, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682374882545647e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 148362, "start": 1495.84, "end": 1501.1399999999999, "text": " We are testing the scalar fields, meaning testing real numbers versus complex numbers,", "tokens": [50976, 492, 366, 4997, 264, 39684, 7909, 11, 3620, 4997, 957, 3547, 5717, 3997, 3547, 11, 51241], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2294329358385755, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682374882545647e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 148362, "start": 1501.4599999999998, "end": 1503.9799999999998, "text": " against the concept of operational independence.", "tokens": [51257, 1970, 264, 3410, 295, 16607, 14640, 13, 51383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2294329358385755, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682374882545647e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 148362, "start": 1504.2199999999998, "end": 1505.2199999999998, "text": " Operational independence.", "tokens": [51395, 12480, 1478, 14640, 13, 51445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2294329358385755, "compression_ratio": 1.6600985221674878, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682374882545647e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 150522, "start": 1505.22, "end": 1509.52, "text": " If I have a quantum system sitting on a desk here in my lab, and you have a system sitting", "tokens": [50365, 759, 286, 362, 257, 13018, 1185, 3798, 322, 257, 10026, 510, 294, 452, 2715, 11, 293, 291, 362, 257, 1185, 3798, 50580], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11886684629652235, "compression_ratio": 1.6729857819905214, "no_speech_prob": 2.271279301788165e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 150522, "start": 1509.52, "end": 1514.52, "text": " on a desk in your lab, and we bring them together, how does the math handle that combination?", "tokens": [50580, 322, 257, 10026, 294, 428, 2715, 11, 293, 321, 1565, 552, 1214, 11, 577, 775, 264, 5221, 4813, 300, 6562, 30, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11886684629652235, "compression_ratio": 1.6729857819905214, "no_speech_prob": 2.271279301788165e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 150522, "start": 1515.38, "end": 1519.48, "text": " To test this, the text relies on an assumption called local tomography.", "tokens": [50873, 1407, 1500, 341, 11, 264, 2487, 30910, 322, 364, 15302, 1219, 2654, 2916, 5820, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11886684629652235, "compression_ratio": 1.6729857819905214, "no_speech_prob": 2.271279301788165e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 150522, "start": 1520.04, "end": 1521.32, "text": " I need you to translate that for me.", "tokens": [51106, 286, 643, 291, 281, 13799, 300, 337, 385, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11886684629652235, "compression_ratio": 1.6729857819905214, "no_speech_prob": 2.271279301788165e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 150522, "start": 1521.68, "end": 1525.08, "text": " What does local tomography mean in plain, everyday English?", "tokens": [51188, 708, 775, 2654, 2916, 5820, 914, 294, 11121, 11, 7429, 3669, 30, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11886684629652235, "compression_ratio": 1.6729857819905214, "no_speech_prob": 2.271279301788165e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 152508, "start": 1525.08, "end": 1531.54, "text": " Local tomography is the assumption that a joint state, the combined ultimate reality of both", "tokens": [50365, 22755, 2916, 5820, 307, 264, 15302, 300, 257, 7225, 1785, 11, 264, 9354, 9705, 4103, 295, 1293, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09032535552978516, "compression_ratio": 1.4113475177304964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147395699537715e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 152508, "start": 1531.54, "end": 1537.96, "text": " our systems together, is exactly as informative as a complete set of local measurements on", "tokens": [50688, 527, 3652, 1214, 11, 307, 2293, 382, 27759, 382, 257, 3566, 992, 295, 2654, 15383, 322, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09032535552978516, "compression_ratio": 1.4113475177304964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147395699537715e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 152508, "start": 1537.96, "end": 1538.96, "text": " each subsystem.", "tokens": [51009, 1184, 2090, 9321, 13, 51059], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09032535552978516, "compression_ratio": 1.4113475177304964, "no_speech_prob": 1.7147395699537715e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 153896, "start": 1538.96, "end": 1540.18, "text": " Okay, let me think through that.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 385, 519, 807, 300, 13, 50426], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1321145561006334, "compression_ratio": 1.6830601092896176, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191891798368995e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 153896, "start": 1540.54, "end": 1545.68, "text": " Meaning, if I measure absolutely everything possible of my system on my desk, and you", "tokens": [50444, 19948, 11, 498, 286, 3481, 3122, 1203, 1944, 295, 452, 1185, 322, 452, 10026, 11, 293, 291, 50701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1321145561006334, "compression_ratio": 1.6830601092896176, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191891798368995e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 153896, "start": 1545.68, "end": 1549.32, "text": " measure absolutely everything possible about your system on your desk, and then we call", "tokens": [50701, 3481, 3122, 1203, 1944, 466, 428, 1185, 322, 428, 10026, 11, 293, 550, 321, 818, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1321145561006334, "compression_ratio": 1.6830601092896176, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191891798368995e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 153896, "start": 1549.32, "end": 1555.5, "text": " each other and compare our notes, we should completely, 100% understand the combined system.", "tokens": [50883, 1184, 661, 293, 6794, 527, 5570, 11, 321, 820, 2584, 11, 2319, 4, 1223, 264, 9354, 1185, 13, 51192], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1321145561006334, "compression_ratio": 1.6830601092896176, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191891798368995e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 153896, "start": 1555.66, "end": 1556.14, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51200, 7587, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1321145561006334, "compression_ratio": 1.6830601092896176, "no_speech_prob": 1.5191891798368995e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 155614, "start": 1556.14, "end": 1561.72, "text": " There shouldn't be any spooky, hidden variables or secret data that we can only see if we", "tokens": [50365, 821, 4659, 380, 312, 604, 30510, 11, 7633, 9102, 420, 4054, 1412, 300, 321, 393, 787, 536, 498, 321, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 155614, "start": 1561.72, "end": 1566.2800000000002, "text": " plug both systems into a giant, room-sized machine simultaneously.", "tokens": [50644, 5452, 1293, 3652, 666, 257, 7410, 11, 1808, 12, 20614, 3479, 16561, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 155614, "start": 1566.5200000000002, "end": 1566.72, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50884, 1779, 13, 50894], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 155614, "start": 1566.9, "end": 1570.46, "text": " The whole is exactly equal to the sum of its locally measurable parts.", "tokens": [50903, 440, 1379, 307, 2293, 2681, 281, 264, 2408, 295, 1080, 16143, 43615, 3166, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 155614, "start": 1570.5800000000002, "end": 1571.42, "text": " You've got it perfectly.", "tokens": [51087, 509, 600, 658, 309, 6239, 13, 51129], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 155614, "start": 1571.5600000000002, "end": 1573.16, "text": " It's a deeply intuitive assumption.", "tokens": [51136, 467, 311, 257, 8760, 21769, 15302, 13, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 155614, "start": 1573.44, "end": 1575.2, "text": " We expect the universe to behave this way.", "tokens": [51230, 492, 2066, 264, 6445, 281, 15158, 341, 636, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 155614, "start": 1575.3200000000002, "end": 1575.5400000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51324, 1779, 13, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 155614, "start": 1575.8400000000001, "end": 1580.7800000000002, "text": " To test if our math obeys this assumption, the author uses a dimension counting argument,", "tokens": [51350, 1407, 1500, 498, 527, 5221, 36346, 749, 341, 15302, 11, 264, 3793, 4960, 257, 10139, 13251, 6770, 11, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 155614, "start": 1581.3200000000002, "end": 1583.9, "text": " originally developed by physicists Araki and Hardy.", "tokens": [51624, 7993, 4743, 538, 48716, 18601, 2984, 293, 43930, 13, 51753], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 155614, "start": 1584.26, "end": 1584.96, "text": " Dimension counting.", "tokens": [51771, 20975, 3378, 13251, 13, 51806], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 155614, "start": 1584.96, "end": 1585.94, "text": " That sounds straightforward.", "tokens": [51806, 663, 3263, 15325, 13, 51855], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15530139749700372, "compression_ratio": 1.6, "no_speech_prob": 1.5014845920410802e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 158614, "start": 1586.14, "end": 1587.8000000000002, "text": " The premise is incredibly simple.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 22045, 307, 6252, 2199, 13, 50448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 158614, "start": 1588.2, "end": 1592.6200000000001, "text": " We literally just count the number of parameters, the mathematical dials, or degrees of freedom", "tokens": [50468, 492, 3736, 445, 1207, 264, 1230, 295, 9834, 11, 264, 18894, 5502, 82, 11, 420, 5310, 295, 5645, 50689], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 158614, "start": 1592.6200000000001, "end": 1594.5800000000002, "text": " required to describe the systems.", "tokens": [50689, 4739, 281, 6786, 264, 3652, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 158614, "start": 1594.96, "end": 1596.0400000000002, "text": " Okay, I want to do this math.", "tokens": [50806, 1033, 11, 286, 528, 281, 360, 341, 5221, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 158614, "start": 1596.1000000000001, "end": 1597.22, "text": " I want to walk through this slowly.", "tokens": [50863, 286, 528, 281, 1792, 807, 341, 5692, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 158614, "start": 1597.44, "end": 1597.6000000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50930, 865, 13, 50938], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 158614, "start": 1597.8200000000002, "end": 1599.8600000000001, "text": " Let's say we have two standard quantum systems.", "tokens": [50949, 961, 311, 584, 321, 362, 732, 3832, 13018, 3652, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 158614, "start": 1600.5400000000002, "end": 1605.2800000000002, "text": " For complex numbers, the math we currently use to build our semiconductors, how does the", "tokens": [51085, 1171, 3997, 3547, 11, 264, 5221, 321, 4362, 764, 281, 1322, 527, 36924, 5547, 11, 577, 775, 264, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 158614, "start": 1605.2800000000002, "end": 1606.64, "text": " dimension counting work out?", "tokens": [51322, 10139, 13251, 589, 484, 30, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 158614, "start": 1607.0800000000002, "end": 1610.22, "text": " Let's start with a standard two-level system, a single quibit.", "tokens": [51412, 961, 311, 722, 365, 257, 3832, 732, 12, 12418, 1185, 11, 257, 2167, 421, 897, 270, 13, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 158614, "start": 1610.44, "end": 1616.1000000000001, "text": " To mathematically describe a quibit in complex numbers, you use a 2x2 Hermitian matrix.", "tokens": [51580, 1407, 44003, 6786, 257, 421, 897, 270, 294, 3997, 3547, 11, 291, 764, 257, 568, 87, 17, 21842, 270, 952, 8141, 13, 51863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16046241919199625, "compression_ratio": 1.719626168224299, "no_speech_prob": 1.7078020855126885e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 161614, "start": 1616.14, "end": 1617.64, "text": " Wait, Hermitian matrix?", "tokens": [50365, 3802, 11, 21842, 270, 952, 8141, 30, 50440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1723656803369522, "compression_ratio": 1.5125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034036720557256e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 161614, "start": 1617.8400000000001, "end": 1619.68, "text": " Let's define that so we don't lose anyone.", "tokens": [50450, 961, 311, 6964, 300, 370, 321, 500, 380, 3624, 2878, 13, 50542], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1723656803369522, "compression_ratio": 1.5125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034036720557256e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 161614, "start": 1619.88, "end": 1624.74, "text": " A Hermitian matrix is a specific grid of numbers where the diagonal values are purely", "tokens": [50552, 316, 21842, 270, 952, 8141, 307, 257, 2685, 10748, 295, 3547, 689, 264, 21539, 4190, 366, 17491, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1723656803369522, "compression_ratio": 1.5125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034036720557256e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 161614, "start": 1624.74, "end": 1629.1200000000001, "text": " real numbers and the numbers across the diagonal are complex mirrors of each other.", "tokens": [50795, 957, 3547, 293, 264, 3547, 2108, 264, 21539, 366, 3997, 24238, 295, 1184, 661, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1723656803369522, "compression_ratio": 1.5125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034036720557256e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 161614, "start": 1629.3000000000002, "end": 1629.6200000000001, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51023, 1033, 13, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1723656803369522, "compression_ratio": 1.5125, "no_speech_prob": 1.8034036720557256e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 162962, "start": 1629.62, "end": 1634.9399999999998, "text": " In physics, we require observables to be Hermitian because it guarantees that when you measure", "tokens": [50365, 682, 10649, 11, 321, 3651, 9951, 2965, 281, 312, 21842, 270, 952, 570, 309, 32567, 300, 562, 291, 3481, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14241745471954345, "compression_ratio": 1.3103448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830273731807452e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 162962, "start": 1634.9399999999998, "end": 1638.0, "text": " the system, the answer, the eigenvalue, is a real number.", "tokens": [50631, 264, 1185, 11, 264, 1867, 11, 264, 10446, 29155, 11, 307, 257, 957, 1230, 13, 50784], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14241745471954345, "compression_ratio": 1.3103448275862069, "no_speech_prob": 1.3830273731807452e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 163800, "start": 1638.0, "end": 1643.9, "text": " Because if you measure the weight of a particle, you want the scale to say 3 grams, not 3 plus", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 498, 291, 3481, 264, 3364, 295, 257, 12359, 11, 291, 528, 264, 4373, 281, 584, 805, 11899, 11, 406, 805, 1804, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 163800, "start": 1643.9, "end": 1644.7, "text": " 2 igrams.", "tokens": [50660, 568, 8508, 2356, 82, 13, 50700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 163800, "start": 1645.1, "end": 1646.78, "text": " You want a real physical answer.", "tokens": [50720, 509, 528, 257, 957, 4001, 1867, 13, 50804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 163800, "start": 1647.1, "end": 1647.5, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50820, 7587, 13, 50840], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 163800, "start": 1647.66, "end": 1653.68, "text": " So to write out this 2x2 complex Hermitian matrix for a single quibit, how many separate", "tokens": [50848, 407, 281, 2464, 484, 341, 568, 87, 17, 3997, 21842, 270, 952, 8141, 337, 257, 2167, 421, 897, 270, 11, 577, 867, 4994, 51149], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 163800, "start": 1653.68, "end": 1656.48, "text": " dials or real parameters do I need to adjust?", "tokens": [51149, 5502, 82, 420, 957, 9834, 360, 286, 643, 281, 4369, 30, 51289], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 163800, "start": 1656.78, "end": 1657.22, "text": " I don't know.", "tokens": [51304, 286, 500, 380, 458, 13, 51326], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 163800, "start": 1657.26, "end": 1657.68, "text": " You tell me.", "tokens": [51328, 509, 980, 385, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 163800, "start": 1657.74, "end": 1660.78, "text": " You need exactly four real parameters to fully define it.", "tokens": [51352, 509, 643, 2293, 1451, 957, 9834, 281, 4498, 6964, 309, 13, 51504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 163800, "start": 1660.82, "end": 1662.18, "text": " Okay, four parameters for my quibit.", "tokens": [51506, 1033, 11, 1451, 9834, 337, 452, 421, 897, 270, 13, 51574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 163800, "start": 1662.26, "end": 1664.94, "text": " You have a quibit on your desk, so that's four parameters for your quibit.", "tokens": [51578, 509, 362, 257, 421, 897, 270, 322, 428, 10026, 11, 370, 300, 311, 1451, 9834, 337, 428, 421, 897, 270, 13, 51712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1263618206155711, "compression_ratio": 1.7132616487455197, "no_speech_prob": 1.9203961337810327e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 166494, "start": 1664.94, "end": 1665.26, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 166494, "start": 1665.78, "end": 1671.1000000000001, "text": " Now, if we combine them into a two-quibit joint system, the combined system operates", "tokens": [50407, 823, 11, 498, 321, 10432, 552, 666, 257, 732, 12, 358, 897, 270, 7225, 1185, 11, 264, 9354, 1185, 22577, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 166494, "start": 1671.1000000000001, "end": 1673.22, "text": " in a larger four-dimensional space.", "tokens": [50673, 294, 257, 4833, 1451, 12, 18759, 1901, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 166494, "start": 1673.3600000000001, "end": 1673.56, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50786, 1033, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 166494, "start": 1673.78, "end": 1679.1000000000001, "text": " A 4x4 complex Hermitian matrix requires exactly 16 real parameters.", "tokens": [50807, 316, 1017, 87, 19, 3997, 21842, 270, 952, 8141, 7029, 2293, 3165, 957, 9834, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 166494, "start": 1679.24, "end": 1680.0, "text": " Let me check the notes here.", "tokens": [51080, 961, 385, 1520, 264, 5570, 510, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 166494, "start": 1680.1200000000001, "end": 1681.28, "text": " Four parameters for my desk.", "tokens": [51124, 7451, 9834, 337, 452, 10026, 13, 51182], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 166494, "start": 1681.54, "end": 1682.56, "text": " Four parameters from your desk.", "tokens": [51195, 7451, 9834, 490, 428, 10026, 13, 51246], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 166494, "start": 1682.66, "end": 1683.72, "text": " Four times four is 16.", "tokens": [51251, 7451, 1413, 1451, 307, 3165, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 166494, "start": 1684.38, "end": 1688.6200000000001, "text": " So our local notes give us 16 dials, and the joint reality requires 16 dials.", "tokens": [51337, 407, 527, 2654, 5570, 976, 505, 3165, 5502, 82, 11, 293, 264, 7225, 4103, 7029, 3165, 5502, 82, 13, 51549], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 166494, "start": 1688.66, "end": 1690.14, "text": " The dimensions match perfectly.", "tokens": [51551, 440, 12819, 2995, 6239, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 166494, "start": 1690.8, "end": 1693.98, "text": " Complex numbers pass the local tomography test flawlessly.", "tokens": [51658, 41184, 3547, 1320, 264, 2654, 2916, 5820, 1500, 13717, 12048, 13, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15572712833720043, "compression_ratio": 1.6829268292682926, "no_speech_prob": 1.5430905251495597e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 169398, "start": 1693.98, "end": 1698.38, "text": " The joint system contains exactly the amount of information you'd expect from combining", "tokens": [50365, 440, 7225, 1185, 8306, 2293, 264, 2372, 295, 1589, 291, 1116, 2066, 490, 21928, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 169398, "start": 1698.38, "end": 1699.54, "text": " the two local systems.", "tokens": [50585, 264, 732, 2654, 3652, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 169398, "start": 1699.78, "end": 1701.06, "text": " No more, no less.", "tokens": [50655, 883, 544, 11, 572, 1570, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 169398, "start": 1701.24, "end": 1701.4, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50728, 1033, 13, 50736], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 169398, "start": 1701.96, "end": 1702.64, "text": " The math works.", "tokens": [50764, 440, 5221, 1985, 13, 50798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 169398, "start": 1702.74, "end": 1703.14, "text": " It's safe.", "tokens": [50803, 467, 311, 3273, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 169398, "start": 1703.98, "end": 1708.24, "text": " But this deep dive is about what happens if we force the universe to run on real numbers.", "tokens": [50865, 583, 341, 2452, 9192, 307, 466, 437, 2314, 498, 321, 3464, 264, 6445, 281, 1190, 322, 957, 3547, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 169398, "start": 1708.6200000000001, "end": 1709.98, "text": " Let's do the count for real numbers.", "tokens": [51097, 961, 311, 360, 264, 1207, 337, 957, 3547, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 169398, "start": 1710.24, "end": 1716.64, "text": " If we restrict ourselves to real numbers, a two-level system is described by a 2x2 real", "tokens": [51178, 759, 321, 7694, 4175, 281, 957, 3547, 11, 257, 732, 12, 12418, 1185, 307, 7619, 538, 257, 568, 87, 17, 957, 51498], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 169398, "start": 1716.64, "end": 1717.6200000000001, "text": " symmetric matrix.", "tokens": [51498, 32330, 8141, 13, 51547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 169398, "start": 1718.14, "end": 1723.02, "text": " Because we've removed the complex numbers, this matrix only requires three parameters to fully", "tokens": [51573, 1436, 321, 600, 7261, 264, 3997, 3547, 11, 341, 8141, 787, 7029, 1045, 9834, 281, 4498, 51817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 169398, "start": 1723.02, "end": 1723.44, "text": " describe.", "tokens": [51817, 6786, 13, 51838], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14036089773396498, "compression_ratio": 1.674496644295302, "no_speech_prob": 2.2980365440433692e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 172344, "start": 1723.44, "end": 1725.4, "text": " Okay, three for me, three for you.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 1045, 337, 385, 11, 1045, 337, 291, 13, 50463], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 172344, "start": 1725.88, "end": 1730.0800000000002, "text": " If I use the same multiplication rule, three times three is nine.", "tokens": [50487, 759, 286, 764, 264, 912, 27290, 4978, 11, 1045, 1413, 1045, 307, 4949, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 172344, "start": 1730.3, "end": 1733.18, "text": " So our combined local notes give us nine parameters of information.", "tokens": [50708, 407, 527, 9354, 2654, 5570, 976, 505, 4949, 9834, 295, 1589, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 172344, "start": 1733.42, "end": 1734.5800000000002, "text": " Now let's look at the joint space.", "tokens": [50864, 823, 718, 311, 574, 412, 264, 7225, 1901, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 172344, "start": 1734.8, "end": 1741.0800000000002, "text": " A 4x4 real symmetric matrix, which describes the combined joint reality of the two real quibits,", "tokens": [50933, 316, 1017, 87, 19, 957, 32330, 8141, 11, 597, 15626, 264, 9354, 7225, 4103, 295, 264, 732, 957, 421, 897, 1208, 11, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 172344, "start": 1741.38, "end": 1742.5800000000002, "text": " requires ten parameters.", "tokens": [51262, 7029, 2064, 9834, 13, 51322], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 172344, "start": 1742.78, "end": 1743.3200000000002, "text": " Wait, hang on.", "tokens": [51332, 3802, 11, 3967, 322, 13, 51359], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 172344, "start": 1743.4, "end": 1743.6200000000001, "text": " Ten.", "tokens": [51363, 9380, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 172344, "start": 1744.0, "end": 1746.3, "text": " But our local notes only multiplied out to nine.", "tokens": [51393, 583, 527, 2654, 5570, 787, 17207, 484, 281, 4949, 13, 51508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 172344, "start": 1746.3600000000001, "end": 1746.64, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51511, 1079, 13, 51525], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15876752989632742, "compression_ratio": 1.6625, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682252367700157e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 174664, "start": 1746.64, "end": 1751.5200000000002, "text": " We have nine parameters of data on our notepads, but the actual joint reality sitting in front", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 4949, 9834, 295, 1412, 322, 527, 406, 595, 5834, 11, 457, 264, 3539, 7225, 4103, 3798, 294, 1868, 50609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.03883254528045654, "compression_ratio": 1.175, "no_speech_prob": 1.1691856250523047e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 175152, "start": 1751.52, "end": 1754.46, "text": " of us requires ten dials to fully describe it.", "tokens": [50365, 295, 505, 7029, 2064, 5502, 82, 281, 4498, 6786, 309, 13, 50512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15695253440311976, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.3506970064983137e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 175152, "start": 1755.16, "end": 1756.16, "text": " We are missing a dial.", "tokens": [50547, 492, 366, 5361, 257, 5502, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15695253440311976, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.3506970064983137e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 175152, "start": 1756.26, "end": 1758.16, "text": " We are missing an entire dimension of reality.", "tokens": [50602, 492, 366, 5361, 364, 2302, 10139, 295, 4103, 13, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15695253440311976, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.3506970064983137e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 175152, "start": 1758.3799999999999, "end": 1761.9, "text": " For real numbers, the composite system has more dimensions than the local parts can account", "tokens": [50708, 1171, 957, 3547, 11, 264, 25557, 1185, 575, 544, 12819, 813, 264, 2654, 3166, 393, 2696, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15695253440311976, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.3506970064983137e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 175152, "start": 1761.9, "end": 1762.16, "text": " for.", "tokens": [50884, 337, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15695253440311976, "compression_ratio": 1.5106382978723405, "no_speech_prob": 1.3506970064983137e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 176216, "start": 1762.16, "end": 1767.0600000000002, "text": " There is a tenth parameter that is completely fundamentally invisible to any local measurement", "tokens": [50365, 821, 307, 257, 27269, 13075, 300, 307, 2584, 17879, 14603, 281, 604, 2654, 13160, 50610], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23313539999502678, "compression_ratio": 1.2178217821782178, "no_speech_prob": 1.992708081877126e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 176216, "start": 1767.0600000000002, "end": 1768.3200000000002, "text": " you or I could ever perform.", "tokens": [50610, 291, 420, 286, 727, 1562, 2042, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.23313539999502678, "compression_ratio": 1.2178217821782178, "no_speech_prob": 1.992708081877126e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 176832, "start": 1768.32, "end": 1770.06, "text": " That is deeply unsettling.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 8760, 43964, 1688, 13, 50452], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17040675810013695, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310980564994803e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 176832, "start": 1770.46, "end": 1771.58, "text": " What if we go the other direction?", "tokens": [50472, 708, 498, 321, 352, 264, 661, 3513, 30, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17040675810013695, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310980564994803e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 176832, "start": 1771.8999999999999, "end": 1773.24, "text": " What if we use quaternions?", "tokens": [50544, 708, 498, 321, 764, 421, 771, 77, 626, 30, 50611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17040675810013695, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310980564994803e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 176832, "start": 1773.6, "end": 1775.58, "text": " Those are the 4D hypercomplex numbers, right?", "tokens": [50629, 3950, 366, 264, 1017, 35, 9848, 1112, 18945, 3547, 11, 558, 30, 50728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17040675810013695, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310980564994803e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 176832, "start": 1775.96, "end": 1776.32, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50747, 1079, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17040675810013695, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310980564994803e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 176832, "start": 1776.62, "end": 1778.72, "text": " Quaternions add more imaginary axes.", "tokens": [50780, 2326, 771, 77, 626, 909, 544, 26164, 35387, 13, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17040675810013695, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310980564994803e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 176832, "start": 1779.52, "end": 1783.7, "text": " But if you do the dimension counting for quaternions, the local dimensions overcount.", "tokens": [50925, 583, 498, 291, 360, 264, 10139, 13251, 337, 421, 771, 77, 626, 11, 264, 2654, 12819, 670, 26050, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17040675810013695, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310980564994803e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 176832, "start": 1783.84, "end": 1784.22, "text": " Oh, really?", "tokens": [51141, 876, 11, 534, 30, 51160], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17040675810013695, "compression_ratio": 1.5277777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310980564994803e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 178422, "start": 1784.42, "end": 1788.0, "text": " The composite system actually has fewer dimensions than the local parts suggest.", "tokens": [50375, 440, 25557, 1185, 767, 575, 13366, 12819, 813, 264, 2654, 3166, 3402, 13, 50554], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 178422, "start": 1788.4, "end": 1789.5, "text": " It's overdetermined.", "tokens": [50574, 467, 311, 670, 49136, 2001, 13, 50629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 178422, "start": 1789.6200000000001, "end": 1793.38, "text": " You end up with phantom data that doesn't correspond to the joint reality.", "tokens": [50635, 509, 917, 493, 365, 903, 25796, 1412, 300, 1177, 380, 6805, 281, 264, 7225, 4103, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 178422, "start": 1793.64, "end": 1797.78, "text": " So complex numbers are like the unique Goldilocks field where the dimensions match exactly.", "tokens": [50836, 407, 3997, 3547, 366, 411, 264, 3845, 6731, 388, 35507, 2519, 689, 264, 12819, 2995, 2293, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 178422, "start": 1797.9, "end": 1798.38, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51049, 7587, 13, 51073], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 178422, "start": 1798.52, "end": 1799.1200000000001, "text": " Not too many.", "tokens": [51080, 1726, 886, 867, 13, 51110], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 178422, "start": 1799.32, "end": 1799.92, "text": " Not too few.", "tokens": [51120, 1726, 886, 1326, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 178422, "start": 1800.3600000000001, "end": 1805.64, "text": " So going back to the real numbers, we have this missing invisible tenth dimension.", "tokens": [51172, 407, 516, 646, 281, 264, 957, 3547, 11, 321, 362, 341, 5361, 14603, 27269, 10139, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 178422, "start": 1805.92, "end": 1807.16, "text": " What hides inside it?", "tokens": [51450, 708, 35953, 1854, 309, 30, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 178422, "start": 1807.32, "end": 1809.64, "text": " What is that missing parameter actually made of?", "tokens": [51520, 708, 307, 300, 5361, 13075, 767, 1027, 295, 30, 51636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 178422, "start": 1810.06, "end": 1811.58, "text": " The author isolates it precisely.", "tokens": [51657, 440, 3793, 7381, 1024, 309, 13402, 13, 51733], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1862583625607374, "compression_ratio": 1.6565656565656566, "no_speech_prob": 1.797188266261518e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 181158, "start": 1811.58, "end": 1814.6799999999998, "text": " It's a mathematical structure they denote as J tensor J.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 18894, 3877, 436, 45708, 382, 508, 40863, 508, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 181158, "start": 1815.06, "end": 1817.78, "text": " That's a J, a circle with a cross in it, and another J.", "tokens": [50539, 663, 311, 257, 508, 11, 257, 6329, 365, 257, 3278, 294, 309, 11, 293, 1071, 508, 13, 50675], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 181158, "start": 1818.08, "end": 1819.6399999999999, "text": " Let's break down J tensor J.", "tokens": [50690, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 508, 40863, 508, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 181158, "start": 1819.82, "end": 1820.8999999999999, "text": " What is the J part first?", "tokens": [50777, 708, 307, 264, 508, 644, 700, 30, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 181158, "start": 1821.26, "end": 1823.1799999999998, "text": " J is an anti-symmetric real matrix.", "tokens": [50849, 508, 307, 364, 6061, 12, 3187, 2174, 17475, 957, 8141, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 181158, "start": 1823.74, "end": 1825.78, "text": " Geometrically, it's very simple to visualize.", "tokens": [50973, 2876, 649, 81, 984, 11, 309, 311, 588, 2199, 281, 23273, 13, 51075], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 181158, "start": 1826.4399999999998, "end": 1831.12, "text": " It represents a perfect quarter turn, a 90 degree rotation in a 2D plane.", "tokens": [51108, 467, 8855, 257, 2176, 6555, 1261, 11, 257, 4289, 4314, 12447, 294, 257, 568, 35, 5720, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 181158, "start": 1831.32, "end": 1831.62, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51352, 1033, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 181158, "start": 1831.9199999999998, "end": 1836.04, "text": " Crucially, it is the real number matrix that behaves exactly like the imaginary number I.", "tokens": [51382, 13586, 1909, 11, 309, 307, 264, 957, 1230, 8141, 300, 36896, 2293, 411, 264, 26164, 1230, 286, 13, 51588], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 181158, "start": 1836.26, "end": 1840.58, "text": " Right, because if you take a vector pointing north and you rotate it 90 degrees,", "tokens": [51599, 1779, 11, 570, 498, 291, 747, 257, 8062, 12166, 6830, 293, 291, 13121, 309, 4289, 5310, 11, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13755921050385161, "compression_ratio": 1.5923566878980893, "no_speech_prob": 1.5612965564501535e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 184058, "start": 1840.58, "end": 1842.1, "text": " that's 1 J, it points west.", "tokens": [50365, 300, 311, 502, 508, 11, 309, 2793, 7009, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 184058, "start": 1842.22, "end": 1842.3, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50447, 865, 13, 50451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 184058, "start": 1842.3799999999999, "end": 1845.84, "text": " If you rotate it 90 degrees again, a second J, it points south.", "tokens": [50455, 759, 291, 13121, 309, 4289, 5310, 797, 11, 257, 1150, 508, 11, 309, 2793, 7377, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 184058, "start": 1846.1, "end": 1846.34, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50641, 1779, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 184058, "start": 1846.52, "end": 1850.32, "text": " It's pointing in the exact negative opposite direction of where it started.", "tokens": [50662, 467, 311, 12166, 294, 264, 1900, 3671, 6182, 3513, 295, 689, 309, 1409, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 184058, "start": 1850.46, "end": 1853.76, "text": " So J squared equals negative 1, just like I squared equals negative 1.", "tokens": [50859, 407, 508, 8889, 6915, 3671, 502, 11, 445, 411, 286, 8889, 6915, 3671, 502, 13, 51024], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 184058, "start": 1853.8799999999999, "end": 1854.32, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51030, 7587, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 184058, "start": 1854.54, "end": 1855.6799999999998, "text": " But why is it invisible?", "tokens": [51063, 583, 983, 307, 309, 14603, 30, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 184058, "start": 1855.96, "end": 1858.22, "text": " Why couldn't we see it in our parameter counting?", "tokens": [51134, 1545, 2809, 380, 321, 536, 309, 294, 527, 13075, 13251, 30, 51247], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 184058, "start": 1858.3999999999999, "end": 1858.62, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51256, 865, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 184058, "start": 1858.82, "end": 1859.6, "text": " Why couldn't we see it?", "tokens": [51277, 1545, 2809, 380, 321, 536, 309, 30, 51316], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15179266496138138, "compression_ratio": 1.6441441441441442, "no_speech_prob": 1.4895706196282887e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 185960, "start": 1859.6, "end": 1861.24, "text": " Because J is anti-symmetric.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 508, 307, 6061, 12, 3187, 2174, 17475, 13, 50447], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16107183411007836, "compression_ratio": 1.664864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992315556736855e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 185960, "start": 1862.08, "end": 1868.3999999999999, "text": " In real number quant mechanics, local observables, the actual physical dials you can turn in", "tokens": [50489, 682, 957, 1230, 4426, 12939, 11, 2654, 9951, 2965, 11, 264, 3539, 4001, 5502, 82, 291, 393, 1261, 294, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16107183411007836, "compression_ratio": 1.664864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992315556736855e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 185960, "start": 1868.3999999999999, "end": 1871.12, "text": " your lab, must be symmetric matrices.", "tokens": [50805, 428, 2715, 11, 1633, 312, 32330, 32284, 13, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16107183411007836, "compression_ratio": 1.664864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992315556736855e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 185960, "start": 1871.48, "end": 1871.7199999999998, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50959, 1033, 13, 50971], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16107183411007836, "compression_ratio": 1.664864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992315556736855e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 185960, "start": 1872.04, "end": 1875.82, "text": " Anti-symmetric matrices do not correspond to valid local measurements.", "tokens": [50987, 27757, 12, 3187, 2174, 17475, 32284, 360, 406, 6805, 281, 7363, 2654, 15383, 13, 51176], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16107183411007836, "compression_ratio": 1.664864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992315556736855e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 185960, "start": 1876.04, "end": 1879.4399999999998, "text": " You can never observe J in your lab, and I can never observe J in mine.", "tokens": [51187, 509, 393, 1128, 11441, 508, 294, 428, 2715, 11, 293, 286, 393, 1128, 11441, 508, 294, 3892, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16107183411007836, "compression_ratio": 1.664864864864865, "no_speech_prob": 1.2992315556736855e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 187944, "start": 1879.44, "end": 1884.06, "text": " But when you use the tensor product to combine them, when you do J tensor J.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 562, 291, 764, 264, 40863, 1674, 281, 10432, 552, 11, 562, 291, 360, 508, 40863, 508, 13, 50596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052506697805305, "compression_ratio": 1.7219917012448134, "no_speech_prob": 1.707779208846849e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 187944, "start": 1884.88, "end": 1889.8400000000001, "text": " The rules of matrix algebra dictate that the tensor product of two anti-symmetric matrices", "tokens": [50637, 440, 4474, 295, 8141, 21989, 36071, 300, 264, 40863, 1674, 295, 732, 6061, 12, 3187, 2174, 17475, 32284, 50885], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052506697805305, "compression_ratio": 1.7219917012448134, "no_speech_prob": 1.707779208846849e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 187944, "start": 1889.8400000000001, "end": 1892.16, "text": " results in a symmetric matrix.", "tokens": [50885, 3542, 294, 257, 32330, 8141, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052506697805305, "compression_ratio": 1.7219917012448134, "no_speech_prob": 1.707779208846849e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 187944, "start": 1892.3, "end": 1894.54, "text": " J tensor J is perfectly symmetric.", "tokens": [51008, 508, 40863, 508, 307, 6239, 32330, 13, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052506697805305, "compression_ratio": 1.7219917012448134, "no_speech_prob": 1.707779208846849e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 187944, "start": 1895.26, "end": 1900.6200000000001, "text": " Therefore, it is a completely valid physical observable measurement on the joint system.", "tokens": [51156, 7504, 11, 309, 307, 257, 2584, 7363, 4001, 9951, 712, 13160, 322, 264, 7225, 1185, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052506697805305, "compression_ratio": 1.7219917012448134, "no_speech_prob": 1.707779208846849e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 187944, "start": 1901.06, "end": 1906.88, "text": " But because its constituent parts are locally impossible to observe, you can never construct", "tokens": [51446, 583, 570, 1080, 16085, 317, 3166, 366, 16143, 6243, 281, 11441, 11, 291, 393, 1128, 7690, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13052506697805305, "compression_ratio": 1.7219917012448134, "no_speech_prob": 1.707779208846849e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 190688, "start": 1906.88, "end": 1907.98, "text": " it from your local notes.", "tokens": [50365, 309, 490, 428, 2654, 5570, 13, 50420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 190688, "start": 1908.14, "end": 1909.44, "text": " I'm trying to picture this physically.", "tokens": [50428, 286, 478, 1382, 281, 3036, 341, 9762, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 190688, "start": 1909.6000000000001, "end": 1915.0, "text": " It's like, imagine a massive bank vault that requires two physical keys to be turned at", "tokens": [50501, 467, 311, 411, 11, 3811, 257, 5994, 3765, 27134, 300, 7029, 732, 4001, 9317, 281, 312, 3574, 412, 50771], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 190688, "start": 1915.0, "end": 1916.48, "text": " the exact same millisecond.", "tokens": [50771, 264, 1900, 912, 27940, 18882, 13, 50845], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 190688, "start": 1916.5400000000002, "end": 1916.72, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50848, 1033, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 682, "seek": 190688, "start": 1916.8000000000002, "end": 1917.4, "text": " I like this.", "tokens": [50861, 286, 411, 341, 13, 50891], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 683, "seek": 190688, "start": 1917.8200000000002, "end": 1923.74, "text": " But the weird part is, neither you nor I can even see our own keyholes when we are standing", "tokens": [50912, 583, 264, 3657, 644, 307, 11, 9662, 291, 6051, 286, 393, 754, 536, 527, 1065, 2141, 37894, 562, 321, 366, 4877, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 684, "seek": 190688, "start": 1923.74, "end": 1924.7600000000002, "text": " in our separate labs.", "tokens": [51208, 294, 527, 4994, 20339, 13, 51259], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 685, "seek": 190688, "start": 1925.18, "end": 1927.22, "text": " The keyholes literally don't exist locally.", "tokens": [51280, 440, 2141, 37894, 3736, 500, 380, 2514, 16143, 13, 51382], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 686, "seek": 190688, "start": 1927.2600000000002, "end": 1927.5800000000002, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51384, 1779, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 687, "seek": 190688, "start": 1927.5800000000002, "end": 1931.94, "text": " They only pop into physical existence when we bring the two vaults together into a single", "tokens": [51400, 814, 787, 1665, 666, 4001, 9123, 562, 321, 1565, 264, 732, 27134, 82, 1214, 666, 257, 2167, 51618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 688, "seek": 190688, "start": 1931.94, "end": 1934.22, "text": " room and look at them as a unified whole.", "tokens": [51618, 1808, 293, 574, 412, 552, 382, 257, 26787, 1379, 13, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 689, "seek": 190688, "start": 1934.46, "end": 1936.0600000000002, "text": " That is a fantastic visualization.", "tokens": [51744, 663, 307, 257, 5456, 25801, 13, 51824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14209721793591137, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 2.052431792229359e-12}, {"id": 690, "seek": 193606, "start": 1936.06, "end": 1937.96, "text": " The keyholes only exist globally.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 2141, 37894, 787, 2514, 18958, 13, 50460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14649923555143587, "compression_ratio": 1.5875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160349325401111e-12}, {"id": 691, "seek": 193606, "start": 1938.1399999999999, "end": 1940.86, "text": " And this isn't just an abstract mathematical quirk either.", "tokens": [50469, 400, 341, 1943, 380, 445, 364, 12649, 18894, 421, 18610, 2139, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14649923555143587, "compression_ratio": 1.5875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160349325401111e-12}, {"id": 692, "seek": 193606, "start": 1941.3999999999999, "end": 1946.1599999999999, "text": " The text proves that this invisible parameter, which we can call C, represents a whole family", "tokens": [50632, 440, 2487, 25019, 300, 341, 14603, 13075, 11, 597, 321, 393, 818, 383, 11, 8855, 257, 1379, 1605, 50870], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14649923555143587, "compression_ratio": 1.5875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160349325401111e-12}, {"id": 693, "seek": 193606, "start": 1946.1599999999999, "end": 1947.1, "text": " of physical states.", "tokens": [50870, 295, 4001, 4368, 13, 50917], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14649923555143587, "compression_ratio": 1.5875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160349325401111e-12}, {"id": 694, "seek": 193606, "start": 1947.56, "end": 1951.76, "text": " The parameter C can slide on a scale anywhere between Megas 1 and 1.", "tokens": [50940, 440, 13075, 383, 393, 4137, 322, 257, 4373, 4992, 1296, 9986, 296, 502, 293, 502, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14649923555143587, "compression_ratio": 1.5875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160349325401111e-12}, {"id": 695, "seek": 193606, "start": 1951.96, "end": 1952.54, "text": " Meaning what?", "tokens": [51160, 19948, 437, 30, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14649923555143587, "compression_ratio": 1.5875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160349325401111e-12}, {"id": 696, "seek": 193606, "start": 1952.76, "end": 1959.1, "text": " Meaning there is an entire continuous spectrum of physical realities, an entire interval of", "tokens": [51200, 19948, 456, 307, 364, 2302, 10957, 11143, 295, 4001, 27785, 11, 364, 2302, 15035, 295, 51517], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14649923555143587, "compression_ratio": 1.5875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4160349325401111e-12}, {"id": 697, "seek": 195910, "start": 1959.1, "end": 1966.32, "text": " valid joint states that are completely 100% indistinguishable from each other to any local observer.", "tokens": [50365, 7363, 7225, 4368, 300, 366, 2584, 2319, 4, 1016, 468, 7050, 742, 712, 490, 1184, 661, 281, 604, 2654, 27878, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230209466182825, "compression_ratio": 1.4083769633507854, "no_speech_prob": 1.875931267963926e-12}, {"id": 698, "seek": 195910, "start": 1966.6399999999999, "end": 1966.76, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50742, 3153, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230209466182825, "compression_ratio": 1.4083769633507854, "no_speech_prob": 1.875931267963926e-12}, {"id": 699, "seek": 195910, "start": 1967.4599999999998, "end": 1970.1599999999999, "text": " Which brings us perfectly to the concept of entanglement.", "tokens": [50783, 3013, 5607, 505, 6239, 281, 264, 3410, 295, 948, 656, 3054, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230209466182825, "compression_ratio": 1.4083769633507854, "no_speech_prob": 1.875931267963926e-12}, {"id": 700, "seek": 195910, "start": 1970.52, "end": 1975.6599999999999, "text": " Because this invisible parameter C fundamentally redefines what we mean by that word.", "tokens": [50936, 1436, 341, 14603, 13075, 383, 17879, 38818, 1652, 437, 321, 914, 538, 300, 1349, 13, 51193], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230209466182825, "compression_ratio": 1.4083769633507854, "no_speech_prob": 1.875931267963926e-12}, {"id": 701, "seek": 195910, "start": 1975.78, "end": 1976.56, "text": " It absolutely does.", "tokens": [51199, 467, 3122, 775, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230209466182825, "compression_ratio": 1.4083769633507854, "no_speech_prob": 1.875931267963926e-12}, {"id": 702, "seek": 197656, "start": 1976.56, "end": 1982.3, "text": " And to understand the illusion of entanglement here, we have to explore a mathematical tool", "tokens": [50365, 400, 281, 1223, 264, 18854, 295, 948, 656, 3054, 510, 11, 321, 362, 281, 6839, 257, 18894, 2290, 50652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17582986468360537, "compression_ratio": 1.6091370558375635, "no_speech_prob": 2.3119130308085767e-12}, {"id": 703, "seek": 197656, "start": 1982.3, "end": 1983.6599999999999, "text": " called the partial trace.", "tokens": [50652, 1219, 264, 14641, 13508, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17582986468360537, "compression_ratio": 1.6091370558375635, "no_speech_prob": 2.3119130308085767e-12}, {"id": 704, "seek": 197656, "start": 1983.86, "end": 1984.52, "text": " The partial trace.", "tokens": [50730, 440, 14641, 13508, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17582986468360537, "compression_ratio": 1.6091370558375635, "no_speech_prob": 2.3119130308085767e-12}, {"id": 705, "seek": 197656, "start": 1985.0, "end": 1986.26, "text": " It sounds like an auditing term.", "tokens": [50787, 467, 3263, 411, 364, 2379, 1748, 1433, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17582986468360537, "compression_ratio": 1.6091370558375635, "no_speech_prob": 2.3119130308085767e-12}, {"id": 706, "seek": 197656, "start": 1986.52, "end": 1987.62, "text": " How does it work physically?", "tokens": [50863, 1012, 775, 309, 589, 9762, 30, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17582986468360537, "compression_ratio": 1.6091370558375635, "no_speech_prob": 2.3119130308085767e-12}, {"id": 707, "seek": 197656, "start": 1987.96, "end": 1991.26, "text": " Think of it as the mathematical operation of ignoring a subsystem.", "tokens": [50935, 6557, 295, 309, 382, 264, 18894, 6916, 295, 26258, 257, 2090, 9321, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17582986468360537, "compression_ratio": 1.6091370558375635, "no_speech_prob": 2.3119130308085767e-12}, {"id": 708, "seek": 197656, "start": 1991.48, "end": 1992.98, "text": " It's how we calculate shadows.", "tokens": [51111, 467, 311, 577, 321, 8873, 14740, 13, 51186], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17582986468360537, "compression_ratio": 1.6091370558375635, "no_speech_prob": 2.3119130308085767e-12}, {"id": 709, "seek": 197656, "start": 1993.1799999999998, "end": 1993.8999999999999, "text": " Calculating shadows.", "tokens": [51196, 3511, 2444, 990, 14740, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17582986468360537, "compression_ratio": 1.6091370558375635, "no_speech_prob": 2.3119130308085767e-12}, {"id": 710, "seek": 199390, "start": 1993.9, "end": 1999.0600000000002, "text": " Suppose you and I share a joint quantum state, but you take your half to Mars, and I keep", "tokens": [50365, 21360, 291, 293, 286, 2073, 257, 7225, 13018, 1785, 11, 457, 291, 747, 428, 1922, 281, 9692, 11, 293, 286, 1066, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 711, "seek": 199390, "start": 1999.0600000000002, "end": 1999.94, "text": " my half on Earth.", "tokens": [50623, 452, 1922, 322, 4755, 13, 50667], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 712, "seek": 199390, "start": 2000.3400000000001, "end": 2000.68, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50687, 1033, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 713, "seek": 199390, "start": 2000.8400000000001, "end": 2004.68, "text": " If I want to calculate what I will see in my lab on Earth, I can't measure your system.", "tokens": [50712, 759, 286, 528, 281, 8873, 437, 286, 486, 536, 294, 452, 2715, 322, 4755, 11, 286, 393, 380, 3481, 428, 1185, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 714, "seek": 199390, "start": 2004.94, "end": 2009.46, "text": " I have to mathematically trace out or average over all the possibilities of your half of", "tokens": [50917, 286, 362, 281, 44003, 13508, 484, 420, 4274, 670, 439, 264, 12178, 295, 428, 1922, 295, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 715, "seek": 199390, "start": 2009.46, "end": 2009.88, "text": " the system.", "tokens": [51143, 264, 1185, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 716, "seek": 199390, "start": 2009.98, "end": 2011.02, "text": " I marginalize it.", "tokens": [51169, 286, 16885, 1125, 309, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 717, "seek": 199390, "start": 2011.0600000000002, "end": 2014.14, "text": " Imagine two synchronized dancers in a pitch black room.", "tokens": [51223, 11739, 732, 19331, 1602, 25199, 294, 257, 7293, 2211, 1808, 13, 51377], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 718, "seek": 199390, "start": 2014.8200000000002, "end": 2020.3200000000002, "text": " If I only have one spotlight and I shine it entirely on dancer A, I am essentially applying", "tokens": [51411, 759, 286, 787, 362, 472, 24656, 293, 286, 12207, 309, 7696, 322, 21621, 316, 11, 286, 669, 4476, 9275, 51686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 719, "seek": 199390, "start": 2020.3200000000002, "end": 2022.1200000000001, "text": " a partial trace to dancer B.", "tokens": [51686, 257, 14641, 13508, 281, 21621, 363, 13, 51776], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1284038715792778, "compression_ratio": 1.6847457627118645, "no_speech_prob": 1.9813586535355476e-12}, {"id": 720, "seek": 202212, "start": 2022.12, "end": 2028.1999999999998, "text": " I'm ignoring dancer B's specific movements and just looking at the chaotic, seeming shadow", "tokens": [50365, 286, 478, 26258, 21621, 363, 311, 2685, 9981, 293, 445, 1237, 412, 264, 27013, 11, 1643, 278, 8576, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 721, "seek": 202212, "start": 2028.1999999999998, "end": 2031.4399999999998, "text": " dancer A is casting based on their unseen interaction.", "tokens": [50669, 21621, 316, 307, 17301, 2361, 322, 641, 40608, 9285, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 722, "seek": 202212, "start": 2031.56, "end": 2032.1, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50837, 7587, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 723, "seek": 202212, "start": 2032.26, "end": 2033.12, "text": " That is a great analogy.", "tokens": [50872, 663, 307, 257, 869, 21663, 13, 50915], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 724, "seek": 202212, "start": 2033.6799999999998, "end": 2039.1399999999999, "text": " When you apply this partial trace operation to our invisible J tensor J direction, the math", "tokens": [50943, 1133, 291, 3079, 341, 14641, 13508, 6916, 281, 527, 14603, 508, 40863, 508, 3513, 11, 264, 5221, 51216], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 725, "seek": 202212, "start": 2039.1399999999999, "end": 2040.8999999999999, "text": " is totally unambiguous.", "tokens": [51216, 307, 3879, 517, 2173, 30525, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 726, "seek": 202212, "start": 2041.1, "end": 2043.56, "text": " The partial trace completely annihilates it.", "tokens": [51314, 440, 14641, 13508, 2584, 40430, 388, 1024, 309, 13, 51437], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 727, "seek": 202212, "start": 2043.78, "end": 2044.2199999999998, "text": " Annihilates it.", "tokens": [51448, 1107, 3722, 42829, 1024, 309, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 728, "seek": 202212, "start": 2044.2399999999998, "end": 2047.6399999999999, "text": " If you trace out my system, the J tensor J term drops to zero.", "tokens": [51471, 759, 291, 13508, 484, 452, 1185, 11, 264, 508, 40863, 508, 1433, 11438, 281, 4018, 13, 51641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 729, "seek": 202212, "start": 2048.2, "end": 2050.2599999999998, "text": " If I trace out your system, it drops to zero.", "tokens": [51669, 759, 286, 13508, 484, 428, 1185, 11, 309, 11438, 281, 4018, 13, 51772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12152783332332488, "compression_ratio": 1.7350746268656716, "no_speech_prob": 1.3887721268118769e-12}, {"id": 730, "seek": 205026, "start": 2050.26, "end": 2055.42, "text": " From either local perspective, this joint state looks entirely devoid of structure.", "tokens": [50365, 3358, 2139, 2654, 4585, 11, 341, 7225, 1785, 1542, 7696, 1905, 17079, 295, 3877, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 731, "seek": 205026, "start": 2055.5800000000004, "end": 2056.6200000000003, "text": " It looks like pure static.", "tokens": [50631, 467, 1542, 411, 6075, 13437, 13, 50683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 732, "seek": 205026, "start": 2056.7400000000002, "end": 2058.1800000000003, "text": " It looks maximally mixed.", "tokens": [50689, 467, 1542, 5138, 379, 7467, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 733, "seek": 205026, "start": 2058.34, "end": 2058.5, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50769, 1033, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 734, "seek": 205026, "start": 2058.6000000000004, "end": 2064.5800000000004, "text": " So the state has this deeply hidden structure globally, the two keyholes, but locally it", "tokens": [50782, 407, 264, 1785, 575, 341, 8760, 7633, 3877, 18958, 11, 264, 732, 2141, 37894, 11, 457, 16143, 309, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 735, "seek": 205026, "start": 2064.5800000000004, "end": 2066.0, "text": " just looks like random static.", "tokens": [51081, 445, 1542, 411, 4974, 13437, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 736, "seek": 205026, "start": 2066.1400000000003, "end": 2066.36, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51159, 865, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 737, "seek": 205026, "start": 2066.44, "end": 2068.6600000000003, "text": " That sounds exactly like the definition of entanglement.", "tokens": [51174, 663, 3263, 2293, 411, 264, 7123, 295, 948, 656, 3054, 13, 51285], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 738, "seek": 205026, "start": 2068.78, "end": 2071.6800000000003, "text": " And this is where the author delivers an absolute knockout punch.", "tokens": [51291, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 3793, 24860, 364, 8236, 6728, 346, 8135, 13, 51436], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 739, "seek": 205026, "start": 2071.9, "end": 2073.5, "text": " This is the crux of the entire text.", "tokens": [51447, 639, 307, 264, 5140, 87, 295, 264, 2302, 2487, 13, 51527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 740, "seek": 205026, "start": 2073.6400000000003, "end": 2075.5400000000004, "text": " Is this state actually entangled?", "tokens": [51534, 1119, 341, 1785, 767, 948, 39101, 30, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13112722237904867, "compression_ratio": 1.6923076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839893636847679e-12}, {"id": 741, "seek": 207554, "start": 2075.54, "end": 2077.42, "text": " Well, is it?", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 307, 309, 30, 50459], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1609854016985212, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349433521773872e-12}, {"id": 742, "seek": 207554, "start": 2077.64, "end": 2082.5, "text": " If the universe runs on real quantum mechanics, if we are confined to real numbers, the answer", "tokens": [50470, 759, 264, 6445, 6676, 322, 957, 13018, 12939, 11, 498, 321, 366, 31745, 281, 957, 3547, 11, 264, 1867, 50713], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1609854016985212, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349433521773872e-12}, {"id": 743, "seek": 207554, "start": 2082.5, "end": 2084.14, "text": " is unambiguously yes.", "tokens": [50713, 307, 517, 2173, 16397, 5098, 2086, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1609854016985212, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349433521773872e-12}, {"id": 744, "seek": 207554, "start": 2084.64, "end": 2090.4, "text": " For any value of co other than zero, that state cannot be factored into independent local", "tokens": [50820, 1171, 604, 2158, 295, 598, 661, 813, 4018, 11, 300, 1785, 2644, 312, 1186, 2769, 666, 6695, 2654, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1609854016985212, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349433521773872e-12}, {"id": 745, "seek": 207554, "start": 2090.4, "end": 2091.2599999999998, "text": " product states.", "tokens": [51108, 1674, 4368, 13, 51151], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1609854016985212, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349433521773872e-12}, {"id": 746, "seek": 207554, "start": 2091.56, "end": 2094.58, "text": " It is mathematically, provably entangled.", "tokens": [51166, 467, 307, 44003, 11, 1439, 1188, 948, 39101, 13, 51317], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1609854016985212, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349433521773872e-12}, {"id": 747, "seek": 207554, "start": 2094.96, "end": 2095.16, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51336, 1033, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1609854016985212, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349433521773872e-12}, {"id": 748, "seek": 207554, "start": 2095.2, "end": 2098.16, "text": " But what if the universe runs on complex numbers?", "tokens": [51348, 583, 437, 498, 264, 6445, 6676, 322, 3997, 3547, 30, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1609854016985212, "compression_ratio": 1.5416666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7349433521773872e-12}, {"id": 749, "seek": 209816, "start": 2098.16, "end": 2103.2599999999998, "text": " Under standard complex numbers, that exact same family of states, that identical physical", "tokens": [50365, 6974, 3832, 3997, 3547, 11, 300, 1900, 912, 1605, 295, 4368, 11, 300, 14800, 4001, 50620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 750, "seek": 209816, "start": 2103.2599999999998, "end": 2106.68, "text": " matrix sitting on the table, is completely separable.", "tokens": [50620, 8141, 3798, 322, 264, 3199, 11, 307, 2584, 3128, 712, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 751, "seek": 209816, "start": 2106.96, "end": 2108.2, "text": " It is not entangled at all.", "tokens": [50805, 467, 307, 406, 948, 39101, 412, 439, 13, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 752, "seek": 209816, "start": 2108.3199999999997, "end": 2108.52, "text": " Wait.", "tokens": [50873, 3802, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 753, "seek": 209816, "start": 2108.96, "end": 2109.2999999999997, "text": " Stop.", "tokens": [50905, 5535, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 754, "seek": 209816, "start": 2109.44, "end": 2111.12, "text": " Let me make sure I'm hearing you correctly here.", "tokens": [50929, 961, 385, 652, 988, 286, 478, 4763, 291, 8944, 510, 13, 51013], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 755, "seek": 209816, "start": 2111.18, "end": 2111.46, "text": " Go ahead.", "tokens": [51016, 1037, 2286, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 756, "seek": 209816, "start": 2111.66, "end": 2117.62, "text": " You're saying that entanglement, the spooky action at a distance that famously drove Albert", "tokens": [51040, 509, 434, 1566, 300, 948, 656, 3054, 11, 264, 30510, 3069, 412, 257, 4560, 300, 34360, 13226, 20812, 51338], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 757, "seek": 209816, "start": 2117.62, "end": 2123.12, "text": " Einstein crazy, the thing we considered the defining feature of the quantum realm, isn't", "tokens": [51338, 23486, 3219, 11, 264, 551, 321, 4888, 264, 17827, 4111, 295, 264, 13018, 15355, 11, 1943, 380, 51613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 758, "seek": 209816, "start": 2123.12, "end": 2125.66, "text": " actually a property of the physical system itself.", "tokens": [51613, 767, 257, 4707, 295, 264, 4001, 1185, 2564, 13, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 759, "seek": 209816, "start": 2125.7799999999997, "end": 2126.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51746, 1779, 13, 51759], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10197939638231622, "compression_ratio": 1.6140939597315436, "no_speech_prob": 1.5735374158179494e-12}, {"id": 760, "seek": 212604, "start": 2126.04, "end": 2129.14, "text": " It's a property of the math we are using to look at the system.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 4707, 295, 264, 5221, 321, 366, 1228, 281, 574, 412, 264, 1185, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 761, "seek": 212604, "start": 2129.34, "end": 2132.58, "text": " You are grasping the exact magnitude of what this text proves.", "tokens": [50530, 509, 366, 29444, 3381, 264, 1900, 15668, 295, 437, 341, 2487, 25019, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 762, "seek": 212604, "start": 2133.06, "end": 2137.1, "text": " Entanglement is not an intrinsic, unchangeable property of a physical matrix.", "tokens": [50716, 3951, 656, 3054, 307, 406, 364, 35698, 11, 517, 15431, 712, 4707, 295, 257, 4001, 8141, 13, 50918], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 763, "seek": 212604, "start": 2137.3, "end": 2138.2, "text": " It is just, wow.", "tokens": [50928, 467, 307, 445, 11, 6076, 13, 50973], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 764, "seek": 212604, "start": 2138.44, "end": 2139.38, "text": " It is field relative.", "tokens": [50985, 467, 307, 2519, 4972, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 765, "seek": 212604, "start": 2139.72, "end": 2143.44, "text": " It is entirely relative to the scalar field, real or complex, doing the composing.", "tokens": [51049, 467, 307, 7696, 4972, 281, 264, 39684, 2519, 11, 957, 420, 3997, 11, 884, 264, 715, 6110, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 766, "seek": 212604, "start": 2143.72, "end": 2148.68, "text": " Because if you switch to complex numbers, that invisible J tensor J witness is no longer", "tokens": [51249, 1436, 498, 291, 3679, 281, 3997, 3547, 11, 300, 14603, 508, 40863, 508, 7286, 307, 572, 2854, 51497], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 767, "seek": 212604, "start": 2148.68, "end": 2151.74, "text": " built out of locally impossible antisymmetric matrices.", "tokens": [51497, 3094, 484, 295, 16143, 6243, 2511, 14169, 2174, 17475, 32284, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 768, "seek": 212604, "start": 2152.06, "end": 2152.2599999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51666, 1779, 13, 51676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 769, "seek": 212604, "start": 2152.32, "end": 2154.32, "text": " Because complex numbers handle that inherently.", "tokens": [51679, 1436, 3997, 3547, 4813, 300, 27993, 13, 51779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 770, "seek": 212604, "start": 2154.52, "end": 2155.02, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51789, 7587, 13, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12189490553261577, "compression_ratio": 1.742671009771987, "no_speech_prob": 1.4604505755785868e-12}, {"id": 771, "seek": 215502, "start": 2155.02, "end": 2161.46, "text": " In complex numbers, it is just negative one times the normal product of complex polymatrices.", "tokens": [50365, 682, 3997, 3547, 11, 309, 307, 445, 3671, 472, 1413, 264, 2710, 1674, 295, 3997, 6754, 15677, 24373, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14940945307413736, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246534925353552e-12}, {"id": 772, "seek": 215502, "start": 2161.82, "end": 2165.1, "text": " It's totally observable using complex local bases.", "tokens": [50705, 467, 311, 3879, 9951, 712, 1228, 3997, 2654, 17949, 13, 50869], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14940945307413736, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246534925353552e-12}, {"id": 773, "seek": 215502, "start": 2165.56, "end": 2172.46, "text": " What requires spooky entanglement in real numbers is just a mundane classical correlation in complex", "tokens": [50892, 708, 7029, 30510, 948, 656, 3054, 294, 957, 3547, 307, 445, 257, 43497, 13735, 20009, 294, 3997, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14940945307413736, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246534925353552e-12}, {"id": 774, "seek": 215502, "start": 2172.46, "end": 2172.88, "text": " numbers.", "tokens": [51237, 3547, 13, 51258], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14940945307413736, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246534925353552e-12}, {"id": 775, "seek": 215502, "start": 2173.08, "end": 2174.14, "text": " That is mind-blowing.", "tokens": [51268, 663, 307, 1575, 12, 43788, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14940945307413736, "compression_ratio": 1.5333333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.8246534925353552e-12}, {"id": 776, "seek": 217414, "start": 2174.14, "end": 2175.52, "text": " I need to put this into an analogy.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 643, 281, 829, 341, 666, 364, 21663, 13, 50434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 777, "seek": 217414, "start": 2176.2, "end": 2179.48, "text": " Imagine two people sitting in a room sharing a secret language.", "tokens": [50468, 11739, 732, 561, 3798, 294, 257, 1808, 5414, 257, 4054, 2856, 13, 50632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 778, "seek": 217414, "start": 2179.64, "end": 2179.8399999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50640, 1779, 13, 50650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 779, "seek": 217414, "start": 2180.04, "end": 2184.7, "text": " Let's say they are perfectly fluent in Navajo and they are discussing a complex engineering", "tokens": [50660, 961, 311, 584, 436, 366, 6239, 40799, 294, 9219, 13440, 293, 436, 366, 10850, 257, 3997, 7043, 50893], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 780, "seek": 217414, "start": 2184.7, "end": 2185.16, "text": " project.", "tokens": [50893, 1716, 13, 50916], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 781, "seek": 217414, "start": 2185.2599999999998, "end": 2185.48, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50921, 1033, 13, 50932], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 782, "seek": 217414, "start": 2185.56, "end": 2186.0, "text": " I'm tracking.", "tokens": [50936, 286, 478, 11603, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 783, "seek": 217414, "start": 2186.2, "end": 2189.08, "text": " Now, imagine an English-only speaker is watching them.", "tokens": [50968, 823, 11, 3811, 364, 3669, 12, 25202, 8145, 307, 1976, 552, 13, 51112], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 784, "seek": 217414, "start": 2189.48, "end": 2192.22, "text": " The English speaker represents real numbers.", "tokens": [51132, 440, 3669, 8145, 8855, 957, 3547, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 785, "seek": 217414, "start": 2192.68, "end": 2196.5, "text": " To the English speaker, these two people seem telepathically linked.", "tokens": [51292, 1407, 264, 3669, 8145, 11, 613, 732, 561, 1643, 4304, 31852, 984, 9408, 13, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 786, "seek": 217414, "start": 2196.58, "end": 2196.7599999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51487, 1779, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 787, "seek": 217414, "start": 2196.7999999999997, "end": 2198.22, "text": " Because they can't understand the medium.", "tokens": [51498, 1436, 436, 393, 380, 1223, 264, 6399, 13, 51569], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.22262292845636353, "compression_ratio": 1.654275092936803, "no_speech_prob": 1.886265883072058e-12}, {"id": 788, "seek": 219822, "start": 2198.22, "end": 2198.74, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50391], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1873167738129821, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080568730232226e-12}, {"id": 789, "seek": 219822, "start": 2199.16, "end": 2203.4399999999996, "text": " They are coordinating these incredibly complex actions, handing each other tools, anticipating", "tokens": [50412, 814, 366, 37824, 613, 6252, 3997, 5909, 11, 34774, 1184, 661, 3873, 11, 40568, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1873167738129821, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080568730232226e-12}, {"id": 790, "seek": 219822, "start": 2203.4399999999996, "end": 2207.06, "text": " moves, without saying a single word the English speaker can comprehend.", "tokens": [50626, 6067, 11, 1553, 1566, 257, 2167, 1349, 264, 3669, 8145, 393, 38183, 13, 50807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1873167738129821, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080568730232226e-12}, {"id": 791, "seek": 219822, "start": 2207.7799999999997, "end": 2210.08, "text": " To the English speaker, they are entangled.", "tokens": [50843, 1407, 264, 3669, 8145, 11, 436, 366, 948, 39101, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1873167738129821, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080568730232226e-12}, {"id": 792, "seek": 219822, "start": 2210.4199999999996, "end": 2211.12, "text": " It's spooky action.", "tokens": [50975, 467, 311, 30510, 3069, 13, 51010], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1873167738129821, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080568730232226e-12}, {"id": 793, "seek": 219822, "start": 2211.7, "end": 2214.7, "text": " But what happens when a bilingual speaker walks into the room?", "tokens": [51039, 583, 437, 2314, 562, 257, 48757, 8145, 12896, 666, 264, 1808, 30, 51189], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1873167738129821, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080568730232226e-12}, {"id": 794, "seek": 219822, "start": 2214.9599999999996, "end": 2217.48, "text": " The bilingual speaker represents complex numbers.", "tokens": [51202, 440, 48757, 8145, 8855, 3997, 3547, 13, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1873167738129821, "compression_ratio": 1.6603773584905661, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080568730232226e-12}, {"id": 795, "seek": 221748, "start": 2217.48, "end": 2222.34, "text": " They walk in, they listen for two seconds, and the illusion completely shatters.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 1792, 294, 11, 436, 2140, 337, 732, 3949, 11, 293, 264, 18854, 2584, 402, 37690, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 796, "seek": 221748, "start": 2222.52, "end": 2223.34, "text": " It all becomes clear.", "tokens": [50617, 467, 439, 3643, 1850, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 797, "seek": 221748, "start": 2223.52, "end": 2226.84, "text": " The bilingual speaker realizes, oh, they aren't telepathic.", "tokens": [50667, 440, 48757, 8145, 29316, 11, 1954, 11, 436, 3212, 380, 4304, 31852, 299, 13, 50833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 798, "seek": 221748, "start": 2226.98, "end": 2228.18, "text": " They aren't magically entangled.", "tokens": [50840, 814, 3212, 380, 39763, 948, 39101, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 799, "seek": 221748, "start": 2228.46, "end": 2231.18, "text": " They are just reading from the exact same translated script.", "tokens": [50914, 814, 366, 445, 3760, 490, 264, 1900, 912, 16805, 5755, 13, 51050], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 800, "seek": 221748, "start": 2231.32, "end": 2233.72, "text": " They're just speaking a language with a richer vocabulary.", "tokens": [51057, 814, 434, 445, 4124, 257, 2856, 365, 257, 29021, 19864, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 801, "seek": 221748, "start": 2234.02, "end": 2234.34, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51192, 1079, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 802, "seek": 221748, "start": 2234.62, "end": 2239.42, "text": " The entanglement is an illusion caused entirely by the English speaker's limited grammar.", "tokens": [51222, 440, 948, 656, 3054, 307, 364, 18854, 7008, 7696, 538, 264, 3669, 8145, 311, 5567, 22317, 13, 51462], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 803, "seek": 221748, "start": 2239.76, "end": 2242.4, "text": " It's totally separable once you have the right vocabulary.", "tokens": [51479, 467, 311, 3879, 3128, 712, 1564, 291, 362, 264, 558, 19864, 13, 51611], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 804, "seek": 221748, "start": 2242.4, "end": 2247.12, "text": " It forces us to take a massive step back and question absolutely everything.", "tokens": [51611, 467, 5874, 505, 281, 747, 257, 5994, 1823, 646, 293, 1168, 3122, 1203, 13, 51847], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13937564296576813, "compression_ratio": 1.7115987460815048, "no_speech_prob": 2.1591587025249215e-12}, {"id": 805, "seek": 224748, "start": 2247.48, "end": 2252.64, "text": " How much of quantum weirdness is a profound, inescapable truth about reality?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 709, 295, 13018, 3657, 1287, 307, 257, 14382, 11, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 3494, 466, 4103, 30, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1331296838739867, "compression_ratio": 1.6307053941908713, "no_speech_prob": 1.9890966044405767e-12}, {"id": 806, "seek": 224748, "start": 2253.0, "end": 2257.52, "text": " And how much of it is just a shadow cast by our choice of mathematical notation?", "tokens": [50641, 400, 577, 709, 295, 309, 307, 445, 257, 8576, 4193, 538, 527, 3922, 295, 18894, 24657, 30, 50867], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1331296838739867, "compression_ratio": 1.6307053941908713, "no_speech_prob": 1.9890966044405767e-12}, {"id": 807, "seek": 224748, "start": 2257.92, "end": 2259.9, "text": " Which brings us to the assumption audit.", "tokens": [50887, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 15302, 17748, 13, 50986], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1331296838739867, "compression_ratio": 1.6307053941908713, "no_speech_prob": 1.9890966044405767e-12}, {"id": 808, "seek": 224748, "start": 2260.4, "end": 2265.6, "text": " Because if quantum mechanics is so heavily dependent on the mathematical grammar we choose", "tokens": [51011, 1436, 498, 13018, 12939, 307, 370, 10950, 12334, 322, 264, 18894, 22317, 321, 2826, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1331296838739867, "compression_ratio": 1.6307053941908713, "no_speech_prob": 1.9890966044405767e-12}, {"id": 809, "seek": 224748, "start": 2265.6, "end": 2270.84, "text": " to use, what do we actually have to assume to build the standard, complex quantum theory", "tokens": [51271, 281, 764, 11, 437, 360, 321, 767, 362, 281, 6552, 281, 1322, 264, 3832, 11, 3997, 13018, 5261, 51533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1331296838739867, "compression_ratio": 1.6307053941908713, "no_speech_prob": 1.9890966044405767e-12}, {"id": 810, "seek": 224748, "start": 2270.84, "end": 2271.64, "text": " we use today?", "tokens": [51533, 321, 764, 965, 30, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1331296838739867, "compression_ratio": 1.6307053941908713, "no_speech_prob": 1.9890966044405767e-12}, {"id": 811, "seek": 227164, "start": 2271.64, "end": 2278.2599999999998, "text": " After 78 pages of uncompromising dense derivation, the author tallies up the final bill.", "tokens": [50365, 2381, 26369, 7183, 295, 8585, 28722, 3436, 18011, 10151, 399, 11, 264, 3793, 6764, 530, 493, 264, 2572, 2961, 13, 50696], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1970674991607666, "compression_ratio": 1.542857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 812, "seek": 227164, "start": 2278.9, "end": 2285.18, "text": " Out of all the possible ways to build a universe, the author identifies exactly four independent", "tokens": [50728, 5925, 295, 439, 264, 1944, 2098, 281, 1322, 257, 6445, 11, 264, 3793, 34597, 2293, 1451, 6695, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1970674991607666, "compression_ratio": 1.542857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 813, "seek": 227164, "start": 2285.18, "end": 2288.7, "text": " physical assumptions used to recover standard quantum mechanics.", "tokens": [51042, 4001, 17695, 1143, 281, 8114, 3832, 13018, 12939, 13, 51218], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1970674991607666, "compression_ratio": 1.542857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 814, "seek": 227164, "start": 2288.8399999999997, "end": 2289.14, "text": " Four.", "tokens": [51225, 7451, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1970674991607666, "compression_ratio": 1.542857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 815, "seek": 227164, "start": 2289.46, "end": 2292.2599999999998, "text": " Just four pillars holding up the entire sky.", "tokens": [51256, 1449, 1451, 26729, 5061, 493, 264, 2302, 5443, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1970674991607666, "compression_ratio": 1.542857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 816, "seek": 227164, "start": 2292.3799999999997, "end": 2292.92, "text": " Only four.", "tokens": [51402, 5686, 1451, 13, 51429], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1970674991607666, "compression_ratio": 1.542857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 817, "seek": 227164, "start": 2293.02, "end": 2294.54, "text": " Let's walk through them one by one.", "tokens": [51434, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 552, 472, 538, 472, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1970674991607666, "compression_ratio": 1.542857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 818, "seek": 227164, "start": 2294.8199999999997, "end": 2295.2999999999997, "text": " Number one.", "tokens": [51524, 5118, 472, 13, 51548], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1970674991607666, "compression_ratio": 1.542857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 819, "seek": 227164, "start": 2295.8199999999997, "end": 2296.96, "text": " Local tomography.", "tokens": [51574, 22755, 2916, 5820, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1970674991607666, "compression_ratio": 1.542857142857143, "no_speech_prob": 1.965634252587556e-12}, {"id": 820, "seek": 229696, "start": 2296.96, "end": 2302.44, "text": " The assumption we just spent all that time discussing, the idea that joint states are", "tokens": [50365, 440, 15302, 321, 445, 4418, 439, 300, 565, 10850, 11, 264, 1558, 300, 7225, 4368, 366, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 821, "seek": 229696, "start": 2302.44, "end": 2304.54, "text": " fully described by local measurements.", "tokens": [50639, 4498, 7619, 538, 2654, 15383, 13, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 822, "seek": 229696, "start": 2304.68, "end": 2304.9, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50751, 1779, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 823, "seek": 229696, "start": 2305.1, "end": 2307.1, "text": " Remember, the author didn't derive this as a given.", "tokens": [50772, 5459, 11, 264, 3793, 994, 380, 28446, 341, 382, 257, 2212, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 824, "seek": 229696, "start": 2307.52, "end": 2312.1, "text": " They assumed it, tested it, and found that complex numbers pass the test perfectly.", "tokens": [50893, 814, 15895, 309, 11, 8246, 309, 11, 293, 1352, 300, 3997, 3547, 1320, 264, 1500, 6239, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 825, "seek": 229696, "start": 2312.2400000000002, "end": 2312.4, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51129, 1779, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 826, "seek": 229696, "start": 2312.5, "end": 2315.04, "text": " The 16 equals 16 dimension match we did earlier.", "tokens": [51142, 440, 3165, 6915, 3165, 10139, 2995, 321, 630, 3071, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 827, "seek": 229696, "start": 2315.2, "end": 2315.94, "text": " That's pillar one.", "tokens": [51277, 663, 311, 27592, 472, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 828, "seek": 229696, "start": 2316.04, "end": 2316.76, "text": " What is number two?", "tokens": [51319, 708, 307, 1230, 732, 30, 51355], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 829, "seek": 229696, "start": 2316.94, "end": 2317.28, "text": " Two.", "tokens": [51364, 4453, 13, 51381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 830, "seek": 229696, "start": 2317.9, "end": 2320.04, "text": " Pure states are frame-completable vectors.", "tokens": [51412, 29474, 4368, 366, 3920, 12, 1112, 14657, 712, 18875, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 831, "seek": 229696, "start": 2320.28, "end": 2321.2200000000003, "text": " Frame-completable vectors.", "tokens": [51531, 31628, 12, 1112, 14657, 712, 18875, 13, 51578], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 832, "seek": 229696, "start": 2321.3, "end": 2322.7, "text": " Let's translate that for everyone.", "tokens": [51582, 961, 311, 13799, 300, 337, 1518, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17026673546133114, "compression_ratio": 1.667844522968198, "no_speech_prob": 1.1922498578675889e-12}, {"id": 833, "seek": 232270, "start": 2322.7, "end": 2327.4199999999996, "text": " In simple terms, it means that if you have a state of absolute certainty, a pure state,", "tokens": [50365, 682, 2199, 2115, 11, 309, 1355, 300, 498, 291, 362, 257, 1785, 295, 8236, 27022, 11, 257, 6075, 1785, 11, 50601], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195104146407823, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556522862767875e-12}, {"id": 834, "seek": 232270, "start": 2327.54, "end": 2331.96, "text": " where you know exactly what the system is doing, you can mathematically treat that state", "tokens": [50607, 689, 291, 458, 2293, 437, 264, 1185, 307, 884, 11, 291, 393, 44003, 2387, 300, 1785, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195104146407823, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556522862767875e-12}, {"id": 835, "seek": 232270, "start": 2331.96, "end": 2334.8799999999997, "text": " as just one column in a larger transition matrix.", "tokens": [50828, 382, 445, 472, 7738, 294, 257, 4833, 6034, 8141, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195104146407823, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556522862767875e-12}, {"id": 836, "seek": 232270, "start": 2334.98, "end": 2336.62, "text": " You can complete the frame around it.", "tokens": [50979, 509, 393, 3566, 264, 3920, 926, 309, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195104146407823, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556522862767875e-12}, {"id": 837, "seek": 232270, "start": 2336.98, "end": 2337.4199999999996, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51079, 7587, 13, 51101], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195104146407823, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556522862767875e-12}, {"id": 838, "seek": 232270, "start": 2337.7799999999997, "end": 2340.6, "text": " You complete the frame to map out all the other possibilities.", "tokens": [51119, 509, 3566, 264, 3920, 281, 4471, 484, 439, 264, 661, 12178, 13, 51260], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195104146407823, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556522862767875e-12}, {"id": 839, "seek": 232270, "start": 2340.7999999999997, "end": 2342.8599999999997, "text": " And what does assuming that actually buy us?", "tokens": [51270, 400, 437, 775, 11926, 300, 767, 2256, 505, 30, 51373], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195104146407823, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556522862767875e-12}, {"id": 840, "seek": 232270, "start": 2343.0, "end": 2343.9399999999996, "text": " It buys us everything.", "tokens": [51380, 467, 28153, 505, 1203, 13, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195104146407823, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556522862767875e-12}, {"id": 841, "seek": 232270, "start": 2344.52, "end": 2349.0, "text": " By making this one geometric assumption, the author instantly derives the Born Rule.", "tokens": [51456, 3146, 1455, 341, 472, 33246, 15302, 11, 264, 3793, 13518, 1163, 1539, 264, 29808, 27533, 13, 51680], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10195104146407823, "compression_ratio": 1.6920415224913494, "no_speech_prob": 1.6556522862767875e-12}, {"id": 842, "seek": 234900, "start": 2349.0, "end": 2354.92, "text": " The Born Rule is the fundamental law that tells us how to calculate the probability of a quantum event happening.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 29808, 27533, 307, 264, 8088, 2101, 300, 5112, 505, 577, 281, 8873, 264, 8482, 295, 257, 13018, 2280, 2737, 13, 50661], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 843, "seek": 234900, "start": 2355.06, "end": 2355.28, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50668, 1779, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 844, "seek": 234900, "start": 2355.56, "end": 2356.72, "text": " You square the amplitude.", "tokens": [50693, 509, 3732, 264, 27433, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 845, "seek": 234900, "start": 2357.1, "end": 2357.48, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50770, 7587, 13, 50789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 846, "seek": 234900, "start": 2357.96, "end": 2361.4, "text": " In most textbooks, the Born Rule is just handed to you as a postulate.", "tokens": [50813, 682, 881, 33587, 11, 264, 29808, 27533, 307, 445, 16013, 281, 291, 382, 257, 2183, 5256, 13, 50985], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 847, "seek": 234900, "start": 2361.8, "end": 2363.0, "text": " This is how probability works.", "tokens": [51005, 639, 307, 577, 8482, 1985, 13, 51065], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 848, "seek": 234900, "start": 2363.18, "end": 2363.86, "text": " Don't ask why.", "tokens": [51074, 1468, 380, 1029, 983, 13, 51108], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 849, "seek": 234900, "start": 2364.04, "end": 2364.82, "text": " Just accept it.", "tokens": [51117, 1449, 3241, 309, 13, 51156], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 850, "seek": 234900, "start": 2364.92, "end": 2365.1, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51161, 1779, 13, 51170], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 851, "seek": 234900, "start": 2365.58, "end": 2373.28, "text": " But here, the Born Rule emerges organically just from assuming that pure states can be placed inside a complete mathematical frame.", "tokens": [51194, 583, 510, 11, 264, 29808, 27533, 38965, 1798, 984, 445, 490, 11926, 300, 6075, 4368, 393, 312, 7074, 1854, 257, 3566, 18894, 3920, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 852, "seek": 234900, "start": 2373.44, "end": 2374.5, "text": " That's incredibly elegant.", "tokens": [51587, 663, 311, 6252, 21117, 13, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 853, "seek": 234900, "start": 2375.16, "end": 2375.36, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51673, 1033, 13, 51683], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 854, "seek": 234900, "start": 2375.56, "end": 2376.34, "text": " Pillar number three.", "tokens": [51693, 430, 30635, 1230, 1045, 13, 51732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 855, "seek": 234900, "start": 2376.34, "end": 2376.9, "text": " Three.", "tokens": [51732, 6244, 13, 51760], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19106916947798294, "compression_ratio": 1.6266666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7622644879825011e-12}, {"id": 856, "seek": 237690, "start": 2376.9, "end": 2380.54, "text": " Measurement outcomes are labeled by real numbers.", "tokens": [50365, 41436, 518, 10070, 366, 21335, 538, 957, 3547, 13, 50547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1684134977835196, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688897221979083e-12}, {"id": 857, "seek": 237690, "start": 2381.0, "end": 2381.02, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50570, 1033, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1684134977835196, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688897221979083e-12}, {"id": 858, "seek": 237690, "start": 2381.1, "end": 2382.28, "text": " That feels incredibly obvious.", "tokens": [50575, 663, 3417, 6252, 6322, 13, 50634], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1684134977835196, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688897221979083e-12}, {"id": 859, "seek": 237690, "start": 2382.76, "end": 2386.44, "text": " If I measure the weight of a quantum particle, my digital scale gives me a real number.", "tokens": [50658, 759, 286, 3481, 264, 3364, 295, 257, 13018, 12359, 11, 452, 4562, 4373, 2709, 385, 257, 957, 1230, 13, 50842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1684134977835196, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688897221979083e-12}, {"id": 860, "seek": 237690, "start": 2386.56, "end": 2387.76, "text": " It says 5.2.", "tokens": [50848, 467, 1619, 1025, 13, 17, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1684134977835196, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688897221979083e-12}, {"id": 861, "seek": 237690, "start": 2387.98, "end": 2389.6, "text": " It doesn't give me an imaginary number.", "tokens": [50919, 467, 1177, 380, 976, 385, 364, 26164, 1230, 13, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1684134977835196, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688897221979083e-12}, {"id": 862, "seek": 237690, "start": 2389.7200000000003, "end": 2394.96, "text": " It seems obvious to our human experience, but mathematically, this is a profound choice.", "tokens": [51006, 467, 2544, 6322, 281, 527, 1952, 1752, 11, 457, 44003, 11, 341, 307, 257, 14382, 3922, 13, 51268], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1684134977835196, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688897221979083e-12}, {"id": 863, "seek": 237690, "start": 2395.2200000000003, "end": 2395.6, "text": " How so?", "tokens": [51281, 1012, 370, 30, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1684134977835196, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688897221979083e-12}, {"id": 864, "seek": 237690, "start": 2395.8, "end": 2401.6, "text": " This specific assumption is what forces quantum observables to be described by Hermitian matrices.", "tokens": [51310, 639, 2685, 15302, 307, 437, 5874, 13018, 9951, 2965, 281, 312, 7619, 538, 21842, 270, 952, 32284, 13, 51600], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1684134977835196, "compression_ratio": 1.5666666666666667, "no_speech_prob": 1.7688897221979083e-12}, {"id": 865, "seek": 240160, "start": 2401.6, "end": 2410.12, "text": " It forces the math to ensure that the eigenvalues, the actual readings on your digital scale, are strictly real numbers.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 5874, 264, 5221, 281, 5586, 300, 264, 10446, 46033, 11, 264, 3539, 27319, 322, 428, 4562, 4373, 11, 366, 20792, 957, 3547, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230081483915255, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170654205399098e-12}, {"id": 866, "seek": 240160, "start": 2410.52, "end": 2410.88, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [50811, 2438, 13, 50829], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230081483915255, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170654205399098e-12}, {"id": 867, "seek": 240160, "start": 2411.12, "end": 2411.22, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50841, 1033, 13, 50846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230081483915255, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170654205399098e-12}, {"id": 868, "seek": 240160, "start": 2411.22, "end": 2414.62, "text": " It's a choice about how we label the reality we interact with.", "tokens": [50846, 467, 311, 257, 3922, 466, 577, 321, 7645, 264, 4103, 321, 4648, 365, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230081483915255, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170654205399098e-12}, {"id": 869, "seek": 240160, "start": 2414.74, "end": 2416.66, "text": " And finally, pillar number four.", "tokens": [51022, 400, 2721, 11, 27592, 1230, 1451, 13, 51118], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230081483915255, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170654205399098e-12}, {"id": 870, "seek": 240160, "start": 2417.06, "end": 2417.38, "text": " Four.", "tokens": [51138, 7451, 13, 51154], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230081483915255, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170654205399098e-12}, {"id": 871, "seek": 240160, "start": 2417.96, "end": 2421.74, "text": " Time evolution is a strongly continuous unitary group.", "tokens": [51183, 6161, 9303, 307, 257, 10613, 10957, 517, 4109, 1594, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20230081483915255, "compression_ratio": 1.435, "no_speech_prob": 2.1170654205399098e-12}, {"id": 872, "seek": 242174, "start": 2421.74, "end": 2424.1, "text": " Let me focus on the word continuous there.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 385, 1879, 322, 264, 1349, 10957, 456, 13, 50483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19459252241181163, "compression_ratio": 1.541062801932367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245654131496034e-12}, {"id": 873, "seek": 242174, "start": 2424.7799999999997, "end": 2426.18, "text": " Time flows smoothly.", "tokens": [50517, 6161, 12867, 19565, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19459252241181163, "compression_ratio": 1.541062801932367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245654131496034e-12}, {"id": 874, "seek": 242174, "start": 2427.1, "end": 2432.24, "text": " The universe doesn't tick forward in discrete, chunky frames like a 60 frames per second video game.", "tokens": [50633, 440, 6445, 1177, 380, 5204, 2128, 294, 27706, 11, 45392, 12083, 411, 257, 4060, 12083, 680, 1150, 960, 1216, 13, 50890], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19459252241181163, "compression_ratio": 1.541062801932367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245654131496034e-12}, {"id": 875, "seek": 242174, "start": 2432.3599999999997, "end": 2432.62, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50896, 1079, 13, 50909], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19459252241181163, "compression_ratio": 1.541062801932367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245654131496034e-12}, {"id": 876, "seek": 242174, "start": 2432.8999999999996, "end": 2434.4399999999996, "text": " Time is smooth and reversible.", "tokens": [50923, 6161, 307, 5508, 293, 44788, 13, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19459252241181163, "compression_ratio": 1.541062801932367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245654131496034e-12}, {"id": 877, "seek": 242174, "start": 2434.8999999999996, "end": 2441.2799999999997, "text": " And from that assumption of smooth, continuous evolution, the author derives the Schrodinger equation.", "tokens": [51023, 400, 490, 300, 15302, 295, 5508, 11, 10957, 9303, 11, 264, 3793, 1163, 1539, 264, 2065, 340, 3584, 260, 5367, 13, 51342], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19459252241181163, "compression_ratio": 1.541062801932367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245654131496034e-12}, {"id": 878, "seek": 242174, "start": 2441.4399999999996, "end": 2442.0, "text": " Just from that.", "tokens": [51350, 1449, 490, 300, 13, 51378], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19459252241181163, "compression_ratio": 1.541062801932367, "no_speech_prob": 1.5245654131496034e-12}, {"id": 879, "seek": 244200, "start": 2442.0, "end": 2445.84, "text": " And they do it just from a simple, finite-dimensional, ordinary differential equation.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 436, 360, 309, 445, 490, 257, 2199, 11, 19362, 12, 18759, 11, 10547, 15756, 5367, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 880, "seek": 244200, "start": 2445.94, "end": 2450.76, "text": " They don't even need the heavy, infinite-dimensional math usually required in textbooks, like Stone's theorem.", "tokens": [50562, 814, 500, 380, 754, 643, 264, 4676, 11, 13785, 12, 18759, 5221, 2673, 4739, 294, 33587, 11, 411, 15012, 311, 20904, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 881, "seek": 244200, "start": 2451.0, "end": 2451.7, "text": " I have to pause here.", "tokens": [50815, 286, 362, 281, 10465, 510, 13, 50850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 882, "seek": 244200, "start": 2451.9, "end": 2452.54, "text": " That's really it.", "tokens": [50860, 663, 311, 534, 309, 13, 50892], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 883, "seek": 244200, "start": 2452.56, "end": 2453.3, "text": " Just four rules.", "tokens": [50893, 1449, 1451, 4474, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 884, "seek": 244200, "start": 2453.42, "end": 2453.76, "text": " That's it.", "tokens": [50936, 663, 311, 309, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 885, "seek": 244200, "start": 2453.98, "end": 2455.3, "text": " You assume local tomography.", "tokens": [50964, 509, 6552, 2654, 2916, 5820, 13, 51030], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 886, "seek": 244200, "start": 2455.94, "end": 2458.28, "text": " You assume states can be completed into frames.", "tokens": [51062, 509, 6552, 4368, 393, 312, 7365, 666, 12083, 13, 51179], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 887, "seek": 244200, "start": 2458.58, "end": 2460.46, "text": " You use real numbers for your dials.", "tokens": [51194, 509, 764, 957, 3547, 337, 428, 5502, 82, 13, 51288], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 888, "seek": 244200, "start": 2460.78, "end": 2462.46, "text": " And you assume time flows smoothly.", "tokens": [51304, 400, 291, 6552, 565, 12867, 19565, 13, 51388], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 889, "seek": 244200, "start": 2463.02, "end": 2468.82, "text": " And from those four seeds, you grow the entire massive, complex tree of quantum mechanics.", "tokens": [51416, 400, 490, 729, 1451, 9203, 11, 291, 1852, 264, 2302, 5994, 11, 3997, 4230, 295, 13018, 12939, 13, 51706], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 890, "seek": 244200, "start": 2468.9, "end": 2469.32, "text": " You do.", "tokens": [51710, 509, 360, 13, 51731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 891, "seek": 244200, "start": 2469.48, "end": 2470.48, "text": " It scales perfectly.", "tokens": [51739, 467, 17408, 6239, 13, 51789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1657301405785789, "compression_ratio": 1.70926517571885, "no_speech_prob": 1.882962535892929e-12}, {"id": 892, "seek": 247048, "start": 2470.48, "end": 2480.3, "text": " Even highly complex fuzzy measurements, known in physics as POVMs or positive operator-valued measures, emerge naturally.", "tokens": [50365, 2754, 5405, 3997, 34710, 15383, 11, 2570, 294, 10649, 382, 22299, 53, 26386, 420, 3353, 12973, 12, 3337, 5827, 8000, 11, 21511, 8195, 13, 50856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11213969267331637, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 2.227882158270522e-12}, {"id": 893, "seek": 247048, "start": 2480.5, "end": 2482.06, "text": " How do fuzzy measurements fit in?", "tokens": [50866, 1012, 360, 34710, 15383, 3318, 294, 30, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11213969267331637, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 2.227882158270522e-12}, {"id": 894, "seek": 247048, "start": 2482.26, "end": 2485.52, "text": " The text uses a mathematical trick called the Neumark dilation.", "tokens": [50954, 440, 2487, 4960, 257, 18894, 4282, 1219, 264, 1734, 449, 809, 11504, 399, 13, 51117], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11213969267331637, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 2.227882158270522e-12}, {"id": 895, "seek": 247048, "start": 2485.64, "end": 2487.28, "text": " What does a Neumark dilation do?", "tokens": [51123, 708, 775, 257, 1734, 449, 809, 11504, 399, 360, 30, 51205], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11213969267331637, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 2.227882158270522e-12}, {"id": 896, "seek": 247048, "start": 2487.54, "end": 2492.62, "text": " Imagine you are trying to measure a quantum system, but your ruler is blurry.", "tokens": [51218, 11739, 291, 366, 1382, 281, 3481, 257, 13018, 1185, 11, 457, 428, 19661, 307, 37644, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11213969267331637, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 2.227882158270522e-12}, {"id": 897, "seek": 247048, "start": 2492.96, "end": 2494.48, "text": " It's a fuzzy, generalized measurement.", "tokens": [51489, 467, 311, 257, 34710, 11, 44498, 13160, 13, 51565], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11213969267331637, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 2.227882158270522e-12}, {"id": 898, "seek": 247048, "start": 2495.2400000000002, "end": 2496.42, "text": " Okay, I've got a blurry ruler.", "tokens": [51603, 1033, 11, 286, 600, 658, 257, 37644, 19661, 13, 51662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11213969267331637, "compression_ratio": 1.5686274509803921, "no_speech_prob": 2.227882158270522e-12}, {"id": 899, "seek": 249642, "start": 2496.42, "end": 2503.5, "text": " The Neumark dilation proves that any fuzzy measurement is actually just a perfectly sharp, clean measurement happening on a larger system.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 1734, 449, 809, 11504, 399, 25019, 300, 604, 34710, 13160, 307, 767, 445, 257, 6239, 8199, 11, 2541, 13160, 2737, 322, 257, 4833, 1185, 13, 50719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08527523875236512, "compression_ratio": 1.5822784810126582, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232317139736052e-12}, {"id": 900, "seek": 249642, "start": 2503.62, "end": 2504.42, "text": " Oh, that's wild.", "tokens": [50725, 876, 11, 300, 311, 4868, 13, 50765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08527523875236512, "compression_ratio": 1.5822784810126582, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232317139736052e-12}, {"id": 901, "seek": 249642, "start": 2504.56, "end": 2509.62, "text": " You just couple your little system to a larger environment, evolve them smoothly together, and then measure the whole thing sharply.", "tokens": [50772, 509, 445, 1916, 428, 707, 1185, 281, 257, 4833, 2823, 11, 16693, 552, 19565, 1214, 11, 293, 550, 3481, 264, 1379, 551, 42893, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08527523875236512, "compression_ratio": 1.5822784810126582, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232317139736052e-12}, {"id": 902, "seek": 249642, "start": 2509.92, "end": 2513.54, "text": " Everything we observe in quantum labs scales perfectly from those four original seeds.", "tokens": [51040, 5471, 321, 11441, 294, 13018, 20339, 17408, 6239, 490, 729, 1451, 3380, 9203, 13, 51221], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08527523875236512, "compression_ratio": 1.5822784810126582, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232317139736052e-12}, {"id": 903, "seek": 251354, "start": 2513.54, "end": 2523.32, "text": " On one hand, four is an astonishingly small number of assumptions to generate the most successful, most heavily tested physical theory in human history.", "tokens": [50365, 1282, 472, 1011, 11, 1451, 307, 364, 35264, 356, 1359, 1230, 295, 17695, 281, 8460, 264, 881, 4406, 11, 881, 10950, 8246, 4001, 5261, 294, 1952, 2503, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09854826174284283, "compression_ratio": 1.3174603174603174, "no_speech_prob": 1.426922273915776e-12}, {"id": 904, "seek": 251354, "start": 2523.56, "end": 2524.44, "text": " It really is.", "tokens": [50866, 467, 534, 307, 13, 50910], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09854826174284283, "compression_ratio": 1.3174603174603174, "no_speech_prob": 1.426922273915776e-12}, {"id": 905, "seek": 252444, "start": 2524.44, "end": 2528.78, "text": " But, on the other hand, it proves that quantum mechanics isn't inevitable.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 11, 322, 264, 661, 1011, 11, 309, 25019, 300, 13018, 12939, 1943, 380, 21451, 13, 50582], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1267184302920387, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612925890693628e-12}, {"id": 906, "seek": 252444, "start": 2529.26, "end": 2531.56, "text": " It's not the only way the universe could have been programmed.", "tokens": [50606, 467, 311, 406, 264, 787, 636, 264, 6445, 727, 362, 668, 31092, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1267184302920387, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612925890693628e-12}, {"id": 907, "seek": 252444, "start": 2532.18, "end": 2533.56, "text": " It is a specific route.", "tokens": [50752, 467, 307, 257, 2685, 7955, 13, 50821], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1267184302920387, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612925890693628e-12}, {"id": 908, "seek": 252444, "start": 2534.04, "end": 2537.82, "text": " We chose those four assumptions based on how we interact with the world.", "tokens": [50845, 492, 5111, 729, 1451, 17695, 2361, 322, 577, 321, 4648, 365, 264, 1002, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1267184302920387, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612925890693628e-12}, {"id": 909, "seek": 252444, "start": 2538.08, "end": 2541.88, "text": " Which sets us up perfectly for the massive plot twist in the final chapters.", "tokens": [51047, 3013, 6352, 505, 493, 6239, 337, 264, 5994, 7542, 8203, 294, 264, 2572, 20013, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1267184302920387, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612925890693628e-12}, {"id": 910, "seek": 252444, "start": 2542.0, "end": 2543.14, "text": " Yes, the plot twist.", "tokens": [51243, 1079, 11, 264, 7542, 8203, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1267184302920387, "compression_ratio": 1.537037037037037, "no_speech_prob": 1.3612925890693628e-12}, {"id": 911, "seek": 254314, "start": 2543.14, "end": 2553.98, "text": " Just when the book has thoroughly convinced us that complex numbers are absolutely mandatory because they are the only field that passes the local tomography dimension counting test perfectly.", "tokens": [50365, 1449, 562, 264, 1446, 575, 17987, 12561, 505, 300, 3997, 3547, 366, 3122, 22173, 570, 436, 366, 264, 787, 2519, 300, 11335, 264, 2654, 2916, 5820, 10139, 13251, 1500, 6239, 13, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12174705289444833, "compression_ratio": 1.6033333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9961590973921473e-12}, {"id": 912, "seek": 254314, "start": 2554.16, "end": 2555.96, "text": " The author pulls the rug out from under us.", "tokens": [50916, 440, 3793, 16982, 264, 18329, 484, 490, 833, 505, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12174705289444833, "compression_ratio": 1.6033333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9961590973921473e-12}, {"id": 913, "seek": 254314, "start": 2556.02, "end": 2557.0, "text": " A total rug pull.", "tokens": [51009, 316, 3217, 18329, 2235, 13, 51058], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12174705289444833, "compression_ratio": 1.6033333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9961590973921473e-12}, {"id": 914, "seek": 254314, "start": 2557.48, "end": 2564.12, "text": " Because they cite groundbreaking new research published right around the same time in 2025 and 2026.", "tokens": [51082, 1436, 436, 37771, 42491, 777, 2132, 6572, 558, 926, 264, 912, 565, 294, 39209, 293, 945, 10880, 13, 51414], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12174705289444833, "compression_ratio": 1.6033333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9961590973921473e-12}, {"id": 915, "seek": 254314, "start": 2564.52, "end": 2565.64, "text": " Let's talk about those papers.", "tokens": [51434, 961, 311, 751, 466, 729, 10577, 13, 51490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12174705289444833, "compression_ratio": 1.6033333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9961590973921473e-12}, {"id": 916, "seek": 254314, "start": 2565.8799999999997, "end": 2571.1, "text": " There are papers by Haforman and Woods and another major paper by Barrios Hita and colleagues.", "tokens": [51502, 821, 366, 10577, 538, 4064, 837, 282, 293, 31559, 293, 1071, 2563, 3035, 538, 4156, 37994, 389, 2786, 293, 7734, 13, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12174705289444833, "compression_ratio": 1.6033333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.9961590973921473e-12}, {"id": 917, "seek": 257110, "start": 2571.1, "end": 2575.52, "text": " These papers attack the very foundation of the local tomography dimension counting.", "tokens": [50365, 1981, 10577, 2690, 264, 588, 7030, 295, 264, 2654, 2916, 5820, 10139, 13251, 13, 50586], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 918, "seek": 257110, "start": 2576.04, "end": 2576.06, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50612, 1033, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 919, "seek": 257110, "start": 2576.22, "end": 2579.16, "text": " They target the mathematical grammar we use to count the parameters.", "tokens": [50621, 814, 3779, 264, 18894, 22317, 321, 764, 281, 1207, 264, 9834, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 920, "seek": 257110, "start": 2579.48, "end": 2581.24, "text": " They target the Kronecker product.", "tokens": [50784, 814, 3779, 264, 6332, 546, 9178, 1674, 13, 50872], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 921, "seek": 257110, "start": 2581.56, "end": 2582.5, "text": " The Kronecker product.", "tokens": [50888, 440, 6332, 546, 9178, 1674, 13, 50935], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 922, "seek": 257110, "start": 2582.8199999999997, "end": 2583.08, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50951, 1033, 13, 50964], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 923, "seek": 257110, "start": 2583.2599999999998, "end": 2583.7599999999998, "text": " Let me review.", "tokens": [50973, 961, 385, 3131, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 924, "seek": 257110, "start": 2584.38, "end": 2593.46, "text": " When we were counting dimensions earlier, when we said four parameters times four parameters equals 16 for complex numbers, or three times three equals nine for real numbers,", "tokens": [51029, 1133, 321, 645, 13251, 12819, 3071, 11, 562, 321, 848, 1451, 9834, 1413, 1451, 9834, 6915, 3165, 337, 3997, 3547, 11, 420, 1045, 1413, 1045, 6915, 4949, 337, 957, 3547, 11, 51483], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 925, "seek": 257110, "start": 2593.7, "end": 2600.2, "text": " we assumed a specific mathematical rule for how you multiply those matrices together to combine the systems.", "tokens": [51495, 321, 15895, 257, 2685, 18894, 4978, 337, 577, 291, 12972, 729, 32284, 1214, 281, 10432, 264, 3652, 13, 51820], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 926, "seek": 257110, "start": 2600.2, "end": 2600.62, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51820, 1079, 13, 51841], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1844523879122143, "compression_ratio": 1.8586572438162545, "no_speech_prob": 1.3996698765283977e-12}, {"id": 927, "seek": 260062, "start": 2600.62, "end": 2602.9, "text": " That rule is the Kronecker product.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 4978, 307, 264, 6332, 546, 9178, 1674, 13, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 928, "seek": 260062, "start": 2603.24, "end": 2605.18, "text": " We assumed it because it is standard.", "tokens": [50496, 492, 15895, 309, 570, 309, 307, 3832, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 929, "seek": 260062, "start": 2605.42, "end": 2607.66, "text": " It is the default grammar of quantum mechanics.", "tokens": [50605, 467, 307, 264, 7576, 22317, 295, 13018, 12939, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 930, "seek": 260062, "start": 2607.94, "end": 2609.06, "text": " But it is an assumption.", "tokens": [50731, 583, 309, 307, 364, 15302, 13, 50787], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 931, "seek": 260062, "start": 2609.38, "end": 2610.5, "text": " It's a choice of representation.", "tokens": [50803, 467, 311, 257, 3922, 295, 10290, 13, 50859], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 932, "seek": 260062, "start": 2610.94, "end": 2611.22, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50881, 1033, 13, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 933, "seek": 260062, "start": 2611.5, "end": 2616.2799999999997, "text": " What these 2025 and 2026 papers show is that if you change the composition rule,", "tokens": [50909, 708, 613, 39209, 293, 945, 10880, 10577, 855, 307, 300, 498, 291, 1319, 264, 12686, 4978, 11, 51148], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 934, "seek": 260062, "start": 2617.1, "end": 2620.74, "text": " you change the mathematical grammar of how two systems combine on paper,", "tokens": [51189, 291, 1319, 264, 18894, 22317, 295, 577, 732, 3652, 10432, 322, 3035, 11, 51371], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 935, "seek": 260062, "start": 2621.52, "end": 2624.64, "text": " you can completely circumvent the failure of real numbers.", "tokens": [51410, 291, 393, 2584, 7125, 2475, 264, 7763, 295, 957, 3547, 13, 51566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 936, "seek": 260062, "start": 2624.8599999999997, "end": 2626.46, "text": " Let me make sure I'm wrapping my head around this.", "tokens": [51577, 961, 385, 652, 988, 286, 478, 21993, 452, 1378, 926, 341, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 937, "seek": 260062, "start": 2626.54, "end": 2627.74, "text": " You don't change the physics.", "tokens": [51661, 509, 500, 380, 1319, 264, 10649, 13, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 938, "seek": 260062, "start": 2627.92, "end": 2629.14, "text": " You don't change the particles.", "tokens": [51730, 509, 500, 380, 1319, 264, 10007, 13, 51791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1816174379035608, "compression_ratio": 1.7147651006711409, "no_speech_prob": 1.6234922477556535e-12}, {"id": 939, "seek": 262914, "start": 2629.14, "end": 2629.46, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50365, 883, 13, 50381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24054065243951206, "compression_ratio": 1.108695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.9084935454910523e-12}, {"id": 940, "seek": 262914, "start": 2629.46, "end": 2633.18, "text": " You just change the arithmetic rule for how you multiply the matrices on your chalkboard.", "tokens": [50381, 509, 445, 1319, 264, 42973, 4978, 337, 577, 291, 12972, 264, 32284, 322, 428, 28660, 3787, 13, 50567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24054065243951206, "compression_ratio": 1.108695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.9084935454910523e-12}, {"id": 941, "seek": 262914, "start": 2633.2599999999998, "end": 2633.7, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50571, 7587, 13, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.24054065243951206, "compression_ratio": 1.108695652173913, "no_speech_prob": 1.9084935454910523e-12}, {"id": 942, "seek": 263370, "start": 2633.7, "end": 2638.2599999999998, "text": " Specifically, they introduce a different tensor product, denoted with a little r,", "tokens": [50365, 26058, 11, 436, 5366, 257, 819, 40863, 1674, 11, 1441, 23325, 365, 257, 707, 367, 11, 50593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14311883666298605, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.399328894945151e-12}, {"id": 943, "seek": 263370, "start": 2638.2599999999998, "end": 2641.2599999999998, "text": " that mathematically quotients out what's known as phase redistribution.", "tokens": [50593, 300, 44003, 9641, 2448, 484, 437, 311, 2570, 382, 5574, 36198, 30783, 13, 50743], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14311883666298605, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.399328894945151e-12}, {"id": 944, "seek": 263370, "start": 2642.06, "end": 2643.4199999999996, "text": " Let's break down phase redistribution.", "tokens": [50783, 961, 311, 1821, 760, 5574, 36198, 30783, 13, 50851], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14311883666298605, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.399328894945151e-12}, {"id": 945, "seek": 263370, "start": 2643.8199999999997, "end": 2649.96, "text": " In complex quantum mechanics, a global phase, a sort of overall mathematical shift in the wave,", "tokens": [50871, 682, 3997, 13018, 12939, 11, 257, 4338, 5574, 11, 257, 1333, 295, 4787, 18894, 5513, 294, 264, 5772, 11, 51178], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14311883666298605, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.399328894945151e-12}, {"id": 946, "seek": 263370, "start": 2650.1, "end": 2656.6, "text": " can be arbitrarily assigned to particle A or particle B without changing any of the observable physics.", "tokens": [51185, 393, 312, 19071, 3289, 13279, 281, 12359, 316, 420, 12359, 363, 1553, 4473, 604, 295, 264, 9951, 712, 10649, 13, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14311883666298605, "compression_ratio": 1.6198347107438016, "no_speech_prob": 1.399328894945151e-12}, {"id": 947, "seek": 265660, "start": 2656.6, "end": 2657.04, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19119866286651999, "compression_ratio": 1.5345622119815667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610619351000277e-12}, {"id": 948, "seek": 265660, "start": 2657.16, "end": 2657.7799999999997, "text": " It's ambiguous.", "tokens": [50393, 467, 311, 39465, 13, 50424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19119866286651999, "compression_ratio": 1.5345622119815667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610619351000277e-12}, {"id": 949, "seek": 265660, "start": 2658.06, "end": 2663.64, "text": " The standard Kronecker product, when forced to use real numbers, gets horribly tangled up by this ambiguity.", "tokens": [50438, 440, 3832, 6332, 546, 9178, 1674, 11, 562, 7579, 281, 764, 957, 3547, 11, 2170, 45028, 47192, 493, 538, 341, 46519, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19119866286651999, "compression_ratio": 1.5345622119815667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610619351000277e-12}, {"id": 950, "seek": 265660, "start": 2663.98, "end": 2667.2, "text": " It creates phantom mathematical dimensions to account for it,", "tokens": [50734, 467, 7829, 903, 25796, 18894, 12819, 281, 2696, 337, 309, 11, 50895], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19119866286651999, "compression_ratio": 1.5345622119815667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610619351000277e-12}, {"id": 951, "seek": 265660, "start": 2667.24, "end": 2671.04, "text": " which is exactly why we ended up with 10 dimensions instead of 9 earlier.", "tokens": [50897, 597, 307, 2293, 983, 321, 4590, 493, 365, 1266, 12819, 2602, 295, 1722, 3071, 13, 51087], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19119866286651999, "compression_ratio": 1.5345622119815667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610619351000277e-12}, {"id": 952, "seek": 265660, "start": 2671.3199999999997, "end": 2674.38, "text": " The grammar was creating dimensions that didn't physically exist.", "tokens": [51101, 440, 22317, 390, 4084, 12819, 300, 994, 380, 9762, 2514, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19119866286651999, "compression_ratio": 1.5345622119815667, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610619351000277e-12}, {"id": 953, "seek": 267438, "start": 2674.38, "end": 2675.98, "text": " It's like the new grammar fixes it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 411, 264, 777, 22317, 32539, 309, 13, 50445], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18518944309182364, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 2.1503948795242867e-12}, {"id": 954, "seek": 267438, "start": 2675.98, "end": 2681.92, "text": " If you quotient out that ambiguity mathematically, if you tell the math to ignore that phase shift,", "tokens": [50445, 759, 291, 9641, 1196, 484, 300, 46519, 44003, 11, 498, 291, 980, 264, 5221, 281, 11200, 300, 5574, 5513, 11, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18518944309182364, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 2.1503948795242867e-12}, {"id": 955, "seek": 267438, "start": 2682.12, "end": 2685.6800000000003, "text": " you can reproduce all of quantum mechanics using only real numbers.", "tokens": [50752, 291, 393, 29501, 439, 295, 13018, 12939, 1228, 787, 957, 3547, 13, 50930], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18518944309182364, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 2.1503948795242867e-12}, {"id": 956, "seek": 267438, "start": 2685.84, "end": 2686.1400000000003, "text": " All of it.", "tokens": [50938, 1057, 295, 309, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18518944309182364, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 2.1503948795242867e-12}, {"id": 957, "seek": 267438, "start": 2686.4, "end": 2693.12, "text": " Every single empirical prediction, every experiment, replicated perfectly without a single imaginary eye.", "tokens": [50966, 2048, 2167, 31886, 17630, 11, 633, 5120, 11, 46365, 6239, 1553, 257, 2167, 26164, 3313, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18518944309182364, "compression_ratio": 1.5311004784688995, "no_speech_prob": 2.1503948795242867e-12}, {"id": 958, "seek": 269312, "start": 2693.12, "end": 2697.48, "text": " So wait, we can build the universe with real numbers after all.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 1699, 11, 321, 393, 1322, 264, 6445, 365, 957, 3547, 934, 439, 13, 50583], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 959, "seek": 269312, "start": 2697.64, "end": 2698.2799999999997, "text": " We can.", "tokens": [50591, 492, 393, 13, 50623], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 960, "seek": 269312, "start": 2698.74, "end": 2701.54, "text": " If that's true, then why on earth do we use complex numbers?", "tokens": [50646, 759, 300, 311, 2074, 11, 550, 983, 322, 4120, 360, 321, 764, 3997, 3547, 30, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 961, "seek": 269312, "start": 2701.98, "end": 2705.3599999999997, "text": " Where does the imaginary eye come from if reality doesn't actually need it?", "tokens": [50808, 2305, 775, 264, 26164, 3313, 808, 490, 498, 4103, 1177, 380, 767, 643, 309, 30, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 962, "seek": 269312, "start": 2705.5, "end": 2707.5, "text": " This is perhaps my favorite part of the entire text.", "tokens": [50984, 639, 307, 4317, 452, 2954, 644, 295, 264, 2302, 2487, 13, 51084], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 963, "seek": 269312, "start": 2707.6, "end": 2709.04, "text": " This is where we talk about the Amplitwist.", "tokens": [51089, 639, 307, 689, 321, 751, 466, 264, 2012, 564, 270, 86, 468, 13, 51161], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 964, "seek": 269312, "start": 2709.3399999999997, "end": 2710.46, "text": " The Amplitwist.", "tokens": [51176, 440, 2012, 564, 270, 86, 468, 13, 51232], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 965, "seek": 269312, "start": 2710.9, "end": 2713.16, "text": " That sounds like a 1960s dance move.", "tokens": [51254, 663, 3263, 411, 257, 16157, 82, 4489, 1286, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 966, "seek": 269312, "start": 2713.3599999999997, "end": 2718.38, "text": " It does, but the author cites Tristan Needham's work on visual complex analysis.", "tokens": [51377, 467, 775, 11, 457, 264, 3793, 269, 3324, 1765, 7559, 16984, 4822, 311, 589, 322, 5056, 3997, 5215, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 967, "seek": 269312, "start": 2719.2599999999998, "end": 2720.7599999999998, "text": " What is a complex number, really?", "tokens": [51672, 708, 307, 257, 3997, 1230, 11, 534, 30, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15715094173655791, "compression_ratio": 1.6423611111111112, "no_speech_prob": 2.1256787562790036e-12}, {"id": 968, "seek": 272076, "start": 2720.76, "end": 2722.9, "text": " We get so hung up on the word imaginary.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 483, 370, 5753, 493, 322, 264, 1349, 26164, 13, 50472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 969, "seek": 272076, "start": 2723.2200000000003, "end": 2724.0200000000004, "text": " It sounds so mystical.", "tokens": [50488, 467, 3263, 370, 40565, 13, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 970, "seek": 272076, "start": 2724.42, "end": 2727.98, "text": " But multiplication by eye isn't some mystical ghostly process.", "tokens": [50548, 583, 27290, 538, 3313, 1943, 380, 512, 40565, 8359, 356, 1399, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 971, "seek": 272076, "start": 2728.5200000000004, "end": 2731.9, "text": " Geometrically, it is simply simultaneous scaling and rotation.", "tokens": [50753, 2876, 649, 81, 984, 11, 309, 307, 2935, 46218, 21589, 293, 12447, 13, 50922], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 972, "seek": 272076, "start": 2732.34, "end": 2733.5400000000004, "text": " It is an Amplitwist.", "tokens": [50944, 467, 307, 364, 2012, 564, 270, 86, 468, 13, 51004], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 973, "seek": 272076, "start": 2733.6600000000003, "end": 2734.7200000000003, "text": " Scaling and rotation.", "tokens": [51010, 2747, 4270, 293, 12447, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 974, "seek": 272076, "start": 2735.34, "end": 2736.94, "text": " Stretching a vector and twisting it.", "tokens": [51094, 38817, 278, 257, 8062, 293, 34491, 309, 13, 51174], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 975, "seek": 272076, "start": 2737.0, "end": 2738.88, "text": " Think back to the invisible matrix J.", "tokens": [51177, 6557, 646, 281, 264, 14603, 8141, 508, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 976, "seek": 272076, "start": 2739.46, "end": 2745.6200000000003, "text": " The quarter turn, 90 degree rotation matrix that was hiding inside the invisible real dimension J tensor J.", "tokens": [51300, 440, 6555, 1261, 11, 4289, 4314, 12447, 8141, 300, 390, 10596, 1854, 264, 14603, 957, 10139, 508, 40863, 508, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 977, "seek": 272076, "start": 2745.78, "end": 2747.44, "text": " Yeah, the one that acts exactly like eye,", "tokens": [51616, 865, 11, 264, 472, 300, 10672, 2293, 411, 3313, 11, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1353107514928599, "compression_ratio": 1.6863468634686347, "no_speech_prob": 1.3145446103174363e-12}, {"id": 978, "seek": 274744, "start": 2747.44, "end": 2751.28, "text": " because rotating 90 degrees twice points you backward to negative one.", "tokens": [50365, 570, 19627, 4289, 5310, 6091, 2793, 291, 23897, 281, 3671, 472, 13, 50557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17882412471128314, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 979, "seek": 274744, "start": 2751.6, "end": 2753.96, "text": " The text proves that J literally is eye.", "tokens": [50573, 440, 2487, 25019, 300, 508, 3736, 307, 3313, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17882412471128314, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 980, "seek": 274744, "start": 2754.28, "end": 2757.86, "text": " They are identical geometric operations just written in different fonts.", "tokens": [50707, 814, 366, 14800, 33246, 7705, 445, 3720, 294, 819, 35316, 13, 50886], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17882412471128314, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 981, "seek": 274744, "start": 2758.08, "end": 2758.3, "text": " Wow.", "tokens": [50897, 3153, 13, 50908], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17882412471128314, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 982, "seek": 274744, "start": 2758.42, "end": 2760.54, "text": " Complex numbers are not magical entities.", "tokens": [50914, 41184, 3547, 366, 406, 12066, 16667, 13, 51020], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17882412471128314, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 983, "seek": 274744, "start": 2760.9, "end": 2766.88, "text": " They are just a highly efficient compressed bookkeeping tool for real-world geometric twists and rotations in a plane.", "tokens": [51038, 814, 366, 445, 257, 5405, 7148, 30353, 1446, 25769, 2290, 337, 957, 12, 13217, 33246, 35290, 293, 44796, 294, 257, 5720, 13, 51337], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17882412471128314, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 984, "seek": 274744, "start": 2767.08, "end": 2769.96, "text": " Here is where it gets incredibly profound to me.", "tokens": [51347, 1692, 307, 689, 309, 2170, 6252, 14382, 281, 385, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17882412471128314, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6617229510809683e-12}, {"id": 985, "seek": 276996, "start": 2769.96, "end": 2774.12, "text": " The author isn't invalidating their own earlier proofs.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 1943, 380, 34702, 990, 641, 1065, 3071, 8177, 82, 13, 50573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15783953415720087, "compression_ratio": 1.5730337078651686, "no_speech_prob": 2.635317094754064e-12}, {"id": 986, "seek": 276996, "start": 2774.2200000000003, "end": 2774.92, "text": " No, not at all.", "tokens": [50578, 883, 11, 406, 412, 439, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15783953415720087, "compression_ratio": 1.5730337078651686, "no_speech_prob": 2.635317094754064e-12}, {"id": 987, "seek": 276996, "start": 2775.08, "end": 2778.02, "text": " They prove that real numbers fail under the Kronecker representation.", "tokens": [50621, 814, 7081, 300, 957, 3547, 3061, 833, 264, 6332, 546, 9178, 10290, 13, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15783953415720087, "compression_ratio": 1.5730337078651686, "no_speech_prob": 2.635317094754064e-12}, {"id": 988, "seek": 276996, "start": 2778.7200000000003, "end": 2782.98, "text": " But by showing that changing the grammar fixes the problem, they prove something deeper.", "tokens": [50803, 583, 538, 4099, 300, 4473, 264, 22317, 32539, 264, 1154, 11, 436, 7081, 746, 7731, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15783953415720087, "compression_ratio": 1.5730337078651686, "no_speech_prob": 2.635317094754064e-12}, {"id": 989, "seek": 276996, "start": 2783.7, "end": 2787.36, "text": " Complex numbers aren't a mystical requirement handed down by the universe.", "tokens": [51052, 41184, 3547, 3212, 380, 257, 40565, 11695, 16013, 760, 538, 264, 6445, 13, 51235], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15783953415720087, "compression_ratio": 1.5730337078651686, "no_speech_prob": 2.635317094754064e-12}, {"id": 990, "seek": 276996, "start": 2787.5, "end": 2787.94, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51242, 7587, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15783953415720087, "compression_ratio": 1.5730337078651686, "no_speech_prob": 2.635317094754064e-12}, {"id": 991, "seek": 276996, "start": 2788.1, "end": 2793.68, "text": " They are just the most efficient human language for describing a universe that involves geometric twists.", "tokens": [51272, 814, 366, 445, 264, 881, 7148, 1952, 2856, 337, 16141, 257, 6445, 300, 11626, 33246, 35290, 13, 51551], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15783953415720087, "compression_ratio": 1.5730337078651686, "no_speech_prob": 2.635317094754064e-12}, {"id": 992, "seek": 279368, "start": 2793.68, "end": 2794.44, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 50403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20416668483189174, "compression_ratio": 1.4734299516908214, "no_speech_prob": 2.1499405988140152e-12}, {"id": 993, "seek": 279368, "start": 2794.8399999999997, "end": 2797.2, "text": " The ambiguity isn't destroyed by the new math.", "tokens": [50423, 440, 46519, 1943, 380, 8937, 538, 264, 777, 5221, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20416668483189174, "compression_ratio": 1.4734299516908214, "no_speech_prob": 2.1499405988140152e-12}, {"id": 994, "seek": 279368, "start": 2797.44, "end": 2798.66, "text": " It's just reorganized.", "tokens": [50553, 467, 311, 445, 41203, 1602, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20416668483189174, "compression_ratio": 1.4734299516908214, "no_speech_prob": 2.1499405988140152e-12}, {"id": 995, "seek": 279368, "start": 2799.08, "end": 2802.8399999999997, "text": " The structure of reality is perfectly preserved, but our lens shifts.", "tokens": [50635, 440, 3877, 295, 4103, 307, 6239, 22242, 11, 457, 527, 6765, 19201, 13, 50823], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20416668483189174, "compression_ratio": 1.4734299516908214, "no_speech_prob": 2.1499405988140152e-12}, {"id": 996, "seek": 279368, "start": 2803.08, "end": 2807.66, "text": " Okay, so if real numbers can be salvaged with a twist, it makes me wonder about going up.", "tokens": [50835, 1033, 11, 370, 498, 957, 3547, 393, 312, 26858, 2980, 365, 257, 8203, 11, 309, 1669, 385, 2441, 466, 516, 493, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20416668483189174, "compression_ratio": 1.4734299516908214, "no_speech_prob": 2.1499405988140152e-12}, {"id": 997, "seek": 279368, "start": 2807.94, "end": 2809.8399999999997, "text": " What about pushing to higher dimensions?", "tokens": [51078, 708, 466, 7380, 281, 2946, 12819, 30, 51173], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20416668483189174, "compression_ratio": 1.4734299516908214, "no_speech_prob": 2.1499405988140152e-12}, {"id": 998, "seek": 279368, "start": 2809.96, "end": 2810.8799999999997, "text": " What about quaternions?", "tokens": [51179, 708, 466, 421, 771, 77, 626, 30, 51225], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20416668483189174, "compression_ratio": 1.4734299516908214, "no_speech_prob": 2.1499405988140152e-12}, {"id": 999, "seek": 281088, "start": 2810.88, "end": 2818.2000000000003, "text": " If real numbers are 1D lines and complex numbers are 2D planes, quaternions are 4D hypercomplex numbers.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 957, 3547, 366, 502, 35, 3876, 293, 3997, 3547, 366, 568, 35, 14952, 11, 421, 771, 77, 626, 366, 1017, 35, 9848, 1112, 18945, 3547, 13, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11069680750370026, "compression_ratio": 1.6718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.012250826036177e-12}, {"id": 1000, "seek": 281088, "start": 2818.32, "end": 2819.1800000000003, "text": " 4D numbers, okay.", "tokens": [50737, 1017, 35, 3547, 11, 1392, 13, 50780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11069680750370026, "compression_ratio": 1.6718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.012250826036177e-12}, {"id": 1001, "seek": 281088, "start": 2819.2400000000002, "end": 2822.6800000000003, "text": " They have three separate imaginary axes, I, J, and K.", "tokens": [50783, 814, 362, 1045, 4994, 26164, 35387, 11, 286, 11, 508, 11, 293, 591, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11069680750370026, "compression_ratio": 1.6718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.012250826036177e-12}, {"id": 1002, "seek": 281088, "start": 2822.9, "end": 2828.7000000000003, "text": " It's entirely natural to wonder, if we can go from real to complex, do we need to go to quaternions?", "tokens": [50966, 467, 311, 7696, 3303, 281, 2441, 11, 498, 321, 393, 352, 490, 957, 281, 3997, 11, 360, 321, 643, 281, 352, 281, 421, 771, 77, 626, 30, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11069680750370026, "compression_ratio": 1.6718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.012250826036177e-12}, {"id": 1003, "seek": 281088, "start": 2829.1600000000003, "end": 2831.08, "text": " Could the universe actually be quaternionic?", "tokens": [51279, 7497, 264, 6445, 767, 312, 421, 771, 77, 313, 299, 30, 51375], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11069680750370026, "compression_ratio": 1.6718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.012250826036177e-12}, {"id": 1004, "seek": 281088, "start": 2831.2400000000002, "end": 2834.32, "text": " So we test quaternions using the same graph machinery from earlier.", "tokens": [51383, 407, 321, 1500, 421, 771, 77, 626, 1228, 264, 912, 4295, 27302, 490, 3071, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11069680750370026, "compression_ratio": 1.6718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.012250826036177e-12}, {"id": 1005, "seek": 281088, "start": 2834.56, "end": 2836.62, "text": " We build Escher stairs out of quaternions.", "tokens": [51549, 492, 1322, 2313, 6759, 13471, 484, 295, 421, 771, 77, 626, 13, 51652], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11069680750370026, "compression_ratio": 1.6718146718146718, "no_speech_prob": 2.012250826036177e-12}, {"id": 1006, "seek": 283662, "start": 2836.62, "end": 2841.68, "text": " We could, but the text notes a sudden, fascinating collapse in the math at higher dimensions.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 727, 11, 457, 264, 2487, 5570, 257, 3990, 11, 10343, 15584, 294, 264, 5221, 412, 2946, 12819, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09221206846691313, "compression_ratio": 1.6323529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.4550612234195959e-12}, {"id": 1007, "seek": 283662, "start": 2842.3399999999997, "end": 2849.2999999999997, "text": " Remember how real numbers safely handled a single matrix at D equals 2 and only failed when we built a triangle loop?", "tokens": [50651, 5459, 577, 957, 3547, 11750, 18033, 257, 2167, 8141, 412, 413, 6915, 568, 293, 787, 7612, 562, 321, 3094, 257, 13369, 6367, 30, 50999], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09221206846691313, "compression_ratio": 1.6323529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.4550612234195959e-12}, {"id": 1008, "seek": 283662, "start": 2849.4, "end": 2851.22, "text": " Yeah, the single coin flip was safe.", "tokens": [51004, 865, 11, 264, 2167, 11464, 7929, 390, 3273, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09221206846691313, "compression_ratio": 1.6323529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.4550612234195959e-12}, {"id": 1009, "seek": 283662, "start": 2851.3399999999997, "end": 2856.02, "text": " For any dimension 3 or higher, the minimal witness graph collapses to 0.", "tokens": [51101, 1171, 604, 10139, 805, 420, 2946, 11, 264, 13206, 7286, 4295, 48765, 281, 1958, 13, 51335], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09221206846691313, "compression_ratio": 1.6323529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.4550612234195959e-12}, {"id": 1010, "seek": 283662, "start": 2856.16, "end": 2857.2, "text": " You don't even need a cycle.", "tokens": [51342, 509, 500, 380, 754, 643, 257, 6586, 13, 51394], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09221206846691313, "compression_ratio": 1.6323529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.4550612234195959e-12}, {"id": 1011, "seek": 283662, "start": 2857.46, "end": 2863.3399999999997, "text": " A single isolated edge, a single measurement context is enough to separate real from complex.", "tokens": [51407, 316, 2167, 14621, 4691, 11, 257, 2167, 13160, 4319, 307, 1547, 281, 4994, 957, 490, 3997, 13, 51701], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09221206846691313, "compression_ratio": 1.6323529411764706, "no_speech_prob": 1.4550612234195959e-12}, {"id": 1012, "seek": 286334, "start": 2863.34, "end": 2869.92, "text": " Because of that Fourier transform matrix we talked about, the 3x3 Hadamard impossibility, it fails on a single edge.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 295, 300, 36810, 4088, 8141, 321, 2825, 466, 11, 264, 805, 87, 18, 12298, 335, 515, 38802, 2841, 11, 309, 18199, 322, 257, 2167, 4691, 13, 50694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12135818412712028, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 1013, "seek": 286334, "start": 2870.02, "end": 2870.34, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50699, 7587, 13, 50715], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12135818412712028, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 1014, "seek": 286334, "start": 2870.6200000000003, "end": 2876.06, "text": " So the graph cycle machinery isn't actually needed to break real numbers at higher dimensions.", "tokens": [50729, 407, 264, 4295, 6586, 27302, 1943, 380, 767, 2978, 281, 1821, 957, 3547, 412, 2946, 12819, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12135818412712028, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 1015, "seek": 286334, "start": 2876.28, "end": 2876.5, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51012, 1033, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12135818412712028, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 1016, "seek": 286334, "start": 2876.7000000000003, "end": 2881.6000000000004, "text": " But it might be exactly what we need to break complex numbers and prove quaternions are necessary.", "tokens": [51033, 583, 309, 1062, 312, 2293, 437, 321, 643, 281, 1821, 3997, 3547, 293, 7081, 421, 771, 77, 626, 366, 4818, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12135818412712028, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 1017, "seek": 286334, "start": 2881.84, "end": 2884.0, "text": " So the author asks a fundamental question.", "tokens": [51290, 407, 264, 3793, 8962, 257, 8088, 1168, 13, 51398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12135818412712028, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 1018, "seek": 286334, "start": 2884.76, "end": 2890.6400000000003, "text": " Can quaternions mathematically support even more mutually unbiased bases than complex numbers?", "tokens": [51436, 1664, 421, 771, 77, 626, 44003, 1406, 754, 544, 39144, 517, 5614, 1937, 17949, 813, 3997, 3547, 30, 51730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12135818412712028, "compression_ratio": 1.630281690140845, "no_speech_prob": 1.519184626187775e-12}, {"id": 1019, "seek": 289064, "start": 2890.64, "end": 2894.7599999999998, "text": " We know complex numbers max out at D plus 1 mutually unbiased bases.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 458, 3997, 3547, 11469, 484, 412, 413, 1804, 502, 39144, 517, 5614, 1937, 17949, 13, 50571], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1020, "seek": 289064, "start": 2895.06, "end": 2897.7, "text": " For a two-dimensional cribbit, you can have three MEB.", "tokens": [50586, 1171, 257, 732, 12, 18759, 47163, 5260, 11, 291, 393, 362, 1045, 12003, 33, 13, 50718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1021, "seek": 289064, "start": 2897.7799999999997, "end": 2898.04, "text": " Nice.", "tokens": [50722, 5490, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1022, "seek": 289064, "start": 2898.2799999999997, "end": 2902.2, "text": " For example, measuring spin along the x-axis, the y-axis, and the z-axis.", "tokens": [50747, 1171, 1365, 11, 13389, 6060, 2051, 264, 2031, 12, 24633, 11, 264, 288, 12, 24633, 11, 293, 264, 710, 12, 24633, 13, 50943], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1023, "seek": 289064, "start": 2902.48, "end": 2906.7599999999998, "text": " You can't fit a fourth mutually unbiased measurement into a 2D complex system.", "tokens": [50957, 509, 393, 380, 3318, 257, 6409, 39144, 517, 5614, 1937, 13160, 666, 257, 568, 35, 3997, 1185, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1024, "seek": 289064, "start": 2906.94, "end": 2907.2999999999997, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51180, 1779, 13, 51198], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1025, "seek": 289064, "start": 2907.7599999999998, "end": 2911.42, "text": " But calculating this limit for quaternions is incredibly difficult.", "tokens": [51221, 583, 28258, 341, 4948, 337, 421, 771, 77, 626, 307, 6252, 2252, 13, 51404], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1026, "seek": 289064, "start": 2911.7799999999997, "end": 2913.46, "text": " The math is fraught with traps.", "tokens": [51422, 440, 5221, 307, 6600, 1599, 365, 24173, 13, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1027, "seek": 289064, "start": 2913.66, "end": 2914.2799999999997, "text": " What kind of traps?", "tokens": [51516, 708, 733, 295, 24173, 30, 51547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1028, "seek": 289064, "start": 2914.4, "end": 2917.8799999999997, "text": " The author highlights two specific traps that usually ruin these calculations.", "tokens": [51553, 440, 3793, 14254, 732, 2685, 24173, 300, 2673, 15514, 613, 20448, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1682615774649161, "compression_ratio": 1.605263157894737, "no_speech_prob": 1.3722608119270951e-12}, {"id": 1029, "seek": 291788, "start": 2917.88, "end": 2920.48, "text": " First, the phase freedom.", "tokens": [50365, 2386, 11, 264, 5574, 5645, 13, 50495], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1030, "seek": 291788, "start": 2920.7200000000003, "end": 2920.96, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50507, 1033, 13, 50519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1031, "seek": 291788, "start": 2921.26, "end": 2926.3, "text": " In complex numbers, you can shift the phase of a quantum state in a 1D circle, mathematically", "tokens": [50534, 682, 3997, 3547, 11, 291, 393, 5513, 264, 5574, 295, 257, 13018, 1785, 294, 257, 502, 35, 6329, 11, 44003, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1032, "seek": 291788, "start": 2926.3, "end": 2927.7200000000003, "text": " denoted as U1.", "tokens": [50786, 1441, 23325, 382, 624, 16, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1033, "seek": 291788, "start": 2927.94, "end": 2930.5, "text": " But in quaternions, the phase freedom isn't a circle.", "tokens": [50868, 583, 294, 421, 771, 77, 626, 11, 264, 5574, 5645, 1943, 380, 257, 6329, 13, 50996], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1034, "seek": 291788, "start": 2930.84, "end": 2932.84, "text": " It's a 3D sphere, SP1.", "tokens": [51013, 467, 311, 257, 805, 35, 16687, 11, 8420, 16, 13, 51113], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1035, "seek": 291788, "start": 2932.9, "end": 2934.26, "text": " A 3D sphere of phase.", "tokens": [51116, 316, 805, 35, 16687, 295, 5574, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1036, "seek": 291788, "start": 2934.38, "end": 2937.06, "text": " You can shift the phase in three different directions simultaneously.", "tokens": [51190, 509, 393, 5513, 264, 5574, 294, 1045, 819, 11095, 16561, 13, 51324], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1037, "seek": 291788, "start": 2937.44, "end": 2939.08, "text": " That sounds like an accounting nightmare.", "tokens": [51343, 663, 3263, 411, 364, 19163, 18724, 13, 51425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1038, "seek": 291788, "start": 2939.2400000000002, "end": 2939.98, "text": " It is a total nightmare.", "tokens": [51433, 467, 307, 257, 3217, 18724, 13, 51470], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1039, "seek": 291788, "start": 2940.1400000000003, "end": 2941.92, "text": " And the second trap is the trace.", "tokens": [51478, 400, 264, 1150, 11487, 307, 264, 13508, 13, 51567], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1040, "seek": 291788, "start": 2942.06, "end": 2942.5, "text": " The trace.", "tokens": [51574, 440, 13508, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1041, "seek": 291788, "start": 2942.6800000000003, "end": 2945.46, "text": " Like the sum of the numbers along the diagonal of a matrix.", "tokens": [51605, 1743, 264, 2408, 295, 264, 3547, 2051, 264, 21539, 295, 257, 8141, 13, 51744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19061224225541235, "compression_ratio": 1.7117437722419928, "no_speech_prob": 1.5671669691130763e-12}, {"id": 1042, "seek": 294546, "start": 2945.46, "end": 2945.86, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50385], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.136132487544307, "compression_ratio": 1.6491228070175439, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490748011242172e-12}, {"id": 1043, "seek": 294546, "start": 2946.12, "end": 2952.2200000000003, "text": " In complex matrices, the trace is cyclic, meaning the trace of matrix A times matrix B equals", "tokens": [50398, 682, 3997, 32284, 11, 264, 13508, 307, 38154, 1050, 11, 3620, 264, 13508, 295, 8141, 316, 1413, 8141, 363, 6915, 50703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.136132487544307, "compression_ratio": 1.6491228070175439, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490748011242172e-12}, {"id": 1044, "seek": 294546, "start": 2952.2200000000003, "end": 2956.38, "text": " the trace of B times A. It's a wonderful, reliable property.", "tokens": [50703, 264, 13508, 295, 363, 1413, 316, 13, 467, 311, 257, 3715, 11, 12924, 4707, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.136132487544307, "compression_ratio": 1.6491228070175439, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490748011242172e-12}, {"id": 1045, "seek": 294546, "start": 2956.48, "end": 2957.64, "text": " I'm sensing a but here.", "tokens": [50916, 286, 478, 30654, 257, 457, 510, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.136132487544307, "compression_ratio": 1.6491228070175439, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490748011242172e-12}, {"id": 1046, "seek": 294546, "start": 2957.88, "end": 2959.7400000000002, "text": " In quaternions, that is false.", "tokens": [50986, 682, 421, 771, 77, 626, 11, 300, 307, 7908, 13, 51079], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.136132487544307, "compression_ratio": 1.6491228070175439, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490748011242172e-12}, {"id": 1047, "seek": 294546, "start": 2960.32, "end": 2962.14, "text": " Matrix trace is not cyclic.", "tokens": [51108, 36274, 13508, 307, 406, 38154, 1050, 13, 51199], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.136132487544307, "compression_ratio": 1.6491228070175439, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490748011242172e-12}, {"id": 1048, "seek": 294546, "start": 2962.6, "end": 2967.48, "text": " If you blindly apply standard complex proofs to quaternions, your math will collapse.", "tokens": [51222, 759, 291, 47744, 3079, 3832, 3997, 8177, 82, 281, 421, 771, 77, 626, 11, 428, 5221, 486, 15584, 13, 51466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.136132487544307, "compression_ratio": 1.6491228070175439, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490748011242172e-12}, {"id": 1049, "seek": 294546, "start": 2967.82, "end": 2969.94, "text": " So how does the author navigate this minefield?", "tokens": [51483, 407, 577, 775, 264, 3793, 12350, 341, 3892, 7610, 30, 51589], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.136132487544307, "compression_ratio": 1.6491228070175439, "no_speech_prob": 1.4490748011242172e-12}, {"id": 1050, "seek": 296994, "start": 2969.94, "end": 2974.08, "text": " By carefully using only the real part of the quaternionic trace.", "tokens": [50365, 3146, 7500, 1228, 787, 264, 957, 644, 295, 264, 421, 771, 77, 313, 299, 13508, 13, 50572], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13453615239236208, "compression_ratio": 1.689795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 1051, "seek": 296994, "start": 2974.78, "end": 2977.92, "text": " It turns out the real part of the trace is cyclic.", "tokens": [50607, 467, 4523, 484, 264, 957, 644, 295, 264, 13508, 307, 38154, 1050, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13453615239236208, "compression_ratio": 1.689795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 1052, "seek": 296994, "start": 2978.04, "end": 2978.56, "text": " Oh, that's clever.", "tokens": [50770, 876, 11, 300, 311, 13494, 13, 50796], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13453615239236208, "compression_ratio": 1.689795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 1053, "seek": 296994, "start": 2979.26, "end": 2985.2400000000002, "text": " By carefully navigating these traps and utilizing the real trace, the author derives a rigorous", "tokens": [50831, 3146, 7500, 32054, 613, 24173, 293, 26775, 264, 957, 13508, 11, 264, 3793, 1163, 1539, 257, 29882, 51130], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13453615239236208, "compression_ratio": 1.689795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 1054, "seek": 296994, "start": 2985.2400000000002, "end": 2987.62, "text": " quaternionic MUB bound.", "tokens": [51130, 421, 771, 77, 313, 299, 17935, 33, 5472, 13, 51249], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13453615239236208, "compression_ratio": 1.689795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 1055, "seek": 296994, "start": 2988.56, "end": 2994.2200000000003, "text": " Quaternions can mathematically support up to two pale plus one mutually unbiased bases.", "tokens": [51296, 2326, 771, 77, 626, 393, 44003, 1406, 493, 281, 732, 19546, 1804, 472, 39144, 517, 5614, 1937, 17949, 13, 51579], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13453615239236208, "compression_ratio": 1.689795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 1056, "seek": 296994, "start": 2994.46, "end": 2995.6, "text": " Two can plus one.", "tokens": [51591, 4453, 393, 1804, 472, 13, 51648], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13453615239236208, "compression_ratio": 1.689795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 1057, "seek": 296994, "start": 2995.8, "end": 2998.3, "text": " That's almost double the capacity of complex numbers.", "tokens": [51658, 663, 311, 1920, 3834, 264, 6042, 295, 3997, 3547, 13, 51783], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13453615239236208, "compression_ratio": 1.689795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7832582199089897e-12}, {"id": 1058, "seek": 299830, "start": 2998.3, "end": 3000.92, "text": " Think about the physical implications of that.", "tokens": [50365, 6557, 466, 264, 4001, 16602, 295, 300, 13, 50496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1059, "seek": 299830, "start": 3001.0800000000004, "end": 3004.1600000000003, "text": " It's like finding a secret hidden floor in an apartment building.", "tokens": [50504, 467, 311, 411, 5006, 257, 4054, 7633, 4123, 294, 364, 9587, 2390, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1060, "seek": 299830, "start": 3004.46, "end": 3004.82, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50673, 7587, 13, 50691], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1061, "seek": 299830, "start": 3005.04, "end": 3009.28, "text": " You live in a complex number building and the landlord tells you there are D plus one apartments", "tokens": [50702, 509, 1621, 294, 257, 3997, 1230, 2390, 293, 264, 32654, 5112, 291, 456, 366, 413, 1804, 472, 29056, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1062, "seek": 299830, "start": 3009.28, "end": 3009.88, "text": " per floor.", "tokens": [50914, 680, 4123, 13, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1063, "seek": 299830, "start": 3010.1400000000003, "end": 3011.6600000000003, "text": " You look around, all the doors are full.", "tokens": [50957, 509, 574, 926, 11, 439, 264, 8077, 366, 1577, 13, 51033], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1064, "seek": 299830, "start": 3011.76, "end": 3013.54, "text": " You think the building's at maximum capacity.", "tokens": [51038, 509, 519, 264, 2390, 311, 412, 6674, 6042, 13, 51127], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1065, "seek": 299830, "start": 3013.78, "end": 3013.94, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51139, 1779, 13, 51147], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1066, "seek": 299830, "start": 3014.28, "end": 3019.78, "text": " But then a quaternionic architect comes along, opens a hidden panel in the hallway, and manages", "tokens": [51164, 583, 550, 257, 421, 771, 77, 313, 299, 6331, 1487, 2051, 11, 9870, 257, 7633, 4831, 294, 264, 23903, 11, 293, 22489, 51439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1067, "seek": 299830, "start": 3019.78, "end": 3023.8, "text": " to pack in almost double the apartments on the exact same footprint.", "tokens": [51439, 281, 2844, 294, 1920, 3834, 264, 29056, 322, 264, 1900, 912, 24222, 13, 51640], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1068, "seek": 299830, "start": 3024.2000000000003, "end": 3026.1000000000004, "text": " It's a stunning mathematical construction.", "tokens": [51660, 467, 311, 257, 18550, 18894, 6435, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13293114873289152, "compression_ratio": 1.6964856230031948, "no_speech_prob": 1.6684897821001021e-12}, {"id": 1069, "seek": 302610, "start": 3026.1, "end": 3027.64, "text": " It proves the space is there.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 25019, 264, 1901, 307, 456, 13, 50442], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12604774825874415, "compression_ratio": 1.662280701754386, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417414082190885e-12}, {"id": 1070, "seek": 302610, "start": 3028.14, "end": 3031.56, "text": " But the text offers a crucial grounding warning here.", "tokens": [50467, 583, 264, 2487, 7736, 257, 11462, 46727, 9164, 510, 13, 50638], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12604774825874415, "compression_ratio": 1.662280701754386, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417414082190885e-12}, {"id": 1071, "seek": 302610, "start": 3032.12, "end": 3036.58, "text": " Just because there's mathematical space for two can plus one bases doesn't mean they", "tokens": [50666, 1449, 570, 456, 311, 18894, 1901, 337, 732, 393, 1804, 472, 17949, 1177, 380, 914, 436, 50889], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12604774825874415, "compression_ratio": 1.662280701754386, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417414082190885e-12}, {"id": 1072, "seek": 302610, "start": 3036.58, "end": 3038.18, "text": " actually exist physically.", "tokens": [50889, 767, 2514, 9762, 13, 50969], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12604774825874415, "compression_ratio": 1.662280701754386, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417414082190885e-12}, {"id": 1073, "seek": 302610, "start": 3038.66, "end": 3038.7599999999998, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50993, 1779, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12604774825874415, "compression_ratio": 1.662280701754386, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417414082190885e-12}, {"id": 1074, "seek": 302610, "start": 3039.3199999999997, "end": 3043.2599999999998, "text": " Just because the architect drew the blueprints for the secret apartments doesn't mean anyone", "tokens": [51026, 1449, 570, 264, 6331, 12804, 264, 888, 23547, 47523, 337, 264, 4054, 29056, 1177, 380, 914, 2878, 51223], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12604774825874415, "compression_ratio": 1.662280701754386, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417414082190885e-12}, {"id": 1075, "seek": 302610, "start": 3043.2599999999998, "end": 3046.8399999999997, "text": " can actually build them out of real bricks and mortar without the walls collapsing.", "tokens": [51223, 393, 767, 1322, 552, 484, 295, 957, 25497, 293, 33956, 1553, 264, 7920, 45339, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12604774825874415, "compression_ratio": 1.662280701754386, "no_speech_prob": 1.7417414082190885e-12}, {"id": 1076, "seek": 304684, "start": 3046.84, "end": 3052.78, "text": " The author leaves the actual physical existence of these quaternionic structures as a tantalizing", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 5510, 264, 3539, 4001, 9123, 295, 613, 421, 771, 77, 313, 299, 9227, 382, 257, 12095, 304, 3319, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096296999827925, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599758877859475e-12}, {"id": 1077, "seek": 304684, "start": 3052.78, "end": 3053.58, "text": " open question.", "tokens": [50662, 1269, 1168, 13, 50702], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096296999827925, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599758877859475e-12}, {"id": 1078, "seek": 304684, "start": 3054.06, "end": 3059.08, "text": " It shows that the mathematical room exists in the universe's geometry, but physics has", "tokens": [50726, 467, 3110, 300, 264, 18894, 1808, 8198, 294, 264, 6445, 311, 18426, 11, 457, 10649, 575, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096296999827925, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599758877859475e-12}, {"id": 1079, "seek": 304684, "start": 3059.08, "end": 3060.96, "text": " not yet found a reason to move in.", "tokens": [50977, 406, 1939, 1352, 257, 1778, 281, 1286, 294, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096296999827925, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599758877859475e-12}, {"id": 1080, "seek": 304684, "start": 3061.3, "end": 3065.34, "text": " This has been an absolutely wild, brain-bending journey.", "tokens": [51088, 639, 575, 668, 364, 3122, 4868, 11, 3567, 12, 65, 2029, 4671, 13, 51290], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096296999827925, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599758877859475e-12}, {"id": 1081, "seek": 304684, "start": 3065.5, "end": 3067.28, "text": " It really covers a lot of ground.", "tokens": [51298, 467, 534, 10538, 257, 688, 295, 2727, 13, 51387], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1096296999827925, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0599758877859475e-12}, {"id": 1082, "seek": 306728, "start": 3067.28, "end": 3070.92, "text": " We started with the simplest, most mundane thing imaginable.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 1409, 365, 264, 22811, 11, 881, 43497, 551, 23427, 712, 13, 50547], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14943160080328222, "compression_ratio": 1.5846774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722205659428722e-12}, {"id": 1083, "seek": 306728, "start": 3071.2000000000003, "end": 3073.2200000000003, "text": " Basic coin flips and probability shapes.", "tokens": [50561, 31598, 11464, 40249, 293, 8482, 10854, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14943160080328222, "compression_ratio": 1.5846774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722205659428722e-12}, {"id": 1084, "seek": 306728, "start": 3073.82, "end": 3078.1200000000003, "text": " We learned that simply requiring a system to preserve information means you fundamentally", "tokens": [50692, 492, 3264, 300, 2935, 24165, 257, 1185, 281, 15665, 1589, 1355, 291, 17879, 50907], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14943160080328222, "compression_ratio": 1.5846774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722205659428722e-12}, {"id": 1085, "seek": 306728, "start": 3078.1200000000003, "end": 3079.46, "text": " cannot decrease entropy.", "tokens": [50907, 2644, 11514, 30867, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14943160080328222, "compression_ratio": 1.5846774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722205659428722e-12}, {"id": 1086, "seek": 306728, "start": 3080.26, "end": 3082.5, "text": " The arrow of time emerges from geometry.", "tokens": [51014, 440, 11610, 295, 565, 38965, 490, 18426, 13, 51126], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14943160080328222, "compression_ratio": 1.5846774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722205659428722e-12}, {"id": 1087, "seek": 306728, "start": 3082.84, "end": 3087.5600000000004, "text": " We saw how stitching those probabilities together blindly loses the crucial interference data,", "tokens": [51143, 492, 1866, 577, 30714, 729, 33783, 1214, 47744, 18293, 264, 11462, 24497, 1412, 11, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14943160080328222, "compression_ratio": 1.5846774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722205659428722e-12}, {"id": 1088, "seek": 306728, "start": 3088.0600000000004, "end": 3090.26, "text": " demanding a coherent lift to amplitudes.", "tokens": [51404, 19960, 257, 36239, 5533, 281, 9731, 16451, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14943160080328222, "compression_ratio": 1.5846774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 1.4722205659428722e-12}, {"id": 1089, "seek": 309026, "start": 3090.26, "end": 3095.94, "text": " We discovered that trying to glue those coherent amplitudes into a closed triangle loop mathematically", "tokens": [50365, 492, 6941, 300, 1382, 281, 8998, 729, 36239, 9731, 16451, 666, 257, 5395, 13369, 6367, 44003, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10415735698881604, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 1.843243873506095e-12}, {"id": 1090, "seek": 309026, "start": 3095.94, "end": 3101.44, "text": " breaks the real numbers, forcing an Escher-like paradox where an angle doesn't equal itself.", "tokens": [50649, 9857, 264, 957, 3547, 11, 19030, 364, 2313, 6759, 12, 4092, 26221, 689, 364, 5802, 1177, 380, 2681, 2564, 13, 50924], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10415735698881604, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 1.843243873506095e-12}, {"id": 1091, "seek": 309026, "start": 3101.7400000000002, "end": 3107.5200000000004, "text": " And then we unpacked the dimension counting argument and uncovered the invisible J tensor J parameter", "tokens": [50939, 400, 550, 321, 26699, 292, 264, 10139, 13251, 6770, 293, 37729, 264, 14603, 508, 40863, 508, 13075, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10415735698881604, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 1.843243873506095e-12}, {"id": 1092, "seek": 309026, "start": 3107.5200000000004, "end": 3110.32, "text": " that hides entirely between local measurements.", "tokens": [51228, 300, 35953, 7696, 1296, 2654, 15383, 13, 51368], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10415735698881604, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 1.843243873506095e-12}, {"id": 1093, "seek": 309026, "start": 3110.48, "end": 3116.2200000000003, "text": " Which revealed that the very concept of quantum entanglement spooky action at a distance changes", "tokens": [51376, 3013, 9599, 300, 264, 588, 3410, 295, 13018, 948, 656, 3054, 30510, 3069, 412, 257, 4560, 2962, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10415735698881604, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 1.843243873506095e-12}, {"id": 1094, "seek": 309026, "start": 3116.2200000000003, "end": 3120.0800000000004, "text": " entirely depending on whether you view the universe through real or complex numbers.", "tokens": [51663, 7696, 5413, 322, 1968, 291, 1910, 264, 6445, 807, 957, 420, 3997, 3547, 13, 51856], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10415735698881604, "compression_ratio": 1.6677215189873418, "no_speech_prob": 1.843243873506095e-12}, {"id": 1095, "seek": 312008, "start": 3120.08, "end": 3120.44, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50383], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13424992143062123, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.6456625518839205e-12}, {"id": 1096, "seek": 312008, "start": 3120.7799999999997, "end": 3124.92, "text": " We counted the four exact pillars required to build the standard quantum universe.", "tokens": [50400, 492, 20150, 264, 1451, 1900, 26729, 4739, 281, 1322, 264, 3832, 13018, 6445, 13, 50607], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13424992143062123, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.6456625518839205e-12}, {"id": 1097, "seek": 312008, "start": 3125.56, "end": 3131.66, "text": " Local tomography, pure states as completable frames, real number labels for our dials,", "tokens": [50639, 22755, 2916, 5820, 11, 6075, 4368, 382, 1557, 712, 12083, 11, 957, 1230, 16949, 337, 527, 5502, 82, 11, 50944], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13424992143062123, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.6456625518839205e-12}, {"id": 1098, "seek": 312008, "start": 3131.7799999999997, "end": 3134.34, "text": " and smooth, continuous time evolution.", "tokens": [50950, 293, 5508, 11, 10957, 565, 9303, 13, 51078], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13424992143062123, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.6456625518839205e-12}, {"id": 1099, "seek": 312008, "start": 3134.54, "end": 3138.84, "text": " And finally we saw that even the complex numbers themselves, the imaginary eye that defines modern", "tokens": [51088, 400, 2721, 321, 1866, 300, 754, 264, 3997, 3547, 2969, 11, 264, 26164, 3313, 300, 23122, 4363, 51303], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13424992143062123, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.6456625518839205e-12}, {"id": 1100, "seek": 312008, "start": 3138.84, "end": 3141.18, "text": " physics, might just be an amplitwist.", "tokens": [51303, 10649, 11, 1062, 445, 312, 364, 9731, 270, 86, 468, 13, 51420], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13424992143062123, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.6456625518839205e-12}, {"id": 1101, "seek": 312008, "start": 3141.54, "end": 3146.84, "text": " A highly efficient grammatical shorthand for describing the geometry of twisting amplitudes", "tokens": [51438, 316, 5405, 7148, 17570, 267, 804, 402, 2652, 474, 337, 16141, 264, 18426, 295, 34491, 9731, 16451, 51703], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13424992143062123, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.6456625518839205e-12}, {"id": 1102, "seek": 312008, "start": 3146.84, "end": 3149.62, "text": " rather than an absolute mandate from the cosmos.", "tokens": [51703, 2831, 813, 364, 8236, 23885, 490, 264, 41794, 13, 51842], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13424992143062123, "compression_ratio": 1.648829431438127, "no_speech_prob": 2.6456625518839205e-12}, {"id": 1103, "seek": 314962, "start": 3149.62, "end": 3150.7799999999997, "text": " It's a lot to take in.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 257, 688, 281, 747, 294, 13, 50423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1380134768190637, "compression_ratio"